K.A={}
K.A["1"]="Cloth is the dress of the spellcasters, who trade protection for the freedom to work the art, and of everyone else when they are not fighting."
K.A["2"]="Leather armour is the dress of rogues, druids and the lighter hunters, quiet and supple."
K.A["3"]="Mail is the armour of the hunters and shaman and of the younger warriors and paladins, rings riveted over leather."
K.A["4"]="Plate is the armour of the warriors and paladins who have earned it, the heaviest protection the smiths can forge."
K.A["6"]="The shield is the warrior's and paladin's second weapon, and the shaman's."
K.A["7"]="A libram is the paladin's book of devotions, carried into battle as a relic."
K.A["8"]="An idol is the druid's carved totem of the wild gods."
K.A["9"]="A totem is the shaman's relic, carved with the signs of the elements."
K.B={}
K.B["basilisks"]="Basilisks are stone-skinned lizards of the deserts and badlands whose hides and eyes are used in alchemy."
K.B["bats"]="Bats roost in the caverns and ruins of Tirisfal, Silverpine and the Hinterlands, and the Forsaken have bred some for riding."
K.B["bears"]="Bears range the temperate forests and the hills of Lordaeron and Kalimdor, and their meat and warm pelts are staples of the frontier."
K.B["beetles"]="The great beetles and wasps of the deserts."
K.B["boars"]="Boars root through every lowland from Elwynn to Durotar and the Barrens, and their ribs, snouts and tusks are the first trophies most young hunters bring home."
K.B["carrion birds"]="Buzzards, vultures and condors wheel over the dry country of Westfall, the Barrens and Tanaris, picking the bones of travellers and whatever those travellers carried."
K.B["chimaera"]="Chimaera are two-headed winged beasts of Winterspring and Feralas, bred long ago by the night elves for war."
K.B["crabs"]="Crabs scuttle along every beach and marsh, and their shells and meat are coastal staples."
K.B["crocolisks"]="Crocolisks lurk in the rivers and marshes of the Wetlands, Dustwallow and Stranglethorn, and swallow whatever falls in the water."
K.B["gorillas"]="The apes of Stranglethorn and Un'Goro are strong, clever and territorial."
K.B["great cats"]="The great cats, from Elwynn's mountain lions to Stranglethorn's panthers and the sabres of Teldrassil and Winterspring, are the most prized of hunters' quarry for their hides."
K.B["hippogryphs"]="Hippogryphs are the half-stag, half-raptor mounts of the night elves, found wild in Feralas and Azshara."
K.B["hounds"]="Core hounds are the two-headed lava-dogs of the Molten Core, Ragnaros's kennel."
K.B["hyenas"]="Hyenas scavenge the Barrens, Thousand Needles and the Badlands in cackling packs."
K.B["kodo beasts"]="Kodo are the great grey beasts of burden of the tauren and the Horde, whose wild herds roam Mulgore and the Barrens and whose hides are the stuff of tents and armour."
K.B["owls"]="Owls hunt the night woods of Teldrassil and Duskwood, and their feathers are a reagent of the druids and the Darnassian craft."
K.B["plainstriders"]="Plainstriders are the long-legged flightless birds of the Barrens and Mulgore, hunted for meat and feathers."
K.B["primordial beasts"]="Un'Goro's devilsaurs, stegodons, diemetradons and pterrordaxes are survivors of an age before the Titans' ordering of the world."
K.B["rams"]="Rams of the dwarven hills, which the dwarves have ridden for centuries."
K.B["raptors"]="Raptors are swift pack-hunting lizards of the Barrens, the Wetlands and Stranglethorn, and their hides, teeth and eggs are much sought."
K.B["scorpids"]="Scorpids are the great scorpions of Durotar, Tanaris and the Blasted Lands, whose stingers and venom the alchemists want."
K.B["sea creatures"]="The threshers, sharks and makrura of the coasts and the deep."
K.B["spiders"]="Giant spiders infest the dark woods and caves, from Duskwood's webwoods to the lava spiders of Searing Gorge, and their silk and venom sacs are traded by tailors and alchemists."
K.B["stags"]="Stags and deer browse the gentler forests of Elwynn, Teldrassil and Ashenvale."
K.B["turtles"]="Giant turtles haul out along the coasts and the swamps, and their meat and scales have uses in the kitchen and the forge."
K.B["wind serpents"]="Wind serpents are winged snakes of the Barrens, Thousand Needles and the Wailing Caverns, whose scales and venom are traded by trolls and tauren."
K.B["wolves"]="Wolves hunt in packs across every forest and plain from Dun Morogh to Durotar; the orcs ride them, the Wildhammer hunt them, and their pelts and flanks are everywhere at market."
K.B["worms and grubs"]="The grubs, larvae and leeches of the caves and swamps."
K.B["wyverns"]="Wyverns are the winged lion-scorpions of Kalimdor's highlands, which the Horde tamed for riding."
K.B["zhevra"]="Zhevra are the striped horse-like grazers of the Barrens."
K.C={}
K.C["0"]="Its red bandana motif marks it as Defias work, the brand of the Brotherhood that rules Westfall."
K.C["1"]="It is in the style of the Scarlet Crusade, whose zealots dress in crimson and gold and whose smiths work in the Monastery."
K.C["10"]="It is Forsaken work, from the Undercity, grim and practical."
K.C["11"]="It is in the style of the human kingdoms, the plain good steel and cloth of Stormwind and old Lordaeron."
K.C["12"]="It bears the devices of the Argent Dawn, who hold Light's Hope Chapel against the Scourge."
K.C["13"]="It is of thorium, the dense black metal whose working the Thorium Brotherhood guards."
K.C["14"]="It is of mithril, the light silvery metal the dwarves prize above steel."
K.C["15"]="It is of truesilver, the rare luminous metal that takes enchantment like no other."
K.C["16"]="It is of arcanite, the alchemists' transmuted metal, which only the master smiths can work."
K.C["17"]="It is woven of runecloth, the finest ordinary cloth of the age."
K.C["18"]="It is woven of mooncloth, felcloth purified under Elune's light."
K.C["19"]="It is steeped in fel, the taint of the Burning Legion."
K.C["2"]="It is gnomish work, from the tinkers of Gnomeregan and Tinker Town, which is to say ingenious and not entirely safe."
K.C["20"]="It comes from the Darkmoon Faire, Silas Darkmoon's travelling carnival, and is as strange as everything else there."
K.C["21"]="It is of the qiraji, the insect-lords of Ahn'Qiraj, chitinous and alien."
K.C["22"]="It carries the mark of the black dragonflight."
K.C["23"]="It is of the fire of the Molten Core, the Firelord's domain."
K.C["24"]="It carries the taint of the Scourge."
K.C["25"]="It is of the Cenarion Circle, the druids who hold Silithus against the qiraji."
K.C["27"]="It is of the Timbermaw furbolg, the last sane tribe, who hold the pass to Winterspring."
K.C["28"]="It is Wildhammer work, from the gryphon-riding dwarves of Aerie Peak."
K.C["29"]="It is a pirate's gear, from the Bloodsail and Southsea fleets."
K.C["3"]="It is goblin manufacture, from the engineers of the Steamwheedle Cartel, built to a price and apt to explode."
K.C["30"]="It is Syndicate gear, from the fallen nobles of Alterac."
K.C["31"]="It is Venture Company issue, the goblin company's cheap kit for its hired hands."
K.C["32"]="It is Highborne work, from the lost empire of Queen Azshara, ten thousand years old."
K.C["33"]="It is Titan-forged, from the vaults the makers of the world left behind."
K.C["34"]="It is Blackrock work, from the orcs of the Spire."
K.C["35"]="It is ogre work, oversized and crude."
K.C["36"]="It is centaur work, from the clans of Desolace and the Barrens."
K.C["37"]="It is quilboar work, of thorn, hide and bone."
K.C["38"]="It is murloc make, which is to say damp."
K.C["4"]="It is dwarven work from the forges of Ironforge, sturdy, plain and made to last a lifetime."
K.C["40"]="It is naga work, of coral, shell and salt-hardened scale."
K.C["41"]="It is Atal'ai work, from the troll priesthood of the Sunken Temple."
K.C["42"]="It bears the devices of the Twilight's Hammer, the cult of the Old Gods."
K.C["43"]="It is of the Wailing Caverns' deviate creatures, touched by the nightmare."
K.C["44"]="It is of the druidic orders."
K.C["45"]="It is of the shamanic traditions of the Horde."
K.C["46"]="It is of the orders of paladins, the Silver Hand's heirs."
K.C["47"]="It is in the style of the mages of Dalaran and the Kirin Tor."
K.C["48"]="It is of the warlock covens."
K.C["49"]="It is in the style of the rogues' guilds, SI:7 and the Deathstalkers."
K.C["5"]="It is Dark Iron work, from the Shadowforge under Blackrock Mountain, whose smiths rival the Firelord's own."
K.C["50"]="It is in the style of the great hunters."
K.C["51"]="It is of the priesthoods, the Cathedral of Light and the Forsaken cult of the Forgotten Shadow alike."
K.C["52"]="It is in the style of the warrior orders of both factions."
K.C["6"]="It is night elf work, in the graceful style of Darnassus and the Sentinels, often inlaid with moonstone or carved with the crescent of Elune."
K.C["7"]="It is orcish work, from the forges of Orgrimmar, heavy and spiked in the manner of the Horde."
K.C["8"]="It is troll work, in the style of the great tribes, worked with bone, feather and the fetishes of the loa."
K.C["9"]="It is tauren work, of hide, wood and bone in the manner of Thunder Bluff."
K.D={}
K.D["Ahn'Qiraj"]="The Temple of Ahn'Qiraj is the inner city of the qiraji, where the Twin Emperors rule in the name of the Old God C'Thun, who stirs beneath the temple floor."
K.D["Blackfathom Deeps"]="Blackfathom Deeps is a drowned temple of Elune on the Darkshore coast, taken by the naga and the Twilight's Hammer cult, who worship the Old God's servant Aku'mai in its depths."
K.D["Blackrock Depths"]="Blackrock Depths is the Dark Iron city under Blackrock Mountain: the Shadowforge, the Ring of Law, the Grim Guzzler tavern and the throne of Emperor Dagran Thaurissan, who holds the dwarven princess Moira as his bride."
K.D["Blackrock Spire"]="Blackrock Spire is the upper fortress of Blackrock Mountain, where the Blackrock orcs under Warchief Rend Blackhand serve the black dragon Nefarian, alongside Smolderthorn trolls, Spirestone ogres and the dragonspawn of the black flight."
K.D["Blackwing Lair"]="Blackwing Lair is Nefarian's seat at the peak of Blackrock Spire, where the son of Deathwing breeds the chromatic dragonflight from the eggs of every other flight."
K.D["Gnomeregan"]="Gnomeregan was the gnomes' great city under Dun Morogh until the trogg invasion drove Mekgineer Thermaplugg to flood it with radiation. Leper gnomes, troggs and runaway machines now hold its halls."
K.D["Maraudon"]="Maraudon is the great cavern-temple of the centaur in Desolace, tomb of their ancestress Theradras, the earth elemental who bore the first centaur to the demigod Zaetar. Satyrs, corrupted elementals and the centaur's own Maraudine guard it."
K.D["Molten Core"]="The Molten Core is the heart of Blackrock Mountain, the lava sea where Ragnaros the Firelord has been imprisoned since the Dark Irons summoned him. Flamewaker lieutenants, core hounds and fire giants guard him, and Majordomo Executus keeps his court."
K.D["Naxxramas"]="Naxxramas is the floating necropolis of the lich Kel'Thuzad, anchored over the Eastern Plaguelands. Its wings hold the Scourge's plague works, spider breeders, the Four Horsemen and the frost wyrm Sapphiron."
K.D["Onyxia's Lair"]="Onyxia's Lair is the brood-cave of the black dragon Onyxia, hidden beneath Dustwallow Marsh. In human guise she sat on Stormwind's council as Lady Katrana Prestor until she was unmasked."
K.D["Ragefire Chasm"]="Ragefire Chasm is the volcanic cavern beneath Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, where the Burning Blade cult and the Searing Blade troggs plot against Thrall under the very feet of the Horde."
K.D["Razorfen Downs"]="Razorfen Downs is the quilboar's sacred burial warren, where the Scourge has installed the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer and raised the dead quilboar as his army."
K.D["Razorfen Kraul"]="Razorfen Kraul is the quilboar's thorn-walled warren at the southern edge of the Barrens, grown from the bones of the demigod Agamaggan. The Death's Head tribe rules it with boars, bats and dark shamanism."
K.D["Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj"]="The Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj are the outer city of the qiraji in Silithus, opened when the Scarab Wall fell. Silithid and qiraji warriors swarm its courts under the prophet Ossirian the Unscarred."
K.D["Scarlet Monastery"]="The Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal is the fortress-abbey of the Scarlet Crusade, zealots who hunt the undead and anyone else they judge tainted. Its graveyard, library, armory and cathedral are each garrisoned by the Crusade's elite."
K.D["Scholomance"]="Scholomance is the school of necromancy in the crypts beneath Caer Darrow, where the Cult of the Damned trains its necromancers under Darkmaster Gandling and the lich Ras Frostwhisper."
K.D["Shadowfang Keep"]="Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine was the baron's castle until the mage Arugal fled there with the worgen he had summoned. Its halls hold the cursed Sons of Arugal, the ghosts of the baron's household and the Dalaran apprentice who followed Arugal into madness."
K.D["Stratholme"]="Stratholme is the burned city where Arthas culled his own people. Its western half is held by the Scarlet Crusade under Grand Crusader Dathrohan, its eastern half by the Scourge under Baron Rivendare, and plague and fire never leave its streets."
K.D["Sunken Temple"]="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar lies drowned beneath the Swamp of Sorrows, sunk by the green dragonflight to stop the Atal'ai trolls summoning the blood god Hakkar. The Atal'ai still labour there among green drakes gone mad."
K.D["The Deadmines"]="The Deadmines beneath Moonbrook in Westfall are the Defias Brotherhood's stronghold, where Edwin VanCleef's masons and goblin shipwrights are building a warship in the flooded heart of the mine."
K.D["The Stockade"]="The Stockade is Stormwind's prison beneath the Canals, where Defias convicts under Bazil Thredd have overpowered the guards and hold the cells."
K.D["Uldaman"]="Uldaman is a Titan vault in the Badlands, excavated by the Explorers' League and the Dark Iron dwarves alike. Troggs and stone constructs guard its halls, and the Titan's keeper Archaedas sleeps at its heart with the Discs of Norgannon."
K.D["Wailing Caverns"]="The Wailing Caverns are a cave system beneath the Barrens where the druid Naralex tried to dream a new forest into being and fell into a nightmare. His Druids of the Fang went mad, and the caverns teem with deviate creatures twisted by the dream."
K.D["Zul'Farrak"]="Zul'Farrak is the sandstone city of the Sandfury trolls in northern Tanaris, where the hydra Gahz'rilla sleeps in the sacred pool and the witch doctors raise troll dead."
K.D["Zul'Gurub"]="Zul'Gurub is the ancient capital of the Gurubashi trolls in Stranglethorn, where the Hakkari priesthood has succeeded in summoning the blood god Hakkar the Soulflayer and the high priests of the troll animal gods have fallen to him."
K.I={}
K.I["Ankh"]="The ankh is the shaman's reagent for reincarnation, a symbol of the Earth Mother's cycle."
K.I["Aquamarine"]="Aquamarine, a sea-blue stone of the iron and mithril deposits."
K.I["Arcane Crystal"]="Arcane crystal, a crystallised shard of raw magic found in rich thorium veins and transmuted by alchemists into arcanite."
K.I["Arcane Dust"]="Arcane dust, the reagent of the mages' teleportation."
K.I["Arcane Powder"]="Arcane powder, the mages' reagent for their spells of intellect."
K.I["Arcanite Bar"]="Arcanite is the alchemists' transmutation of thorium and arcane crystal, the metal of the legendary smiths."
K.I["Arthas' Tears"]="Arthas' Tears grow only in the Plaguelands and Felwood, white flowers sprung where the prince's armies passed, and are used in potions against the undead."
K.I["Ashwood Seed"]="The ashwood seed, the druid's reagent for rebirth."
K.I["Azerothian Diamond"]="Azerothian diamond, the hardest and brightest stone of the thorium veins."
K.I["Bear Meat"]="Bear meat, rich and dark, a staple of the northern kingdoms."
K.I["Big Bear Meat"]="The meat of the great bears of the highlands."
K.I["Black Diamond"]="Black diamond, found only in the dark iron deposits of Blackrock Mountain."
K.I["Black Dye"]="Black dye, for the tailor's colours."
K.I["Black Lotus"]="Black lotus is the rarest herb of Azeroth, found only in the harshest country of Winterspring, Silithus, the Burning Steppes and the Eastern Plaguelands, and is the key to the great flasks."
K.I["Black Pearl"]="Black pearls are found in the giant clams of the deep coasts and the shellfish eaten by naga and murlocs."
K.I["Black Vitriol"]="Black vitriol is a corrosive mineral found in the deep veins and used by alchemists."
K.I["Blank Parchment"]="Blank parchment, for the scribe's and the engineer's drawings."
K.I["Bleach"]="Bleach, for the tailor's whitest cloth."
K.I["Blinding Powder"]="Blinding powder, ground from fadeleaf for the rogue's blind."
K.I["Blindweed"]="Blindweed grows in the swamps and pools of the Swamp of Sorrows and Un'Goro, and is used in potions of the mind."
K.I["Blood of the Mountain"]="Blood of the Mountain is the rare red stone found in dark iron deposits, sacred to the Dark Iron dwarves."
K.I["Bloodvine"]="Bloodvine grows only in Zul'Gurub, tangled on the ruins of the Gurubashi, and the Zandalar tribe's tailors prize it."
K.I["Blue Dye"]="Blue dye, for the tailor's and leatherworker's colours."
K.I["Blue Pearl"]="Blue pearls from the clams of the cold coasts."
K.I["Blue Sapphire"]="Blue sapphire, a stone of the thorium veins prized by enchanters."
K.I["Boar Intestines"]="Boar intestines, which cooks in Durotar and Elwynn turn into sausage."
K.I["Boar Ribs"]="The ribs of a boar, for the cook's pot."
K.I["Bolt of Linen Cloth"]="A bolt is cloth made ready for the tailor's shears, several scraps woven and pressed together."
K.I["Bolt of Mageweave"]="A bolt is cloth made ready for the tailor's shears, several scraps woven and pressed together."
K.I["Bolt of Runecloth"]="A bolt is cloth made ready for the tailor's shears, several scraps woven and pressed together."
K.I["Bolt of Silk Cloth"]="A bolt is cloth made ready for the tailor's shears, several scraps woven and pressed together."
K.I["Bolt of Woolen Cloth"]="A bolt is cloth made ready for the tailor's shears, several scraps woven and pressed together."
K.I["Breath of Wind"]="The breath of an air elemental."
K.I["Briarthorn"]="Briarthorn is a thorny shrub of the woods and plains whose stems go into healing potions and the hunters' elixirs."
K.I["Bronze Bar"]="Bronze, the alloy of copper and tin, is the metal of the common soldier's arms."
K.I["Bronze Framework"]="A bronze framework, for the engineer's devices."
K.I["Bronze Tube"]="A bronze tube, for the engineer's scopes and rifles."
K.I["Bruiseweed"]="Bruiseweed is a blue-flowered herb of the middle lands used in potions of healing and defence."
K.I["Buzzard Wing"]="The wing of a buzzard, for the Barrens' roast."
K.I["Chimaerok Tenderloin"]="The tenderloin of the chimaerok of the Isle of Dread, a delicacy of the great cooks."
K.I["Chimera Leather"]="The hide of the chimaera, which holds the tingle of its lightning."
K.I["Chunk of Boar Meat"]="Boar meat, the commonest meat of the lowlands."
K.I["Citrine"]="Citrine, a yellow stone of the iron and gold deposits."
K.I["Clam Meat"]="Clam meat from the clams of the coast."
K.I["Coal"]="Coal, dug from the mines of the dwarves and sold by every mining supplier, fires the forge."
K.I["Coarse Blasting Powder"]="Coarse blasting powder, for the engineer's bombs and dynamite."
K.I["Coarse Stone"]="Coarse stone from the tin veins, for grinding stones and blasting powder."
K.I["Coarse Thread"]="Coarse thread, spun from flax or hemp, binds the seams of the humblest garments and leatherwork."
K.I["Copper Bar"]="Copper smelted into bars, the apprentice smith's and engineer's working metal."
K.I["Copper Modulator"]="A copper modulator, the engineer's first device."
K.I["Copper Ore"]="Copper is the first ore every miner learns to work, found in veins near the surface in every starting land from Dun Morogh to Durotar."
K.I["Copper Tube"]="A copper tube, for the engineer's first scopes and guns."
K.I["Core Leather"]="Core leather is the hide of the core hounds of the Molten Core, which will not burn."
K.I["Core of Earth"]="The core of an earth elemental."
K.I["Coyote Meat"]="The meat of the coyotes of Westfall and the Barrens."
K.I["Crag Boar Rib"]="The ribs of a Dun Morogh crag boar, the dwarves' beer-hall favourite."
K.I["Crawler Claw"]="The claw of a shore crab."
K.I["Crawler Meat"]="The meat of the shore crabs."
K.I["Crisp Spider Meat"]="Spider meat, crisp when fried, a frontier dish."
K.I["Crocolisk Meat"]="Crocolisk meat, from the swamps and rivers."
K.I["Crystal Vial"]="A crystal vial, the alchemist's vessel for the great potions."
K.I["Dark Iron Bar"]="Dark iron, smeltable only in the Black Forge of Blackrock Depths with the Thorium Brotherhood's secret."
K.I["Dark Iron Ore"]="Dark iron is the Dark Iron dwarves' own ore, found only in the Searing Gorge, the Burning Steppes and Blackrock Mountain, and smelted only in the Black Forge itself."
K.I["Dark Rune"]="Dark runes are the Scholomance necromancers' carved stones, which trade life for mana."
K.I["Deeprock Salt"]="Deeprock salt, found in the deep veins, is the curing salt of the leatherworkers."
K.I["Delicate Feather"]="A soft small feather, used in a dozen quests and in the gnomes' lighter devices."
K.I["Demonic Figurine"]="The demonic figurine, the warlock's reagent for summoning a doomguard or infernal."
K.I["Demonic Rune"]="Demonic runes, carved by the Legion's cultists, which trade life for mana."
K.I["Dense Blasting Powder"]="Dense blasting powder, for the greatest of the goblin and gnomish explosives."
K.I["Dense Stone"]="Dense stone from thorium veins, the hardest of the smith's stones."
K.I["Deviate Fish"]="Deviate fish swim only in the pools of the Wailing Caverns and the Barrens' oases, mutated by the nightmare, and eating them does strange things to the eater."
K.I["Deviate Scale"]="The iridescent scales of the deviate creatures of the Wailing Caverns, which hold a trace of the nightmare that made them."
K.I["Devilsaur Leather"]="Devilsaur leather, from the tyrant lizards of Un'Goro Crater, is nearly as hard as plate and the most prized hide in Kalimdor."
K.I["Discolored Worg Heart"]="The heart of a worg of Redridge, discoloured and sought by alchemists."
K.I["Dream Dust"]="Dream dust, from disenchanted items of the highest grades."
K.I["Dreamfoil"]="Dreamfoil grows in the far reaches of Azshara, Un'Goro and the Plaguelands, and is used in the mana potions of the great alchemists."
K.I["Dust of Decay"]="The dust of a fallen undead, for alchemy."
K.I["Dust of Deterioration"]="The dust of the long dead."
K.I["Earthroot"]="Earthroot grows on hillsides and cliff edges, a thick root that alchemists brew for toughness."
K.I["Elemental Air"]="Elemental air is the captured breath of an air elemental."
K.I["Elemental Earth"]="Elemental earth is the solidified essence of an earth elemental, wanted by smiths."
K.I["Elemental Fire"]="Elemental fire is the bottled heart of a fire elemental, wanted by alchemists and engineers."
K.I["Elemental Flux"]="Elemental flux, for smelting the elemental metals."
K.I["Elemental Water"]="Elemental water is the living water of a water elemental."
K.I["Elementium Bar"]="Elementium in bars, forged with the secrets of the black dragonflight."
K.I["Elementium Ore"]="Elementium is a metal from the elemental plane, brought to Azeroth by the black dragonflight and worked only with the secrets of Blackwing Lair."
K.I["Empty Vial"]="An empty vial, the alchemist's first vessel."
K.I["Enchanted Leather"]="Leather infused with arcane essence by an enchanter, which takes enchantment readily."
K.I["Engineer's Ink"]="Engineer's ink, for drawing up schematics."
K.I["Essence of Agony"]="Essence of agony, the greater distillation."
K.I["Essence of Air"]="The essence of a greater air elemental."
K.I["Essence of Earth"]="The essence of a greater earth elemental, wanted by alchemists for the great transmutations and by smiths for the great armours."
K.I["Essence of Fire"]="The essence of a greater fire elemental, the alchemists' key to fire resistance."
K.I["Essence of Pain"]="Essence of pain, distilled from the suffering of the dead."
K.I["Essence of Undeath"]="The distilled essence of the greater undead, used in the alchemists' shadow and undead-slaying brews."
K.I["Essence of Water"]="The essence of a greater water elemental, for the alchemists' frost oils and the great potions."
K.I["Fadeleaf"]="Fadeleaf grows in the shade of the jungles and swamps, and rogues' blinding powder is made from it."
K.I["Felcloth"]="Felcloth is cloth steeped in demonic energy, cut from the robes of the Legion's servants and the satyrs of Felwood, and sought by warlock tailors for their darkest work."
K.I["Fiery Core"]="A fiery core from the elementals of the Molten Core, wanted by the smiths of fire-proof armour."
K.I["Fine Thread"]="Fine thread for the finer seam, sold by every tailoring and leatherworking supplier."
K.I["Firebloom"]="Firebloom grows in the hot, dry country of the Searing Gorge, the Burning Steppes, Tanaris and the Blasted Lands, and is the base of fire protection potions."
K.I["Firefin Snapper"]="The firefin snapper of the warm coasts, whose fins the alchemists render into fire oil."
K.I["Fish Scale"]="The scales of the common fish."
K.I["Fist-sized Spinneret"]="The spinneret of a giant spider, useful to tailors."
K.I["Flash Powder"]="Flash powder, the rogue's reagent for vanishing."
K.I["Flask of Big Mojo"]="A flask of big mojo, the stronger brew of the Gurubashi."
K.I["Flask of Mojo"]="A flask of mojo, the troll witch doctors' bottled spirit-stuff."
K.I["Flask of Oil"]="A flask of oil, for the engineer's mechanisms and the fisherman's lantern."
K.I["Flint and Tinder"]="Flint and tinder, for lighting a campfire anywhere in the world."
K.I["Frostsaber Leather"]="The white pelt of the frostsabers of Winterspring, sacred to the night elves."
K.I["Frozen Rune"]="Frozen runes, from the frost of Naxxramas."
K.I["Fused Wiring"]="Fused wiring, the engineer's spare part, salvaged from every broken machine."
K.I["Ghost Mushroom"]="Ghost mushrooms grow in the caves of the Hinterlands and Maraudon, glowing faintly, and are used in the ghost dye and in invisibility potions."
K.I["Giant Clam Meat"]="The meat of the giant clams of the deep coasts."
K.I["Giant Egg"]="The great eggs of the roc, the owlbeast and the hippogryph, wanted by the cooks of Feralas and the Hinterlands."
K.I["Globe of Water"]="A globe of elemental water."
K.I["Goblin Rocket Fuel"]="Goblin rocket fuel, brewed by alchemists from firebloom and sold to engineers who should know better."
K.I["Gold Bar"]="Gold in bars, for the enchanter's golden rod and the engineer's finer contacts."
K.I["Gold Ore"]="Gold runs in thin veins alongside iron and is wanted by smiths and engineers as much as by the goldsmith."
K.I["Golden Pearl"]="Golden pearls, the rarest of pearls, found in the clams of the far coasts."
K.I["Golden Sansam"]="Golden sansam grows in the highlands of Un'Goro, Felwood and the Plaguelands, and is used in the greatest healing potions."
K.I["Goldthorn"]="Goldthorn is a golden-flowered thorn of the highlands used in elixirs of agility and the superior healing potion."
K.I["Gooey Spider Leg"]="The leg of a giant spider, cooked despite everything."
K.I["Goretusk Liver"]="The liver of a Westfall goretusk, the foundation of Westfall stew."
K.I["Goretusk Snout"]="The snout of a Westfall goretusk."
K.I["Grave Moss"]="Grave moss grows only on graves and in crypts, and the alchemists of the Forsaken want it for their shadow draughts."
K.I["Gray Dye"]="Gray dye, for the tailor's colours."
K.I["Great Goretusk Snout"]="The snout of a great goretusk of Westfall."
K.I["Green Dye"]="Green dye, for the tailor's and leatherworker's colours."
K.I["Gromsblood"]="Gromsblood is a red-black herb that sprang up where orcs' blood fell in Felwood and the Blasted Lands, used in the elixirs of the giants and of demonslaying."
K.I["Guardian Stone"]="A guardian stone, the earth's protection bound in stone."
K.I["Gyrochronatom"]="A gyrochronatom, the gnomish device's sense of balance."
K.I["Handful of Copper Bolts"]="Copper bolts, the engineer's first fastenings."
K.I["Heart of Fire"]="The heart of a fire elemental, hot to the touch."
K.I["Heart of the Wild"]="The heart of a great beast, the druids' reagent."
K.I["Heavy Blasting Powder"]="Heavy blasting powder, for the heavier explosives."
K.I["Heavy Hide"]="A whole heavy hide, thick enough to need curing salt before it can be worked."
K.I["Heavy Kodo Meat"]="The heavy meat of the great kodo of the Barrens and Desolace."
K.I["Heavy Leather"]="Heavy leather, from the great beasts of the highlands and the jungles, makes armour that will turn a blade."
K.I["Heavy Silken Thread"]="Heavy silken thread, for the seams of armour that must take a blow."
K.I["Heavy Stock"]="A heavy wooden stock for the gunsmith's heavier rifles."
K.I["Heavy Stone"]="Heavy stone from iron deposits, for the smith's heavy grinding stones and the engineer's heavy blasting powder."
K.I["Holiday Spices"]="Holiday spices, for the winter feast."
K.I["Holy Candle"]="The holy candle, the priest's reagent for the lesser prayers."
K.I["Hops"]="Hops, for the brewers of Dun Morogh."
K.I["Hornbeam Seed"]="The hornbeam seed, the druid's reagent for rebirth."
K.I["Hot Spices"]="Hot spices, for the cook's heartier dishes."
K.I["Huge Emerald"]="Huge emerald, a green stone of the thorium veins wanted by the great tailors and smiths."
K.I["Huge Venom Sac"]="The venom sac of one of the great spiders of the Plaguelands or Silithus."
K.I["Icecap"]="Icecap grows only in the snows of Winterspring, and is used in frost protection potions."
K.I["Ichor of Undeath"]="The ichor of the undead, for the alchemists."
K.I["Illusion Dust"]="Illusion dust, from the disenchanted items of the great dungeons."
K.I["Imbued Vial"]="An imbued vial, for the alchemist's greatest flasks."
K.I["Incendicite Ore"]="Incendicite is a fiery mineral found only in the Wetlands' Thelgen Rock."
K.I["Indurium Ore"]="Indurium is a hard mineral of Uldaman prized by the gnomes of the Mirage Raceway."
K.I["Infernal Stone"]="The infernal stone, the warlock's reagent for the infernal."
K.I["Inlaid Mithril Cylinder"]="An inlaid mithril cylinder, for the engineer's rifles."
K.I["Iridescent Pearl"]="Iridescent pearls from the clams of the middle coasts."
K.I["Iron Bar"]="Iron in bars, ready for the forge."
K.I["Iron Ore"]="Iron is the metal of the age, dug from the hills of Arathi, Stranglethorn, Desolace and the Badlands and forged into the steel of every army."
K.I["Iron Strut"]="An iron strut, for the engineer's heavier work."
K.I["Ironfeather"]="The iron-hard feathers of the great owlbeasts, used by engineers."
K.I["Ironweb Spider Silk"]="Ironweb silk comes from the vast spiders of the Plaguelands and the Burning Steppes, and is as tough as wire."
K.I["Ironwood Seed"]="The ironwood seed, the druid's reagent for rebirth."
K.I["Jade"]="Jade, a green stone of the iron deposits, cut for jewellery and for the engineer's gnomish devices."
K.I["Jet Black Feather"]="The black feathers of the carrion birds and ravens, used in shadow reagents."
K.I["Khadgar's Whisker"]="Khadgar's Whisker, named for the archmage, grows in the dark forests and swamps and is used in elixirs of intellect and shadow."
K.I["Kingsblood"]="Kingsblood is a red-flowered herb of the hills and plains used in elixirs of strength and the greater healing potion."
K.I["Kodo Meat"]="Kodo meat, the tauren's staple."
K.I["Large Fang"]="A large fang, from a wolf, cat or raptor."
K.I["Large Obsidian Shard"]="A large shard of obsidian, which the Cenarion Circle's smiths work into armour against the qiraji."
K.I["Large Opal"]="Large opal, an iridescent stone of the thorium veins."
K.I["Large Venom Sac"]="The venom sac of a large spider or serpent."
K.I["Larval Acid"]="The acid of silithid larvae."
K.I["Lava Core"]="A lava core from the Molten Core's elementals."
K.I["Leaded Vial"]="A leaded vial, the alchemist's vessel for the middle potions."
K.I["Lean Wolf Flank"]="The lean flank of a northern wolf."
K.I["Lesser Magic Essence"]="Lesser magic essence, drawn from disenchanted trinkets, the enchanter's first essence."
K.I["Lesser Moonstone"]="Lesser moonstone, a milky stone found with tin and silver, sacred to the night elves."
K.I["Liferoot"]="Liferoot grows at the water's edge and in the swamps, a vital root for potions of restoration."
K.I["Light Hide"]="A whole light hide, untrimmed, from the smaller game of the lowlands."
K.I["Light Leather"]="Light leather is the thin hide of young and small game, the stuff of apprentice leatherwork and of every hunter's first armour."
K.I["Lightning Eel"]="The lightning eel of the coasts of Azshara and Feralas."
K.I["Linen Cloth"]="Linen is the coarsest of the woven cloths, spun from flax grown in Elwynn, Tirisfal and the Barrens and worn by peasants and pressed into bandages by every field medic. Tailors make their first bolts of it, and every bandit, kobold and gnoll seems to carry a scrap."
K.I["Lion Meat"]="The meat of the mountain lions of Elwynn and Redridge."
K.I["Living Essence"]="Living essence is the vital spark of the great treants and ancients, used in the alchemists' nature potions."
K.I["Long Tail Feather"]="The long tail feathers of the plainstriders and jungle birds, used by tauren and troll fletchers."
K.I["Mageroyal"]="Mageroyal is a pink-flowered herb of the middle lowlands, used in potions of mana and the restorative draughts of mages."
K.I["Mageweave Cloth"]="Mageweave is cloth woven with a trace of arcane thread so that it holds enchantment, the preferred stuff of the Kirin Tor and every self-respecting cultist's robe."
K.I["Malachite"]="Malachite, a green copper stone found in copper veins and used by apprentice jewellers and leatherworkers."
K.I["Maple Seed"]="The maple seed, the druid's reagent for rebirth."
K.I["Massive Mojo"]="Massive mojo, the mojo of the Hakkari themselves."
K.I["Meaty Bat Wing"]="The wing of a giant bat, which the Forsaken cooks roast."
K.I["Medium Hide"]="A whole medium hide, from the deer, wolves and boars of the middle country."
K.I["Medium Leather"]="Medium leather, from the common game of the middle country, is the everyday leather of the trade."
K.I["Mild Spices"]="Mild spices, the cook's first seasoning."
K.I["Mithril Bar"]="Mithril in bars, light and strong, the dwarven armourer's favourite."
K.I["Mithril Casing"]="A mithril casing, for the engineer's finer devices."
K.I["Mithril Ore"]="Mithril is a light, silvery metal mined in the Badlands, Searing Gorge, Tanaris and the Hinterlands, which the dwarves prize above steel for armour."
K.I["Mithril Tube"]="A mithril tube, for the engineer's rifles and scopes."
K.I["Mooncloth"]="Mooncloth is felcloth purified in a moonwell under Elune's light, a tailoring secret of the night elves that only the devoted may make once in a few days."
K.I["Moss Agate"]="Moss agate, a green-flecked stone of the tin and silver veins."
K.I["Mountain Silversage"]="Mountain silversage grows in the high cold country of Winterspring and the Plaguelands, and is used in the flasks of the master alchemists."
K.I["Murloc Eye"]="A murloc's eye, wanted by cooks in Elwynn for a certain soup."
K.I["Murloc Fin"]="A murloc's fin, which cooks in Stormwind and Darkshore make into soup."
K.I["Mystery Meat"]="Meat of uncertain origin, cooked by goblins into stew of equally uncertain origin."
K.I["Naga Scale"]="The scale of a naga, salt-hardened and faintly magical."
K.I["Ogre Tannin"]="Ogre tannin, the Gordok ogres' secret for tanning the heaviest hides."
K.I["Oily Blackmouth"]="The oily blackmouth is a coastal fish whose oil the alchemists press for their blackmouth oil."
K.I["Okra"]="Okra, for the cooks of Stranglethorn."
K.I["Orange Dye"]="Orange dye, for the tailor's colours."
K.I["Peacebloom"]="Peacebloom is a small white flower that grows in every gentle meadow of Azeroth, the first herb an herbalist learns and the base of the minor healing potion."
K.I["Perfect Deviate Scale"]="A flawless deviate scale, rare even in the Wailing Caverns."
K.I["Pink Dye"]="Pink dye, for the tailor's colours."
K.I["Plaguebloom"]="Plaguebloom grows only where the plague has soaked the earth, in the Plaguelands and Felwood, and alchemists use it in the shadow potions."
K.I["Plated Armorfish"]="The plated armorfish of the deep waters."
K.I["Powerful Mojo"]="Powerful mojo, the greatest of the troll witch doctors' spirit-brews."
K.I["Primal Bat Leather"]="The wing-leather of the great bats of Zul'Gurub."
K.I["Primal Tiger Leather"]="The hide of the great tigers of Zul'Gurub's jungle."
K.I["Purple Dye"]="Purple dye, for the tailor's finer colours."
K.I["Purple Lotus"]="Purple lotus grows in the ruins of Azshara and Feralas and the jungles of Stranglethorn, and is used in the elixirs of the mind and in the wildvine potions."
K.I["Raptor Egg"]="A raptor's egg, large and leathery, used in the cooks' raptor stew."
K.I["Raptor Flesh"]="Raptor flesh, which the cooks of the Wetlands and the Barrens stew."
K.I["Raptor Hide"]="The tough, scaled hide of a raptor."
K.I["Red Dye"]="Red dye, for the tailor's and leatherworker's colours."
K.I["Red Wolf Meat"]="The meat of the red wolves of Feralas and the Hinterlands."
K.I["Righteous Orb"]="A righteous orb is the crystallised faith of the Scarlet Crusade's elite, which enchanters use for the Crusader enchantment."
K.I["Rough Blasting Powder"]="Rough blasting powder, the engineer's first explosive, ground from rough stone."
K.I["Rough Stone"]="Rough stone, chipped from copper veins, is ground by blacksmiths into their first sharpening and grinding stones and by engineers into blasting powder."
K.I["Rugged Hide"]="A whole rugged hide from the great beasts of the far country."
K.I["Rugged Leather"]="Rugged leather is the toughest ordinary leather, from the beasts of Felwood, Winterspring, the Plaguelands and Un'Goro, and the base of the great leatherworkers' masterworks."
K.I["Ruined Leather Scraps"]="Scraps of hide too torn to tan whole, which leatherworkers stitch together into their first light leather."
K.I["Rune Thread"]="Rune thread, spun with the same runic patterning as runecloth, binds enchanted seams."
K.I["Rune of Portals"]="The rune by which a mage opens a portal for others."
K.I["Rune of Teleportation"]="The rune by which a mage teleports to the great cities."
K.I["Runecloth"]="Runecloth is woven with runic patterns that bind magic into the weave itself, the finest ordinary cloth of the age and the material of the great tailors' masterworks. The Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade both dress their elite in it."
K.I["Sacred Candle"]="The sacred candle, the priest's reagent for prayers of fortitude and spirit."
K.I["Salt"]="Salt, for curing hides and seasoning the pot."
K.I["Sandworm Meat"]="The meat of the sandworms of Silithus."
K.I["Scale of Onyxia"]="A scale from the hide of Onyxia herself, Broodmother of the black dragonflight, proof against fire and the stuff of the Onyxia Scale Cloak."
K.I["Scorpid Stinger"]="The stinger of a scorpid, wanted by the Darkspear's and Gadgetzan's alchemists."
K.I["Shadow Silk"]="Shadow silk is the dark, unnaturally fine silk of the spiders of the deep places and the Scourge's breeding pits."
K.I["Shadowcat Hide"]="The black pelt of the shadowcats of Darkshore and Ashenvale."
K.I["Shadowgem"]="Shadowgem, a dark violet stone of the tin veins, wanted by enchanters and engineers."
K.I["Sharp Claw"]="A sharp claw from a cat, raptor or bear."
K.I["Silk Cloth"]="Silk is the fine, strong cloth of the merchant classes, woven in Stormwind and Lordaeron from the thread of cultivated silkworms and, more cheaply, from the spinnerets of giant spiders. The better sort of brigand wears it."
K.I["Silken Thread"]="Silken thread, strong and nearly invisible, for the seams of good cloth."
K.I["Silver Bar"]="Silver in bars, for the jeweller, the enchanter's rods and silvered weapons."
K.I["Silver Contact"]="A silver contact, for the engineer's electrical devices."
K.I["Silver Ore"]="Silver is found in rare veins alongside tin, and is used by jewellers, enchanters and the smiths who make weapons against the undead."
K.I["Silverleaf"]="Silverleaf grows at the foot of trees in every starting land, its silvery leaves used in the simplest potions and salves."
K.I["Simple Wood"]="Simple wood is kindling and whittling stock, sold by every general goods merchant for campfires and the first engineering projects."
K.I["Slimy Murloc Scale"]="The scales of a murloc, which leatherworkers use once they have stopped smelling."
K.I["Small Egg"]="Small eggs are laid by the birds of the plains and coasts and gathered from their nests and the bodies of those that carry them; cooks want them for cakes and omelettes."
K.I["Small Flame Sac"]="The flame sac of a fire-breathing whelp or lizard, used in alchemy and engineering."
K.I["Small Lustrous Pearl"]="Small lustrous pearls from the clams of the shallow coasts."
K.I["Small Obsidian Shard"]="A shard of the black volcanic glass of Blackrock Mountain and Ahn'Qiraj."
K.I["Small Spider Leg"]="The leg of a small spider, for the cook's spider sausage."
K.I["Small Venom Sac"]="The venom sac of a small spider or scorpid, used in anti-venom and the rogues' poisons."
K.I["Soft Frenzy Flesh"]="The soft flesh of the frenzy fish."
K.I["Solid Blasting Powder"]="Solid blasting powder, for the big bombs."
K.I["Solid Stone"]="Solid stone from mithril deposits, dense and fine-grained."
K.I["Soothing Spices"]="Soothing spices, for the cook's finer dishes."
K.I["Soul Dust"]="Soul dust, from disenchanted items of the middle grades."
K.I["Soul Shard"]="A soul shard is the captured soul of a dying foe, the warlock's fuel for summoning and the darkest spells."
K.I["Souldarite"]="Souldarite is a strange mineral found only in the deepest veins of Blackrock Mountain."
K.I["Spider Ichor"]="The ichor of giant spiders."
K.I["Spider's Silk"]="The silk of giant spiders, stronger than any spun by hand, drawn from their spinnerets by tailors who are not squeamish."
K.I["Stag Meat"]="Venison, from the stags of the forests."
K.I["Star Ruby"]="Star ruby, a red stone of the mithril and truesilver deposits that shows a star in its heart."
K.I["Star Wood"]="Star wood, a wood that holds enchantment, for the enchanter's rods."
K.I["Steel Bar"]="Steel is iron smelted with coal, harder and truer than iron alone."
K.I["Stonescale Eel"]="The stonescale eel of the deep coasts, whose oil goes into the great protection potions."
K.I["Stormwind Seasoning Herbs"]="The seasoning herbs of Stormwind's kitchens."
K.I["Strange Dust"]="Strange dust is the residue of disenchanted magical items, the enchanter's first reagent."
K.I["Stranglekelp"]="Stranglekelp grows underwater along the coasts and in deep pools, and is harvested by herbalists who can hold their breath."
K.I["Stranglethorn Seed"]="The stranglethorn seed, the druid's reagent for rebirth."
K.I["Strider Meat"]="The meat of the plainstrider, the Barrens' commonest game."
K.I["Stringy Vulture Meat"]="The tough meat of the buzzards and vultures of the dry lands."
K.I["Stringy Wolf Meat"]="The lean, stringy flank of a wolf, roasted over every campfire in the starting lands."
K.I["Strong Flux"]="Strong flux, the smith's reagent for the finer smelting."
K.I["Sulfuron Ingot"]="A Sulfuron ingot is dark iron shot through with the Firelord's own fire, taken from the Molten Core and worked only on the Black Anvil."
K.I["Sungrass"]="Sungrass is a tall yellow grass of the highlands of Feralas, the Hinterlands and Azshara, used in elixirs of agility and the great healing potions."
K.I["Swiftthistle"]="Swiftthistle grows hidden among briarthorn and mageroyal, and is the key to the swiftness potion."
K.I["Symbol of Divinity"]="The symbol of divinity, the paladin's reagent for divine intervention."
K.I["Symbol of Kings"]="The symbol of kings, the paladin's reagent for the greater blessings."
K.I["Tangy Clam Meat"]="The tangy meat of the larger clams."
K.I["Tender Crab Meat"]="The tender meat of the larger crabs."
K.I["Tender Crocolisk Meat"]="The tender meat of a young crocolisk."
K.I["Tender Wolf Meat"]="The tender cut of a highland wolf."
K.I["Thick Hide"]="A whole thick hide, the kind only an expert skinner takes clean."
K.I["Thick Leather"]="Thick leather, from the hardiest beasts of the wild places, is the leatherworker's high-grade stock."
K.I["Thick Murloc Scale"]="The scales of the larger murlocs, slimy to handle and surprisingly tough."
K.I["Thick Spider's Silk"]="The heavy silk of the great cave and forest spiders, used in the better cloth armour."
K.I["Thick Wolfhide"]="The heavy winter pelt of a great wolf."
K.I["Thieves' Tools"]="Thieves' tools, the rogue's picks and rakes."
K.I["Thin Kodo Leather"]="The lighter hide of a young kodo, worked by the tauren into everything from boots to drums."
K.I["Thorium Bar"]="Thorium in bars, the dense black metal of the great armourers."
K.I["Thorium Ore"]="Thorium is the dense black metal of the deep country, mined in Un'Goro, Winterspring, the Plaguelands and Silithus, and the Thorium Brotherhood guards the secrets of its forging."
K.I["Thorium Tube"]="A thorium tube, for the engineer's greatest rifles."
K.I["Thorium Widget"]="A thorium widget, the engineer's heaviest component."
K.I["Thunder Lizard Tail"]="The tail of a thunder lizard of the Barrens, Desolace or Un'Goro."
K.I["Tiger Meat"]="The meat of the tigers of Stranglethorn."
K.I["Tigerseye"]="Tigerseye, a banded golden stone of the copper veins."
K.I["Tin Ore"]="Tin is alloyed with copper to make bronze, and its veins run through the hills of Redridge, Hillsbrad, the Barrens and Ashenvale."
K.I["Tomb Dust"]="The dust of the tombs of Zul'Farrak."
K.I["Tough Condor Meat"]="The meat of the condors of Thousand Needles and the Badlands."
K.I["Truesilver Bar"]="Truesilver in bars, luminous and precious, for the smith's and enchanter's masterworks."
K.I["Truesilver Ore"]="Truesilver is a rare, faintly luminous metal found beside mithril, which takes enchantment like no other and is the stuff of the smith's masterworks."
K.I["Truesilver Transformer"]="A truesilver transformer, for the engineer's finest work."
K.I["Turtle Meat"]="Turtle meat, for soup."
K.I["Turtle Scale"]="The scutes of the great turtles, which leatherworkers set into scale armour."
K.I["Vision Dust"]="Vision dust, from disenchanted items of the higher grades."
K.I["Warbear Leather"]="The hide of the great warbears of Felwood and Winterspring."
K.I["Weak Flux"]="Weak flux, the smith's reagent for smelting bronze and the first steel."
K.I["Whirring Bronze Gizmo"]="A whirring bronze gizmo, the heart of gnomish devices."
K.I["White Spider Meat"]="The pale meat of the forest spiders."
K.I["Wicked Claw"]="A wicked claw from one of the great predators."
K.I["Wild Berries"]="Wild berries, the druid's reagent for the mark of the wild."
K.I["Wild Steelbloom"]="Wild steelbloom grows on the mountainsides of Arathi, Stonetalon and Stranglethorn, and is used in the elixirs of strength."
K.I["Wild Thornroot"]="Wild thornroot, the druid's reagent for the greater gift of the wild."
K.I["Wildvine"]="Wildvine is a creeper found tangled in purple lotus, wanted by the Gurubashi trolls' witch doctors and by alchemists."
K.I["Wintersbite"]="Wintersbite grows only in the cold hills of Alterac, and is used in the frost oils of the alchemists."
K.I["Wooden Stock"]="A wooden stock for the gunsmith's first rifles, sold by engineering suppliers."
K.I["Wool Cloth"]="Wool is shorn from the sheep of Hillsbrad, the Wetlands and the hills of Khaz Modan and woven into the warm plain garments of the northern kingdoms. Tailors use bolts of it for their second grade of work."
K.I["Yellow Dye"]="Yellow dye, for the tailor's colours."
K.J={}
K.J["11"]="Rings are the commonest of enchanted trinkets, small enough to be carried away by anything with pockets."
K.J["12"]="Trinkets are the odd charms and devices of a hundred crafts and cultures, each with its own small magic."
K.J["19"]="A tabard is the badge of allegiance to a guild, a faction or a cause."
K.J["2"]="Necklaces and amulets are the jewellers' and enchanters' work, and most of those found in the wild were a dead adventurer's."
K.J["23"]="Held in the off hand, books, orbs and skulls serve the casters as foci for the art."
K.J["4"]="A shirt, worn under armour or alone in town."
K.K={}
K.K["0"]="Potions are the alchemists' stock in trade, brewed from the herbs of the field and sold or bartered across Azeroth."
K.K["1"]="Elixirs are the alchemists' lasting draughts, which strengthen body or mind for an hour."
K.K["10"]="Fireworks are the engineers' festival trade."
K.K["11"]="Explosives are the engineers' stock in trade, as dangerous to the thrower as to the target."
K.K["12"]="Reagents are the spellcasters' consumable tools, sold by the reagent vendors of every town."
K.K["13"]="Salves and tinctures are the herbalists' and alchemists' lesser remedies."
K.K["2"]="Flasks are the master alchemists' greatest brews, requiring black lotus and lasting through death itself."
K.K["3"]="Scrolls are enchantments written on parchment, read once and gone, and every brigand seems to carry one."
K.K["4"]="Bandages are the field medic's art, rolled from the cloth of the age."
K.K["5"]="Food is the traveller's first concern, bought from innkeepers and cooks or made over the campfire from what the hunt brings in."
K.K["6"]="Drink is sold by every innkeeper and barkeep from Goldshire to Gadgetzan, and the dwarves and the Winterfall furbolg brew the strongest."
K.K["7"]="Oils are the alchemists' and enchanters' anointings for weapon and armour."
K.K["9"]="Poisons are the rogues' art, brewed from venom sacs and fadeleaf and sold only by the guilds' own vendors."
K.L={}
K.L["0"]="It is fitted to those newly set out on the road."
K.L["1"]="It is fitted to adventurers who have left their home valleys behind."
K.L["2"]="It is fitted to adventurers of some experience, who have seen the middle country."
K.L["3"]="It is fitted to seasoned travellers who have crossed a continent."
K.L["4"]="It is fitted to veterans of the far country and the great dungeons."
K.L["5"]="It is fitted to the heroes who face the old enemies of the world."
K.L["6"]="It is fitted to the champions who stand against the Firelord, the dragonflights and the Scourge."
K.P={}
K.P["Blackrock orcs"]="The Blackrock clan was the backbone of the old Horde and never surrendered. Under Rend Blackhand and the black dragon Nefarian they hold Blackrock Spire and raid the Burning Steppes and Redridge."
K.P["Dalaran wizards"]="The mages of Dalaran, the Kirin Tor, keep agents and apprentices across Lordaeron's ruins, studying the Scourge and the worgen curse at Ambermill and in Silverpine."
K.P["Dark Iron dwarves"]="The Dark Iron dwarves broke from Ironforge in the War of the Three Hammers and, losing, summoned Ragnaros into Blackrock Mountain. From Shadowforge City their emperor's armies hold the Searing Gorge, the Badlands and the Depths, and their smiths are the finest in Azeroth after the Firelord's own."
K.P["Defias brigands"]="The Defias Brotherhood began as the Stonemasons' Guild, the men who rebuilt Stormwind and were cheated of their pay. Under Edwin VanCleef they turned to banditry in Westfall and Elwynn, and their red bandanas mark every highwayman and pillager between Moonbrook and the Stockade."
K.P["Dragonmaw orcs"]="The Dragonmaw clan enslaved the red dragonflight in the Second War and still holds the approaches to Grim Batol in the Wetlands, keeping to the old ways."
K.P["Grimtotem tauren"]="The Grimtotem are the tauren tribe under Magatha Grimtotem that rejects the Horde and plots to rule Mulgore alone. Their camps in Stonetalon, Thousand Needles and Feralas are hostile to everyone."
K.P["Scarlet Crusaders"]="The Scarlet Crusade is the order of zealots who rose from Lordaeron's ruin to purge the undead, and in time any living person they suspect of taint. From the Monastery, Hearthglen, Tyr's Hand and the Bastion of Stratholme they war with the Forsaken, the Scourge and the Argent Dawn alike."
K.P["Syndicate rogues"]="The Syndicate is the remnant of the nobility of Alterac, the kingdom dissolved for treason in the Second War, turned to brigandage. They hold Durnholde and the ruins of Alterac and Stromgarde, and they rob with the manners of the gentry they once were."
K.P["Twilight's Hammer cultists"]="The Twilight's Hammer were once an orc clan and are now a cult of every race, worshipping the Old Gods and working for the end of the world. They gather in Silithus, in Blackfathom Deeps and wherever elemental lords stir."
K.P["Venture Company workers"]="The Venture Company is a goblin trading company that strips forests and mines wherever it can plant a shredder, in Stonetalon, the Barrens, Mulgore and the Hinterlands, with hired muscle of every race to guard the profits."
K.P["Wastewander nomads"]="The Wastewander are human bandits who hold the water holes of Tanaris against the goblins of Gadgetzan, robbing caravans on the desert road."
K.P["abominations"]="Abominations are the Scourge's stitched giants, built in Naxxramas and Stratholme from many corpses and the hooks and chains that bind them."
K.P["air elementals"]="Air elementals, dust devils and cyclones haunt the high and the dry places of Silithus, Arathi and Desolace."
K.P["bandits"]="Bandits, highwaymen and marauders of every stripe plague the roads between settlements, and what they take from travellers they carry until someone takes it back."
K.P["carnivorous plants"]="The carnivorous lashers and bloodpetals of Un'Goro and Maraudon, which take in whatever they catch."
K.P["centaur"]="The centaur are the half-horse children of the earth elemental Theradras and the demigod Zaetar, who have warred on the tauren and on each other for a thousand years. The Kolkar, Magram, Gelkis, Galak and Maraudine clans each carry the spoils of their raids."
K.P["cultists"]="The cults of the Burning Legion, the Burning Blade and the Shadow Council and the Cult of the Damned among them, draw the ambitious and the desperate from every race. Their acolytes carry the reagents and the stolen goods of their rites."
K.P["dragons"]="The great dragons themselves: the black flight of Deathwing's children, the mad green drakes of the Sunken Temple, the blue of Azshara and the red of Grim Batol."
K.P["dragonspawn"]="Dragonspawn are the dragons' serpent-bodied servitor race, the Blackrock Spire's and Blackwing Lair's heavy guard."
K.P["earth elementals"]="Earth elementals and their kin stir in the Badlands, Arathi and Silithus, and their cores and shards are prized by alchemists and blacksmiths."
K.P["elves"]="The night elves of the Sentinels and the Highborne remnants of Azshara and Eldre'Thalas, and those elves who have fallen under the sway of the nightmare or the demons."
K.P["felhounds"]="Felhounds are the Legion's mana-eating hunting beasts, loosed wherever demons gather."
K.P["fire elementals"]="Fire elementals rise wherever Ragnaros's influence is strong: Blackrock Mountain, the Searing Gorge, the Burning Steppes and the fire pits of Un'Goro."
K.P["furbolg"]="Furbolg are great bear-folk of Kalimdor's forests, once gentle. The Legion's corruption during the Third War drove the Gnarlpine, Thistlefur, Foulweald and Deadwood tribes to savagery, and only the Timbermaw and the Stillpine remain sane."
K.P["ghosts and spirits"]="The spirits of the unquiet dead haunt their graves, their ruined homes and the battlefields where they fell, and the ectoplasm and old coins they leave behind are prized by alchemists and collectors."
K.P["ghouls"]="Ghouls are the Scourge's shock troops, peasants raised with hunger and little else in their heads."
K.P["gnolls"]="Gnolls are hyena-headed raiders who live by plunder; the Riverpaw and Redridge packs trouble Stormwind's lands, the Rot Hide serve the Scourge in Silverpine, and the Woodpaw and Palemane roam Kalimdor. What they steal they rarely keep in good repair."
K.P["goblins"]="The goblins of the Steamwheedle, Venture and other cartels are neutral in the great war and loyal only to profit, and their bruisers and tinkers are armed accordingly."
K.P["golems"]="Golems of stone and iron, built by dwarves and Titans to guard and to labour."
K.P["greater demons"]="Doomguards, dreadlords and felguards, the Legion's officers and heavy infantry."
K.P["harpies"]="Harpies are winged, bird-footed women who nest on the cliffs of Kalimdor in matriarchal roosts, the Bloodfury, Witchwing and Windfury among them. They steal shiny things and carry them to their aeries."
K.P["hydras"]="Hydras, many-headed reptiles of the pools of Zul'Farrak and the Swamp of Sorrows."
K.P["infernals"]="Infernals are burning stone giants hurled from the sky by the Legion's summoners."
K.P["insects"]="The giant insects of Silithus, Tanaris, Un'Goro and the Hive: silithid, scarabs and wasps bred by the qiraji."
K.P["leper gnomes"]="The leper gnomes are the survivors of Gnomeregan's irradiation, driven mad and loyal to the usurper Thermaplugg, still tinkering in the ruined city's halls."
K.P["mechanical constructs"]="The machines of gnome and goblin engineering, harvest golems, shredders and the defences of Gnomeregan."
K.P["murlocs"]="Murlocs are amphibious fish-folk who have spread along every coast of Azeroth in the last generation, for reasons no one has fathomed. They gather trinkets from the shallows and the drowned, and their oracles hoard the stranger finds."
K.P["naga"]="The naga are the Highborne who sank with Queen Azshara's palace and were transformed by the Old Gods into sea-serpent folk. They have begun to return to the coasts of Kalimdor and Lordaeron, and their sirens and myrmidons carry the salvage of ten thousand years under the sea."
K.P["ogres"]="Ogres came to Azeroth with the Horde and stayed when it fell, forming clans of their own: the Boulderfist and Crushridge in the north, the Dunemaul of Tanaris, the Gordunni of Feralas and the Stonemaul of Dustwallow. They are strong, dull and acquisitive, and their camps are heaped with loot."
K.P["oozes and slimes"]="Oozes and slimes breed in the plague cauldrons of Lordaeron, the swamps of Un'Goro and the Swamp of Sorrows, and the sewers of the Undercity, digesting whatever they engulf."
K.P["orcs"]="The orcs of the new Horde and the renegade clans, the Warsong and the Bleeding Hollow among them, warriors who carry the trophies of their fights."
K.P["pirates"]="The Bloodsail Buccaneers and Southsea Freebooters are the pirate fleets of the South Seas, at feud with the Steamwheedle goblins over Booty Bay and the Tanaris coast. Their holds are full of everything the trade routes carry."
K.P["quilboar"]="The quilboar are boar-like people who hold the thorny warrens of Razorfen and the bramble camps of the Barrens and Mulgore, worshipping the dead demigod Agamaggan from whose blood they say the thorns grew. The Razormane, Bristleback and Death's Head tribes raid the Horde constantly."
K.P["satyrs"]="Satyrs are night elves corrupted by the Legion into horned, hooved demons, who haunt the ruins of Ashenvale, Felwood and Desolace and tempt others to the same fall."
K.P["skeletons"]="The bones of old wars and plague pits, raised by necromancers to stand guard with rusted blades."
K.P["soldiers and mercenaries"]="Soldiers, deserters and hired blades of every banner, whose kit is whatever their last paymaster issued."
K.P["spellcasters"]="Mages, warlocks, shadow priests and witch doctors of a dozen orders and tribes, who carry the reagents and curios of their art."
K.P["stone constructs"]="Stone and Titan-forged constructs set to guard the ancient vaults."
K.P["tauren"]="The tauren of the plains, great horned nomads who honour the Earth Mother and carry the hides, totems and herbs of their craft."
K.P["the Scourge"]="The Scourge is the Lich King's army of the dead, commanded from Naxxramas and Stratholme by liches, death knights and the Cult of the Damned."
K.P["townsfolk and militia"]="Farmers, miners, militiamen and the ordinary folk of the frontier settlements, some of them driven to violence by plague, possession or desperation."
K.P["treants and bog beasts"]="Treants, bog beasts and the walking plants of the swamps and forests, kin to the ancients."
K.P["troggs"]="Troggs are the stunted, brutish cousins of the dwarves, Titan-made things that burrowed up from the deep when Uldaman was opened and have overrun Gnomeregan and the mines of Khaz Modan."
K.P["trolls"]="The trolls of Azeroth are an ancient people fallen from empire: the Gurubashi jungle tribes of Stranglethorn, the Amani and Witherbark forest trolls of the north, the Sandfury of Tanaris and the Frostmane of Dun Morogh. Save for the Darkspear, who joined the Horde, they are enemies of all, and their witch doctors and headhunters carry the fetishes and coins of their victims."
K.P["voidwalkers"]="Voidwalkers are shadowy servitors drawn from the Twisting Nether by warlocks."
K.P["water elementals"]="Water elementals form from the pools of Azeroth where the elemental plane presses close, and from the summonings of mages."
K.P["whelps"]="Whelps are the hatchlings of the dragonflights, found in nesting grounds such as the Wyrmbog, Lethlor Ravine and the Wetlands marsh."
K.P["worgen"]="The worgen are wolf-men summoned from another world by the mage Arugal to fight the Scourge, who turned on their summoners and spread through Silverpine and Duskwood."
K.P["zombies"]="The shambling dead of plagued villages, still wearing the rags and carrying the pockets of their former lives."
K.Q={}
K.Q["0.0"]="It is poor stuff, worn out or badly made, worth little but to a vendor."
K.Q["0.1"]="Worn, broken or shoddy, it is the sort of thing one sells to the first merchant."
K.Q["1.0"]="It is plain, common work of the kind every settlement produces."
K.Q["1.1"]="It is of ordinary quality, the everyday issue of soldiers and travellers."
K.Q["2.0"]="It is good work, a cut above the common run, with a touch of enchantment in it."
K.Q["2.1"]="A piece of this quality carries a minor enchantment and is worth keeping."
K.Q["3.0"]="It is rare work, the kind a master craftsman makes a few times in a life, carrying a real enchantment."
K.Q["3.1"]="Pieces of this quality are sought after; they carry strong enchantments and change hands for serious coin."
K.Q["4.0"]="It is an epic piece, of the quality that heroes carry and bards name."
K.Q["4.1"]="Work of this quality is legendary in all but name, and the great dungeons are plundered for it."
K.Q["5.0"]="It is a legendary artefact, one of a handful in the world."
K.R={}
K.R["0"]="A leather of the tanners' trade, taken from the hunt and cured for the leatherworkers."
K.R["10"]="A venom of the alchemists' and rogues' trade."
K.R["11"]="A component of the engineers' and smiths' trades."
K.R["12"]="An herb of the herbalists' trade, gathered for the alchemists."
K.R["15"]="A provision of the cooks' trade."
K.R["16"]="A reagent of the spellcasting classes."
K.R["17"]="A supply of the crafting trades."
K.R["3"]="A smelted metal, ready for the forges of the blacksmiths and engineers."
K.R["4"]="A stone of the smiths' and engineers' trade."
K.R["5"]="A reagent of the enchanters' trade, distilled from magical things."
K.R["6"]="A cut of the hunt, for the cook's pot."
K.T={}
K.T["129"]="First aid is the field medic's craft, rolling the cloth of the age into bandages and brewing anti-venom from the sacs of spiders and scorpids."
K.T["164"]="Blacksmiths work the ores of Azeroth at anvils in every town: the Great Forge of Ironforge, the orcish forges of Orgrimmar and the Black Anvil of the Dark Irons. The armoursmiths of Ironforge and the weaponsmiths of Orgrimmar each keep secrets the other does not."
K.T["165"]="Leatherworkers tan the hides of the hunt into armour and kits. The tauren and the night elves are its greatest masters, and its three great schools, the dragonscale, elemental and tribal, each keep their own patterns."
K.T["171"]="Alchemists brew the herbs of Azeroth into potions, elixirs and flasks, and transmute metals and essences into one another. The Royal Apothecary Society of the Undercity and the Gnomeregan alchemists are its rival academies."
K.T["185"]="Cooking is the humblest and most universal of the crafts, practised at every campfire and inn from Goldshire to Gadgetzan with whatever the hunt and the market provide."
K.T["186"]="Miners dig the veins and deposits of Azeroth and smelt the ore into bars for the smiths and engineers."
K.T["197"]="Tailors weave the cloth of Azeroth into the garments and bags of every people; the great tailors of Stormwind and the Kirin Tor and the mooncloth weavers of Darnassus are its masters."
K.T["202"]="Engineering is the gnomes' and goblins' art, turning metal, stone and powder into guns, scopes, bombs and devices that mostly work. The Gnomish and Goblin schools each hold their secrets jealously."
K.T["333"]="Enchanters disenchant the magical goods of the world into dusts and essences and weave them back into weapons and armour with their rods. It is a slow, expensive and arcane trade."
K.T["40"]="Poisons are the rogues' craft, taught in the back rooms of SI:7 and the Deathstalkers."
K.V={}
K.V["Darkmoon Faire vendors"]="The Darkmoon Faire's vendors sell Silas Darkmoon's prizes and curios when the Faire comes to Elwynn or Mulgore."
K.V["alchemy suppliers"]="Alchemy suppliers sell vials and the odd herb to the brewers."
K.V["arcane goods vendors"]="Arcane goods vendors sell the curios and reagents of the mages."
K.V["armorer & shield crafters"]="Armourers and shield-crafters sell their own forged work."
K.V["armorers"]="Armourers sell their own forged work."
K.V["axe merchants"]="Axe merchants sell the Horde's favourite weapon."
K.V["blacksmithing suppliers"]="Blacksmithing suppliers sell flux, coal and the smith's hammers."
K.V["blade merchants"]="Blade merchants sell swords and daggers."
K.V["bow merchants"]="Bow merchants sell bows and arrows."
K.V["bowyers"]="Bowyers sell the bows and arrows of the hunters."
K.V["camp traders"]="Camp traders sell the necessities of the frontier."
K.V["cloth & leather armor merchants"]="Cloth and leather armourers sell the lighter kit of the field."
K.V["cloth armor and accessories"]="Cloth armourers sell robes and accessories."
K.V["cloth armor merchants"]="Cloth armourers sell the robes and hoods of the casting classes."
K.V["clothiers"]="Clothiers sell the finer garments of town."
K.V["cooking suppliers"]="Cooking suppliers sell spices, salt and the odd recipe."
K.V["cool guys"]="An eccentric merchant."
K.V["demon trainers"]="The warlock trainers of the Horde and Alliance, who teach the binding of demons in the Slaughtered Lamb and the Cleft of Shadow, also sell the tools of the art."
K.V["enchanting suppliers"]="Enchanting suppliers sell the rods and vellums of the enchanters."
K.V["engineering suppliers"]="Engineering suppliers sell the stocks, tubes and powders of the tinkers' trade."
K.V["fishermans"]="Fishermen sell their catch and their gear on the docks."
K.V["fishing suppliers"]="Fishing suppliers sell poles, lures and bait on every pier."
K.V["food and drink vendors"]="Cooks, bakers, barkeeps and butchers sell the staples of the road in every inn and market."
K.V["frostwolf supply officers"]="The Frostwolf clan's supply officers issue gear to the Horde's champions of Alterac Valley."
K.V["general goods merchants"]="General goods merchants are the backbone of every settlement, from Goldshire's Smith Argus to the stalls of the Crossroads, selling wood, flint, bags, thread, dye and the odds and ends of travel."
K.V["gun smiths"]="Gunsmiths sell the dwarves' and goblins' firearms and shot."
K.V["gunsmith & bowyers"]="Gunsmiths and bowyers sell the ranged weapons of the hunters."
K.V["heavy armor merchants"]="Heavy armourers sell the mail and plate of the soldiering classes."
K.V["herbalism suppliers"]="Herbalism suppliers sell the herbalist's tools."
K.V["holiday fireworks vendors"]="Fireworks vendors appear for the festivals."
K.V["horse breeders"]="Horse breeders of Elwynn sell the mounts of Stormwind's knights."
K.V["innkeepers"]="Innkeepers keep the hearths where travellers rest, and sell food and drink to those passing through."
K.V["leather armor merchants"]="Leather armourers sell the plain leather kit of hunters and rogues."
K.V["leatherworking suppliers"]="Leatherworking suppliers sell thread, salt and kits to the tanners."
K.V["light armor merchants"]="Light armourers sell the leather and cloth of the lighter classes."
K.V["mail armor merchants"]="Mail armourers sell riveted rings to hunters, shaman and the younger warriors."
K.V["merchants"]="Merchants of every kind, in every market."
K.V["mount vendors"]="Mount vendors sell the riding beasts of their people."
K.V["poison vendors"]="Poison vendors supply the rogues' guilds, and nobody else."
K.V["quartermasters"]="Quartermasters issue the gear of their faction to those who have earned its trust."
K.V["reagent vendors"]="Reagent vendors supply the candles, runes, symbols and powders of the spellcasting classes in every town of any size."
K.V["shield merchants"]="Shield merchants sell bucklers and shields."
K.V["silverwing supply officers"]="The Silverwing Sentinels' supply officers issue gear to the defenders of Ashenvale."
K.V["smokywood pastures"]="Smokywood Pastures is the goblin company that sells the trappings of the Feast of Winter Veil."
K.V["stormpike supply officers"]="The Stormpike Guard's supply officers issue gear to the dwarves' allies in Alterac Valley."
K.V["tailoring suppliers"]="Tailoring suppliers sell thread, dye and the odd bolt to the tailors of every town."
K.V["the argent dawns"]="The Argent Dawn's quartermasters at Light's Hope Chapel issue gear to those who have earned the Dawn's trust against the Scourge."
K.V["the thorium brotherhoods"]="The Thorium Brotherhood's quartermaster at Thorium Point sells the secrets of dark iron to those who have earned the Brotherhood's trust."
K.V["warsong supply officers"]="The Warsong Outriders' supply officers issue gear to the Horde's lumber-camp raiders."
K.V["weapon merchants"]="Weapon merchants sell the plain arms of the common soldier."
K.V["weapon smiths"]="Weaponsmiths sell their own work, the plain steel of the town forge."
K.V["weapon vendors"]="Weapon merchants sell the plain arms of the common soldier."
K.V["weapons merchants"]="Weapon merchants sell the plain arms of the common soldier."
K.W={}
K.W["0"]="The one-handed axe is the orc's weapon of choice and the dwarf's second, swung from the saddle of a wolf or ram as readily as on foot."
K.W["1"]="The great axe is the weapon of the orcish grunt and the dwarven mountaineer, slow and terrible."
K.W["10"]="The staff is the mage's, the priest's and the druid's weapon, as much a focus for the art as a cudgel."
K.W["13"]="Fist weapons, claws and knuckles, are the weapon of the brawlers of Booty Bay, the troll berserkers and the shaman and druids who fight close."
K.W["14"]="An oddity among weapons."
K.W["15"]="The dagger is the rogue's weapon and the mage's sidearm, quick and easily hidden."
K.W["16"]="Thrown weapons, knives and axes, are the hunter's and the warrior's opening volley."
K.W["18"]="The crossbow is the weapon of the dwarven and human militias, slow to load and hard-hitting."
K.W["19"]="Wands are the spellcaster's sidearm, enchanted rods that spit the element bound into them."
K.W["2"]="The bow is the hunter's weapon across Azeroth, the night elves' sentinel longbow and the troll headhunter's shortbow alike."
K.W["20"]="The fishing pole, the angler's only weapon."
K.W["3"]="Firearms are the dwarves' gift to warfare, blunderbusses and rifles turned out by the gunsmiths of Ironforge and copied badly by the goblins."
K.W["4"]="The mace is the weapon of the paladin and the priest, who may not shed blood with an edge, and of the tauren and dwarf who simply like weight."
K.W["5"]="The great hammer is the weapon of the paladin orders and the mountain kings, and of every tauren who can lift one."
K.W["6"]="Polearms are the weapon of the Sentinels and the footmen of the human kingdoms, and of the hunters who keep their quarry at arm's length."
K.W["7"]="The sword is the weapon of the knights and footmen of the human kingdoms and of the warriors of every race who can afford good steel."
K.W["8"]="The great sword is the knight's weapon, and the weapon of the death knights who were knights once."
K.Z={}
K.Z["Alterac Mountains"]="The Alterac Mountains are the cold, ruined homeland of a kingdom destroyed for treason in the Second War. The Syndicate, its former nobles turned bandits, haunts the ruined city, Crushridge ogres hold the heights, yeti and winter wolves the slopes, and in the deepest valley the Frostwolf orcs and Stormpike dwarves fight their endless war."
K.Z["Arathi Highlands"]="The Arathi Highlands are rolling grassland and limestone where the first human kingdom, Arathor, was founded; the ruins of Stromgarde still stand on its western edge, divided between the kingdom's last loyalists, the Syndicate and the Boulderfist ogres. The Horde's Hammerfall rises in the east on the bones of the old internment camp, and the Witherbark trolls hold the southern hills."
K.Z["Ashenvale"]="Ashenvale is the night elves' ancestral forest, a cathedral of ancient trees where Astranaar and the Sentinels hold against the Horde's Warsong lumber camp and the Splintertree outpost. The Thistlefur and Foulweald furbolg have gone wild, the satyrs of Xavian and Satyrnaar corrupt the eastern woods, and the demon-tainted Felfire Hill smoulders near Demon Fall Canyon, where Grom Hellscream fell."
K.Z["Azshara"]="Azshara is the shattered coast of the old Highborne empire, its red-leaved forest strewn with ruined temples where the ghosts of elves still argue. Naga of the Spitelash hold the shore and the Ruins of Eldarath, the blue dragon Azuregos guards the southern coast, and the Horde's Valormok and the Alliance's Talrendis Point watch each other across the ravines."
K.Z["Badlands"]="The Badlands are a wasteland of red rock and dust east of Loch Modan, broken by the ruin of Uldaman, a Titan vault the Dark Iron dwarves and the Shadowforge have dug into. Black dragonkin nest at Lethlor Ravine, ogres and the Rock Elemental roam the canyons, and the goblins of Kargath keep an outpost for the Horde."
K.Z["Blackrock Mountain"]="Blackrock Mountain is the volcano that rose when the Dark Iron dwarves summoned Ragnaros, standing between the Burning Steppes and Searing Gorge. The Dark Irons hold the Depths below, the Blackrock orcs the Spire above, and in the fires beneath the Firelord waits."
K.Z["Blasted Lands"]="The Blasted Lands are what the Dark Portal made of the Black Morass: red dust, dead trees and the hulking stone frame of the Portal itself, guarded now by the Nethergarde Keep mages of Stormwind. Demons and the Shadowsworn cultists of the Burning Legion haunt the Tainted Scar, and the ogres of the Dreadmaul clan hold the southern reaches."
K.Z["Burning Steppes"]="The Burning Steppes are a scorched plain of cinders and lava flows in the shadow of Blackrock Mountain. The Blackrock orcs under the black dragon Nefarian's sway rule it from their camps and the Dreadmaul Rock ogres hold the east, while the Thorium Brotherhood dwarves maintain their forge at Flame Crest and Morgan's Vigil keeps a Stormwind watch on the pass to Redridge."
K.Z["Darkshore"]="Darkshore is a grey, wind-scoured coast of ruined night elf towers north of Ashenvale, served by the port of Auberdine. Naga of the Hatecrest hold the sea caves, the Blackwood furbolg have been corrupted, and the Greymist murlocs crowd the beaches among wrecks the storms throw up."
K.Z["Darnassus"]="Darnassus is the night elves' new capital, built in the boughs of the World Tree Teldrassil after the Third War. Its temples to Elune and the Cenarion enclave look out over quiet lakes, and from Rut'theran Village below the boat sails to Darkshore."
K.Z["Deadwind Pass"]="Deadwind Pass is a shunned gorge between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows, overlooked by the sealed tower of Karazhan, where the Guardian Medivh once lived and died. Nothing wholesome grows there; the Deadwind ogres and the ghosts of the tower's household are its only tenants."
K.Z["Deeprun Tram"]="The Deeprun Tram is the gnomish railway running under the sea between Stormwind and Ironforge, lit by its own power and occasionally by escaped rats."
K.Z["Desolace"]="Desolace is a dead, grey land between Stonetalon and Feralas, where the centaur clans Kolkar, Magram and Gelkis wage their endless war of extermination and the Burning Blade cult holds Mannoroc Coven. The Kodo Graveyard and the demon-haunted ruins of Maraudon lie within it, and both factions keep lonely posts at Nijel's Point and Shadowprey Village."
K.Z["Dire Maul"]="Dire Maul is the ruined Highborne city of Eldre'Thalas in Feralas, where the Gordunni ogres squat in the arena and the Shen'dralar elves, kept alive by the imprisoned demon Immol'thar, haunt the libraries."
K.Z["Dun Morogh"]="Dun Morogh is the snowbound homeland of the Bronzebeard dwarves and the gnome refugees of Gnomeregan, a white valley of pines ringed by mountains, with Ironforge at its heart. Frostmane trolls hold the western caves, Rockjaw troggs infest the mines, and wendigo haunt the frozen tunnels; even so, its hunters and brewers count it a gentle land."
K.Z["Durotar"]="Durotar is the harsh red land Thrall chose for the new Horde after the Third War, named for his father. Orgrimmar rises from its northern canyons, the trolls of the Darkspear tribe hold Sen'jin Village on the coast, and Razor Hill drills the Horde's young. Scorpids and boars live on its scrub, and the Burning Blade cult festers in Skull Rock."
K.Z["Duskwood"]="Duskwood lies under a perpetual twilight. Once it was the sunny Brightwood, but since the necromancer Morbent Fel settled at Forlorn Rowe above Raven Hill, the dead walk its graveyards, giant spiders web the trees and the worgen hunt by night. The Night Watch of Darkshire guards the road, and the fallen hero Mor'Ladim wanders the Raven Hill cemetery."
K.Z["Dustwallow Marsh"]="Dustwallow Marsh is a steaming swamp on Kalimdor's eastern coast, dominated by Lady Jaina Proudmoore's island city of Theramore. The Horde's ogre allies of the Stonemaul clan hold Brackenwall Village, the black dragonflight nests at the Wyrmbog, and beneath the marsh Onyxia's own lair lies hidden."
K.Z["Eastern Plaguelands"]="The Eastern Plaguelands are the Scourge's own country: orange skies, fungal growths and the ruined city of Stratholme, where Prince Arthas first damned himself. The Argent Dawn keeps Light's Hope Chapel, the Scarlet Crusade keeps Tyr's Hand, and everywhere else the ziggurats and plague cauldrons of the Cult of the Damned hold sway."
K.Z["Elwynn Forest"]="Elwynn Forest is the green heart of the kingdom of Stormwind: oak and elm, mill-ponds and farmsteads, the Eastvale logging camp and the quiet lake of Crystal Lake. Its troubles are small ones by the standards of the age, though kobolds squat in the old Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines and Defias stragglers and Riverpaw gnolls harass the roads south of Goldshire."
K.Z["Felwood"]="Felwood is a forest poisoned by the Burning Legion's passage during the Third War, its trees weeping fel, its streams green and its furbolg, the Deadwood and Felpaw, driven mad. The Shadow Council's cultists of Jaedenar work demons there, Timbermaw furbolg hold the pass north to Winterspring, and the Emerald Circle druids labour to cleanse what they can."
K.Z["Feralas"]="Feralas is a lush, rainy highland forest in southwestern Kalimdor, scattered with the ruins of the Highborne. The Gordunni ogres hold the great ruined city of Dire Maul, the Grimtotem and Woodpaw gnolls roam the valleys, and the night elves keep Feathermoon Stronghold on the western isle while the Horde holds Camp Mojache in the east. Hippogryphs and giants are common."
K.Z["Hillsbrad Foothills"]="Hillsbrad is green farming country south of Lordaeron's ruins, contested daily between the Alliance town of Southshore and the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill. The yeti of Alterac come down from the hills, the Syndicate holds Durnholde Keep, and murlocs infest the coast."
K.Z["Ironforge"]="Ironforge is the mountain-city of the Bronzebeard dwarves, carved into the heart of Khaz Modan with the Great Forge at its centre. The gnomes of Tinker Town shelter there since the fall of Gnomeregan, and the Deeprun Tram links it to Stormwind."
K.Z["Loch Modan"]="Loch Modan is a cold, pleasant valley of pine and granite east of Ironforge, held by the great Stonewrought Dam and the lake it makes. Dwarves hold Thelsamar and the Explorers' League digs in the south, but the Stonesplinter and Mo'grosh troggs and ogres have grown bold since Gnomeregan fell, and the Dark Irons stir in the hills."
K.Z["Moonglade"]="Moonglade is the druids' sanctuary in northern Kalimdor, a peaceful lakeside glade where the Cenarion Circle gathers in Nighthaven, tauren and night elf druids study together and the great bear spirit of Remulos presides. Nothing hostile lives there by anyone's leave."
K.Z["Mulgore"]="Mulgore is the grassy, mesa-ringed homeland the tauren finally won from the centaur with the Horde's help, with Thunder Bluff rising on its great mesa and Bloodhoof Village on the lake. Kodo herds, prairie wolves and plainstriders cover the plains, Palemane gnolls and Bristleback quilboar trouble the edges, and the Venture Company mines near the Windfury harpy roost."
K.Z["Orgrimmar"]="Orgrimmar is Thrall's capital, raised in the red canyons of Durotar and named for Orgrim Doomhammer. Its Valley of Strength, Drag and Valley of Spirits hold the Horde's merchants and trainers, and the Cleft of Shadow leads down to Ragefire Chasm, where the Burning Blade plots in secret."
K.Z["Redridge Mountains"]="Redridge is a hard border country of red stone and pine lying between Elwynn and the orc-held Burning Steppes. Its one town, Lakeshire, stands on Lake Everstill with its bridge half-built and its garrison stretched thin, for Blackrock orcs raid down from Stonewatch Keep, the Redridge gnoll packs hold the eastern hills, and murlocs crowd the lakeshore."
K.Z["Searing Gorge"]="Searing Gorge is a black bowl of slag and heat north of Blackrock Mountain, mined for centuries by the Dark Iron dwarves and now worked by their slaves. The Thorium Brotherhood, Dark Irons who broke with their emperor, trade from Thorium Point, and the gorge's heat breeds fire elementals and gigantic lava spiders."
K.Z["Silithus"]="Silithus is the insect-haunted desert in Kalimdor's far southwest, where the silithid hives boil up from the ground and the Twilight's Hammer cult courts the Old Gods. The Cenarion Circle holds Cenarion Hold against them, and behind the Scarab Wall lie the ruins and the temple of Ahn'Qiraj, where the qiraji wait."
K.Z["Silverpine Forest"]="Silverpine is a fog-bound forest of silver-barked pines west of Tirisfal, where the Forsaken's Sepulcher stands against Dalaran's agents at Ambermill, the Rot Hide gnolls, and the worgen that the mage Arugal summoned to Shadowfang Keep. Sons of Arugal roam the roads, and the Greymane Wall seals the south."
K.Z["Stonetalon Mountains"]="The Stonetalon Mountains rise between Ashenvale and Desolace, their peaks holding Stonetalon Peak, where the druid Keeper Ordanus and the Talon Den dwell. The Venture Company strips the forest at Windshear Crag, the Horde holds Sun Rock Retreat, and the Grimtotem tauren and harpies hold the heights."
K.Z["Stormwind City"]="Stormwind is the capital of the Alliance in the Eastern Kingdoms, rebuilt in white stone after the orcs burned it in the First War. Its Trade District, Dwarven District and Mage Quarter hold every craft and guild, and the Cathedral of Light and Stormwind Keep stand over all; under the Keep, the Stockade holds Defias prisoners in revolt."
K.Z["Stranglethorn Vale"]="Stranglethorn is the great jungle of the southern Eastern Kingdoms, steaming and loud with panthers, raptors and parrots. The Gurubashi troll empire once ruled it from Zul'Gurub, and its descendants, the Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter tribes, war over the ruins. Goblins of the Steamwheedle Cartel run the port of Booty Bay at the vale's southern tip, the Bloodsail Buccaneers lurk off the coast, and Nesingwary's camp draws hunters from both factions."
K.Z["Swamp of Sorrows"]="The Swamp of Sorrows is a drowned land of cypress and black water east of Deadwind Pass. The Horde's Stonard, oldest orc settlement in Azeroth, still stands here, as does the refuge of the Lost Ones, draenei broken by the journey through the Dark Portal. Beneath its lake lies the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, where the Atal'ai trolls labour to bring back the blood god Hakkar."
K.Z["Tanaris"]="Tanaris is a vast sand desert on Kalimdor's southern coast, ruled by the Steamwheedle goblins from Gadgetzan and the pirate port of Steamwheedle. The Wastewander nomads hold the watering holes, Southsea pirates the Lost Rigger Cove, and the Sandfury trolls their city of Zul'Farrak; the Caverns of Time lie hidden in the eastern mountains, and the silithid gather in the Noxious Lair."
K.Z["Teldrassil"]="Teldrassil is the World Tree raised by the druids off the coast of Kalimdor, so vast that a whole forest grows on its crown. Its glades are wholesome for the most part, but the Gnarlpine furbolg have turned savage, timberlings and webwood spiders grow strange, and the druids fret about a corruption at the roots."
K.Z["The Barrens"]="The Barrens are the great golden savannah at the centre of Kalimdor, the Horde's heartland between Durotar and Mulgore. The Crossroads sits on its spine, the goblin port of Ratchet trades with everyone, and the Razormane and Bristleback quilboar, Kolkar centaur, harpies and Venture Company encroach from every side. Plainstriders, zhevra and lions roam the grass, and beneath it lie the Wailing Caverns."
K.Z["The Hinterlands"]="The Hinterlands are a high, forested shelf between Alterac and the sea, home of the Wildhammer dwarves and their gryphons at Aerie Peak. The Vilebranch and Witherbark forest trolls hold the eastern hills and the troll city of Jintha'Alor, the Horde's Revantusk trolls keep a village on the coast, and owlbeasts and wolves fill the woods."
K.Z["Thousand Needles"]="Thousand Needles is a dry canyon of red stone spires south of the Barrens, where the tauren keep Freewind Post atop the mesas and the Grimtotem plot below. Galak centaur hold the canyon floor, and at its southern end the salt flats of the Shimmering Flats hold the goblin and gnome racetrack of Mirage Raceway."
K.Z["Thunder Bluff"]="Thunder Bluff is the tauren capital, a city of tents and totems atop a great mesa in Mulgore, reached by lifts from the plain below. Its rises hold the druids, hunters and shaman of the tribes, and its markets trade in hides, herbs and kodo."
K.Z["Tirisfal Glades"]="Tirisfal Glades is the northern forest of the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron, now the home of the Forsaken. Below the ruined capital lies the Undercity, Lady Sylvanas's seat; above, the Scarlet Crusade holds the Monastery and its outposts, mindless Scourge still shamble through Agamand Mills and Brill's dead rest uneasily."
K.Z["Un'Goro Crater"]="Un'Goro Crater is a vast volcanic bowl walled off from Tanaris and Silithus, its floor a primordial jungle of devilsaurs, stegodons and giant insects. The Titans seem to have shaped it, for crystal pylons stand in its corners and the mysterious caretakers of the crater's heart tend it; Marshal's Refuge is its only camp."
K.Z["Undercity"]="The Undercity is the Forsaken capital, dug beneath the ruins of Lordaeron's palace. Its canals run with green slime, its Apothecarium brews plagues, and its merchants sell to any of the Horde who can stomach the air."
K.Z["Western Plaguelands"]="The Western Plaguelands are what the Scourge left of Lordaeron's richest farmland: grey grass, plague cauldrons and the shattered towns of Andorhal and Hearthglen. The Argent Dawn holds Chillwind Camp against the undead, the Scarlet Crusade holds Hearthglen, and beneath Caer Darrow the school of necromancy called Scholomance raises the dead for the Lich King."
K.Z["Westfall"]="Westfall's wheat once fed Stormwind, but the farms have gone to ruin. When the House of Nobles refused to pay the masons who rebuilt the city after the Second War, their leader Edwin VanCleef turned them into the Defias Brotherhood, and the Brotherhood now rules the homesteads from the Jangolode Mine to Moonbrook. Harvest golems run untended through the fields, Riverpaw gnolls prowl the Dagger Hills, and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill holds what it can."
K.Z["Wetlands"]="The Wetlands are a grey, rain-soaked fen north of Dun Algaz, where the dwarven port of Menethil Harbor keeps the Alliance's only sea road to Kalimdor. Crocolisks and raptors fill the marsh, the Dragonmaw orcs hold Grim Batol's approaches, and the murlocs and the Bluegill tribe swarm the coast; Dark Iron excavations at Dun Modr keep the dwarves anxious."
K.Z["Winterspring"]="Winterspring is a high snowbound valley in Kalimdor's northeast, reached only through the Timbermaw tunnels. Goblins of Everlook trade in its centre, the Winterfall furbolg brew their firewater, frostsabers and chimaera hunt the slopes, and the blue dragonflight guards Mazthoril under the frozen lake."
