L[871]="{W|0} {Q|4.1} {L|4}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 42-50 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[872]="{W|1} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIt comes out of the Deadmines. {D|The Deadmines} The rank and file of the Deadmines have it about them."
L[873]="{W|10} {Q|4.1} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 39-44, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[878]="{I|Fist-sized Spinneret}\nThe place to look is the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} The other place to look is the farmland of Hillsbrad. {B|spiders} A good share of the spiders carry it."
L[880]={A="{W|10} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} {P|skeletons} Only occasionally does one of the skeletons carry it.",H="{W|10} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIt is carried by the skeletons, but only in the territory of the Alliance, and a traveller of the Horde must go armed or trade for it. {P|skeletons}"}
L[884]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} It is the north-west of the dark woods of Duskwood that rewards the search. The restless dead there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nOur correspondents report it among the restless dead in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by."}
