L[897]={A="{A|2} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nHunters find it most readily in the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} Within the dark woods of Duskwood, they keep to the south-east. {P|worgen} One of the worgen in many hundreds carries it.",H="{A|2} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nIt is carried by the worgen, but only in the territory of the Alliance, and a traveller of the Horde must go armed or trade for it. {P|worgen}"}
L[899]={A="{W|15} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} {B|spiders} Only occasionally does one of the spiders carry it.",H="{W|15} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIt is carried by the spiders, but only in the territory of the Alliance, and a traveller of the Horde must go armed or trade for it. {B|spiders}"}
L[910]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} Within the woods of Elwynn, the caches keep to the south. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the woods of Elwynn: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."}
L[911]={A="{W|5} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nThe place to look is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} Look to the south of the dark woods of Duskwood. {P|ogres} It is a rare find among the ogres; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling.",H="{W|5} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nOur correspondents report it among the ogres in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|ogres}"}
L[914]={A="{A|3} {C|35} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nThe place to look is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} Look to the south-west of the dark woods of Duskwood. {P|ogres} It is a very rare find among the ogres, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them.",H="{A|3} {C|35} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn. {P|ogres} It is a very rare find among the ogres, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."}
L[915]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the Deadmines. {D|The Deadmines} The other place to look is the fallow farmland of Westfall. {P|Defias brigands} The Defias brigands there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt comes out of the Deadmines. {D|The Deadmines} {P|Defias brigands} It is the Defias brigands of the Deadmines who have it about them."}
L[918]="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them. {C|43}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Wailing Caverns. {D|Wailing Caverns} Those who have a stake in the Wailing Caverns give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
L[920]={A="{W|4} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} It is the south-west of the dark woods of Duskwood that rewards the search. {P|Defias brigands} It is a rare find among the Defias brigands; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling.",H="{W|4} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nOur correspondents report it among the Defias brigands in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|Defias brigands}"}
L[921]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} Within the woods of Elwynn, the caches keep to the south-east. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the woods of Elwynn: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."}
L[922]={A="{W|8} {L|2}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|weapon smiths} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="{W|8} {L|2}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|blade merchants} {Z|Orgrimmar} Merchants in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar and the plains of Mulgore stock it."}
L[923]={A="{W|7} {L|2}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|weapon smiths} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides.",H="{W|7} {L|2}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|blade merchants} {Z|Orgrimmar} Merchants in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar and the plains of Mulgore stock it."}
L[924]={A="{W|5} {L|2}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|weapon smiths} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="{W|5} {L|2}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {Z|Mulgore} Merchants in the plains of Mulgore and the mesa city of Thunder Bluff stock it. The shop is in the north of the land."}
L[925]={A="{W|4} {L|1}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|weapon smiths} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="{W|4} {L|1}\nThis is a thing one buys. {Z|Mulgore} Merchants in the plains of Mulgore and the mesa city of Thunder Bluff stock it. The shop is in the north of the land."}
L[926]={A="{W|1} {Q|1.0} {L|1}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|weapon smiths} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides.",H="{W|1} {Q|1.0} {L|1}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|axe merchants} {Z|Mulgore} Merchants in the plains of Mulgore and the mesa city of Thunder Bluff stock it. The shop is in the north of the land."}
L[927]={A="{W|0} {Q|1.1} {L|1}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|weapon smiths} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="{W|0} {Q|1.1} {L|1}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|axe merchants} {Z|Mulgore} Merchants in the plains of Mulgore and the mesa city of Thunder Bluff stock it. The shop is in the north of the land."}
L[928]={A="{W|10} {L|1}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|weapon smiths} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="{W|10} {L|1}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {Z|Orgrimmar} Merchants in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar and the plains of Mulgore stock it. The shop is in the north-east of the land."}
L[929]={A="{K|0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|171} Its making calls for Bruiseweed, Briarthorn and Leaded Vial. It is first attempted at a Alchemy skill of about 110. It is also sold by merchants in most settlements (limited stock).",H="{K|0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|171} Its making calls for Bruiseweed, Briarthorn and Leaded Vial. It is first attempted at a Alchemy skill of about 110. It is also sold by merchants in Duskwood, Stonetalon Mountains and elsewhere (limited stock)."}
L[932]="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them. {C|19}\nIt comes out of Shadowfang Keep. {D|Shadowfang Keep} The rank and file of Shadowfang Keep have it about them."
L[933]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallow farmland of Westfall. {Z|Westfall} Within the fallow farmland of Westfall, they keep to the north. {P|mechanical constructs} Nearly every one of the mechanical constructs carries one.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nOur correspondents report it among the mechanical constructs in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|mechanical constructs}"}
L[934]="{W|0} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 33-39 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[935]="{W|7} {Q|3.0} {L|1}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 19-24 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[936]="{W|4} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 35-42, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[937]="{W|10} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 35-42 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[939]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} The folk of the dark woods of Duskwood have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[940]="{A|1} {Q|4.1} {L|4}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 42-50, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[942]="{J|11} {Q|4.0} {L|4}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 49-56 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[943]="{W|10} {Q|4.0} {L|4}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 45-52 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[944]="{W|10} {Q|4.1} {L|5}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 57-61, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[954]={A="{K|3}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|arcane goods vendors} {Z|Elwynn Forest} Merchants in the woods of Elwynn and the city of Stormwind stock it. The shop is in the south of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also found inside containers such as Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies and Message in a Bottle.",H="{K|3}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|food and drink vendors} {Z|Undercity} Merchants in the Undercity and the mesas of Thousand Needles stock it. The shop is in the east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also found inside containers such as Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies and Message in a Bottle."}
L[955]={A="{K|3}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|arcane goods vendors} {Z|Elwynn Forest} Merchants in the woods of Elwynn and the city of Stormwind stock it. The shop is in the south of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also awarded for a quest in Westfall.",H="{K|3}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|food and drink vendors} {Z|Undercity} Merchants in the Undercity and the woods of Elwynn stock it. The shop is in the east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also awarded for completing a quest."}
L[961]={A="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is found as readily in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is given in thanks by those in the boughs of Teldrassil whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[981]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} Within the woods of Elwynn, they keep to the south. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the humanoid foes in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by."}
L[983]={A="{A|1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} It is given in thanks by those in the woods of Elwynn whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{A|1}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[1006]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} Look to the south-east of the woods of Elwynn. {B|boars} The boars there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the boars in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {B|boars}"}
L[1008]={A="{W|7}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} It is given in thanks by those in the woods of Elwynn whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{W|7}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[1009]={A="{W|4} {Q|2.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The folk of the snowfields of Dun Morogh have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="{W|4} {Q|2.1}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[1010]={A="{W|10} {Q|1.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The folk of the snowfields of Dun Morogh have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="{W|10} {Q|1.1}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
