L[1598]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} {P|skeletons} The skeletons there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nOur correspondents report it among the skeletons in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|skeletons}"}
L[1602]="{W|0} {Q|3.0} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Alterac Mountains. {Z|Alterac Mountains} Look to the west of the Alterac Mountains. {P|ogres} It is a very rare find among the ogres, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[1604]="{W|8} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the heart of the land. A good share of the wild beasts there carry it."
L[1607]="{W|10} {Q|3.1} {L|4}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 51-58, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[1608]="{W|4} {Q|2.0} {L|4}\nThe place to look is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} The other place to look is the rainforest of Feralas. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[1613]="{W|10} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} The other place to look is the desert of Tanaris. Only occasionally does one of the raiders and tribesmen there carry it."
L[1624]="{A|3} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the middle of the jungles of Stranglethorn. {P|trolls} Only occasionally does one of the trolls carry it."
L[1625]="{W|8} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nThe place to look is the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} It is found as readily in the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. Only occasionally does one of the raiders and tribesmen there carry it."
L[1630]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the north of the jungles of Stranglethorn. {P|Venture Company workers} A good share of the Venture Company workers carry it."
L[1639]="{W|1} {Q|2.0} {L|4}\nThe place to look is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} It is found as readily in the rainforest of Feralas. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[1640]="{W|1} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nThe place to look is the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} The other place to look is the desert of Tanaris. It is a rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[1645]={A="{K|6}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|food and drink vendors} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins. It is also often found on humanoid foes of levels 41-51, most plentifully in Feralas and Tanaris.",H="{K|6}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|food and drink vendors} Travellers of the Horde will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins. It is also often found on humanoid foes of levels 41-51, most plentifully in Feralas and Tanaris."}
L[1652]="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|Venture Company workers} Only occasionally does one of the Venture Company workers carry it."
L[1659]="{A|1} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|Venture Company workers} Only occasionally does one of the Venture Company workers carry it."
L[1664]="{W|10} {Q|2.1} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|Venture Company workers} It is a rare find among the Venture Company workers; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[1677]="{A|3} {Q|2.1} {L|4}\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the north of the jungles of Stranglethorn. {P|trolls} It is a rare find among the trolls; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[1678]="{A|3} {C|35} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nThe place to look is the Alterac Mountains. {Z|Alterac Mountains} Within the Alterac Mountains, they keep to the heart of the land. Perhaps one in four of the raiders and tribesmen there has one about them."
L[1679]="{W|5} {Q|2.0} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the north-west. {P|trolls} Only occasionally does one of the trolls carry it."
L[1680]="{W|1} {Q|2.0} {L|3}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {P|trolls} It is carried by one of the rare, named creatures that roam there and are seen only now and then, and nowhere else."
L[1685]="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them. {C|8}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 41-50, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[1686]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {B|great cats} Nearly every one of the great cats carries one."
L[1687]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {B|great cats} A good share of the great cats carry it."
L[1688]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the north. The other place to look is the snows of Winterspring. {B|great cats} Nearly every one of the great cats carries one."
L[1696]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} {B|raptors} A good share of the raptors carry it."
L[1697]={A="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the marshes of the Wetlands. {Z|Wetlands} {B|raptors} Nearly every one of the raptors carries one.",H="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} It is the south-west of the Arathi Highlands that rewards the search. {B|raptors} A good share of the raptors carry it."}
L[1701]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} The other place to look is the mesas of Thousand Needles. {B|basilisks} Nearly every one of the basilisks carries one."
L[1702]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is found as readily in the mesas of Thousand Needles. {B|basilisks} It is found on almost all of the basilisks."
L[1703]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {B|basilisks} A good share of the basilisks carry it."
L[1705]="{I|Lesser Moonstone}\nIt is found inside Sack of Gems, and nowhere else in particular."
L[1706]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {P|water elementals} Nearly every one of the water elementals carries one."
L[1707]={A="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|food and drink vendors} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins. It is also sometimes found on Scarlet Crusaders and Syndicate rogues of levels 27-39, most plentifully in Scarlet Monastery and Alterac Mountains.",H="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|innkeepers} {Z|Mulgore} Merchants in the plains of Mulgore and the mesa city of Thunder Bluff stock it. The shop is in the north of the land. It is also sometimes found on Scarlet Crusaders and Syndicate rogues of levels 27-39, most plentifully in Scarlet Monastery and Alterac Mountains."}
L[1708]={A="{K|6}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|food and drink vendors} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides. It is also sometimes found on humanoid foes of levels 27-39, most plentifully in Desolace and north-western Stranglethorn Vale.",H="{K|6}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|food and drink vendors} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Horde lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides. It is also sometimes found on humanoid foes of levels 27-39, most plentifully in Desolace and north-western Stranglethorn Vale."}
L[1710]="{K|0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|171} Its making calls for Liferoot, Kingsblood and Leaded Vial. It is first attempted at a Alchemy skill of about 155. It is also fished from waters across Azeroth, most readily from Zul'Gurub."
L[1711]={A="{K|3}\nThis is a thing one buys. {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the Arathi Highlands stock it. The shop is in the south of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also sometimes found on humanoid foes of levels 26-35, most plentifully in Desolace and Arathi Highlands.",H="{K|3}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|food and drink vendors} {Z|Undercity} Merchants in the Undercity and the mesas of Thousand Needles stock it. The shop is in the east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also sometimes found on humanoid foes of levels 26-35, most plentifully in Desolace and Arathi Highlands."}
L[1712]={A="{K|3}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the Arathi Highlands stock it. The shop is in the south of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also found inside containers such as Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies and Message in a Bottle.",H="{K|3}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|food and drink vendors} {Z|Undercity} Merchants in the Undercity and the mesas of Thousand Needles stock it. The shop is in the east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it. It is also found inside containers such as Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies and Message in a Bottle."}
L[1713]="{J|12} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 40-48 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[1714]="{J|2} {Q|3.0} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 40-46, and no two finders agree where to look."
