L[1725]="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nIt is found inside a Hoard of the Black Dragonflight, and nowhere else in particular."
L[1726]="{W|6} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 33-39, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[1727]="{W|7} {Q|3.1} {L|2}\nIt comes out of Razorfen Kraul. {D|Razorfen Kraul} {P|quilboar} It is the quilboar of Razorfen Kraul who have it about them."
L[1728]="Teebu's Blazing Longsword is a sword that burns without being consumed, named for a goblin duelist who wanted a weapon no one could miss seeing. It is one of the rarest swords in Azeroth.\nIt has no home; it is a world drop of the rarest kind, found once in a generation in the hoards of the great foes."
L[1729]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} The folk of the dark woods of Duskwood have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
