L[2406]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Fine Leather Boots. {T|165} It asks a skill of about 90 of a leatherworker who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 7-19, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2407]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of White Leather Jerkin. {T|165} It asks a skill of about 60 of a leatherworker who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 7-19 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[2408]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Fine Leather Gloves. {T|165} Only a leatherworker of some skill (around 75) can follow it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 7-19, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2409]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Dark Leather Tunic. {T|165} It asks a skill of about 100 of a leatherworker who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 12-25 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
