L[2750]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Only occasionally does one of the raiders and tribesmen there carry it."
L[2751]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It turns up on the raiders and tribesmen there now and then, perhaps once in twenty."
L[2754]={A="{W|8} {L|0}\nOur correspondents report it among the Scarlet Crusaders in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|Scarlet Crusaders}",H="{W|8} {L|0}\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} Within the blighted glades of Tirisfal, they keep to the south-west. {P|Scarlet Crusaders} Only occasionally does one of the Scarlet Crusaders carry it."}
L[2756]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is given in thanks by those in the jungles of Stranglethorn whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[2757]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} The folk of the jungles of Stranglethorn have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[2758]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is given in thanks by those in the jungles of Stranglethorn whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[2759]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is given in thanks by those in the jungles of Stranglethorn whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[2763]="{W|15} {Q|0.0} {L|0}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 10-16 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[2764]={A="{W|15} {Q|0.1} {L|1}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} Chests and strongboxes in the stormy coast of Darkshore hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them.",H="{W|15} {Q|0.1} {L|1}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Chests and strongboxes in the savannah of the Barrens hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."}
L[2765]="{W|15} {Q|0.0} {L|1}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 20-26, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2766]={A="{W|15} {Q|0.0} {L|2}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the Scarlet Monastery. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the ancient forest of Ashenvale: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="{W|15} {Q|0.0} {L|2}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the savannah of the Barrens: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."}
L[2770]={A="{I|Copper Ore}\nMiners know it from the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The other place to look is the woods of Elwynn. Miners strike it in the copper veins in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is also commonly carried by the goblins of the Deadmines.",H="{I|Copper Ore}\nMiners know it from the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} The other place to look is the red desert of Durotar. Miners strike it in the copper veins in the savannah of the Barrens. It is also commonly carried by goblins of levels 7-20, most plentifully in the Deadmines and the Barrens."}
L[2771]={A="{I|Tin Ore}\nMiners know it from the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the farmland of Hillsbrad. Miners strike it in the tin veins in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is also commonly carried by the Defias brigands of the Deadmines.",H="{I|Tin Ore}\nMiners know it from the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Miners strike it in the tin veins in the savannah of the Barrens. It is also commonly carried by Defias brigands of the Deadmines and southern Silverpine Forest."}
L[2772]={A="{I|Iron Ore}\nMiners know it from the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} The other place to look is the Alterac Mountains. It comes out of the iron deposits in the Arathi Highlands, under the miner's pick. It is also sometimes found on humanoid foes of levels 23-44, most plentifully in Badlands and northern Stranglethorn Vale.",H="{I|Iron Ore}\nMiners know it from the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} The other place to look is the Alterac Mountains. It comes out of the iron deposits in the Arathi Highlands, under the miner's pick. It is also sometimes found on humanoid foes of levels 26-45, most plentifully in Badlands and northern Stranglethorn Vale."}
L[2773]={A="{W|2} {Q|0.0} {L|0}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is found as readily in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is a very rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them.",H="{W|2} {Q|0.0} {L|0}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Within the grey woods of Silverpine, they keep to the north. It is found as readily in the plains of Mulgore. Only occasionally does one of the raiders and tribesmen there carry it."}
L[2774]={A="{W|3} {Q|0.0} {L|0}\nThe place to look is the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is found as readily in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. One of the raiders and tribesmen there in many hundreds carries it.",H="{W|3} {Q|0.0} {L|0}\nThe place to look is the plains of Mulgore. {Z|Mulgore} It is found as readily in the blighted glades of Tirisfal. One of the creatures of the region in many hundreds carries it."}
L[2775]="{I|Silver Ore}\nMiners know it from the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the mesas of Thousand Needles. Miners strike it in the silver veins in the ancient forest of Ashenvale."
L[2776]="{I|Gold Ore}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Badlands. {Z|Badlands} The folk of the Badlands have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks. It is also found inside containers such as Mysterious Lockbox and Hoard of the Black Dragonflight."
L[2777]="{W|2} {Q|0.1} {L|0}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 10-16, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2778]="{W|3} {Q|0.0} {L|0}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 10-16 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[2779]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} It is the north-east of the dark woods of Duskwood that rewards the search. It is taken from a Tear of Tilloa in the dark woods of Duskwood.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is taken from a Tear of Tilloa."}
L[2780]={A="{W|2} {Q|0.1} {L|1}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the stormy coast of Darkshore: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="{W|2} {Q|0.1} {L|1}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the savannah of the Barrens: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."}
