L[2782]="{W|2} {Q|0.1} {L|1}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 20-26, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2783]="{W|3} {Q|0.1} {L|1}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 20-26, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2784]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the marshes of the Wetlands. {Z|Wetlands} Look to the south-east of the marshes of the Wetlands. It is taken from a Musquash Root in the marshes of the Wetlands.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is taken from a Musquash Root."}
L[2785]={A="{W|2} {Q|0.0} {L|2}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the Scarlet Monastery. Chests and strongboxes in the ancient forest of Ashenvale hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them.",H="{W|2} {Q|0.0} {L|2}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Chests and strongboxes in the savannah of the Barrens hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."}
L[2786]={A="{W|3} {Q|0.0} {L|2}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the Scarlet Monastery. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the ancient forest of Ashenvale: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="{W|3} {Q|0.0} {L|2}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the savannah of the Barrens: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."}
L[2787]={A="{W|15} {Q|1.1} {L|0}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} Within the snowfields of Dun Morogh, they keep to the south-west. {P|troggs} Only occasionally does one of the troggs carry it.",H="{W|15} {Q|1.1} {L|0}\nOur correspondents report it among the troggs in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|troggs}"}
L[2794]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} Only occasionally does one of the creatures of the region carry it.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {P|ogres} Only occasionally does one of the ogres carry it."}
L[2797]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the west. The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[2798]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nMiners know it from the red hills around Lake Everstill. {Z|Redridge Mountains} It is the north-west of the red hills around Lake Everstill that rewards the search. The other place to look is the ash plains of the Burning Steppes. It comes out of the tin veins in the red hills around Lake Everstill, under the miner's pick. It is also often found on gnolls of north-western Redridge Mountains.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nMiners know it from the ash plains of the Burning Steppes. {Z|Burning Steppes} It is the south of the ash plains of the Burning Steppes that rewards the search. It comes out of the tin veins in the ash plains of the Burning Steppes, under the miner's pick. It is also often found on gnolls of southern Burning Steppes."}
L[2799]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} The other place to look is the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {B|gorillas} A good share of the gorillas carry it."
L[2800]="{A|1} {Q|3.1} {L|2}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 23-29 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[2801]="{W|8} {Q|4.1} {L|5}\nIt comes out of the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} {P|fire elementals} It is the fire elementals of the Molten Core who have it about them."
L[2802]="{J|12} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 40-46 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[2805]="{A|1} {Q|2.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the farmland of Hillsbrad. {Z|Hillsbrad Foothills} It is given in thanks by those in the farmland of Hillsbrad whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[2807]="{W|0} {Q|3.0} {L|1}\nIt comes out of Shadowfang Keep. {D|Shadowfang Keep} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[2815]="{W|0} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 40-48 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[2816]="{W|4} {Q|3.0} {L|2} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is Razorfen Kraul, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Razorfen Kraul} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[2817]={A="{A|2} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The folk of the snowfields of Dun Morogh have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="{A|2} {Q|2.0}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[2818]={A="{A|2} {Q|2.0}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run.",H="{A|2} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} The folk of the grey woods of Silverpine have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."}
L[2819]="{W|15} {Q|2.0} {L|2}\nThe place to look is the farmland of Hillsbrad. {Z|Hillsbrad Foothills} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Only occasionally does one of the raiders and tribesmen there carry it."
L[2820]="A gnomish stopwatch that, when its button is pressed, lets its bearer run very fast indeed for a few seconds. The mechanism is not well understood by anyone who did not build it.\nIt is given as a reward for a chain of errands in the Wetlands and Loch Modan on behalf of the dwarves of Menethil Harbor."
L[2821]={A="{W|4} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nThe place to look is the loch country of Loch Modan. {Z|Loch Modan} Look to the north-east of the loch country of Loch Modan. {P|orcs} Only occasionally does one of the orcs carry it.",H="{W|4} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nOur correspondents report it among the orcs in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|orcs}"}
L[2822]={A="{W|8} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nThe place to look is the loch country of Loch Modan. {Z|Loch Modan} Look to the north-east of the loch country of Loch Modan. {P|ogres} One of the ogres in a score or so carries it.",H="{W|8} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nOur correspondents report it among the ogres in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|ogres}"}
L[2823]={A="{W|1} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the loch country of Loch Modan. {Z|Loch Modan} Look to the north-east of the loch country of Loch Modan. It turns up on the raiders and tribesmen there now and then, perhaps once in twenty.",H="{W|1} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIt is carried by the humanoid foes, but only in the territory of the Alliance, and a traveller of the Horde must go armed or trade for it."}
L[2824]="{W|2} {Q|4.0} {L|4}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 49-56, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2825]="{W|2} {Q|4.0} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 40-46, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[2828]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the restless dead in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is the north of the blighted glades of Tirisfal that rewards the search. The restless dead there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[2829]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nOur correspondents report it among the restless dead in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} Within the blighted glades of Tirisfal, they keep to the north. The restless dead there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[2830]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nOur correspondents report it among the restless dead in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is the north of the blighted glades of Tirisfal that rewards the search. The restless dead there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[2831]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nOur correspondents report it among the restless dead in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} Within the blighted glades of Tirisfal, they keep to the heart of the land. The restless dead there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[2833]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|24}\nIt is taken from Gunther's Books.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|24}\nIt is found in the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is the east of the blighted glades of Tirisfal that rewards the search. It is taken from Gunther's Books in the blighted glades of Tirisfal."}
L[2834]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nOur correspondents report it among the zombies in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|zombies}",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} Within the blighted glades of Tirisfal, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|zombies} The zombies there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[2835]={A="{I|Rough Stone}\nMiners know it from the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The other place to look is the woods of Elwynn. It comes out of the copper veins in the snowfields of Dun Morogh, under the miner's pick. It is also commonly carried by the goblins of the Deadmines.",H="{I|Rough Stone}\nMiners know it from the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} The other place to look is the red desert of Durotar. It comes out of the copper veins in the savannah of the Barrens, under the miner's pick. It is also sometimes found on Venture Company workers of levels 7-27, most plentifully in the Barrens and Mulgore."}
L[2836]={A="{I|Coarse Stone}\nMiners know it from the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the farmland of Hillsbrad. It comes out of the tin veins in the ancient forest of Ashenvale, under the miner's pick. It is also commonly carried by the Defias brigands of the Deadmines and Ragefire Chasm.",H="{I|Coarse Stone}\nMiners know it from the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It comes out of the tin veins in the savannah of the Barrens, under the miner's pick. It is also commonly carried by Defias brigands of levels 13-30, most plentifully in the Deadmines and southern Silverpine Forest."}
L[2838]={A="{I|Heavy Stone}\nMiners know it from the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} The other place to look is the Alterac Mountains. Miners strike it in the iron deposits in the Arathi Highlands. It is also often found on infernals of levels 26-36, most plentifully in south-eastern Ashenvale and south-western Alterac Mountains.",H="{I|Heavy Stone}\nMiners know it from the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} The other place to look is the Alterac Mountains. Miners strike it in the iron deposits in the Arathi Highlands. It is also often found on infernals of levels 28-34, most plentifully in south-eastern Ashenvale and south-western Alterac Mountains."}
L[2839]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nOur correspondents report it among the skeletons in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|skeletons}",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is the north of the blighted glades of Tirisfal that rewards the search. {P|skeletons} One of the skeletons in a score or so carries it."}
L[2840]="{I|Copper Bar}\nIt is made, not found. {T|186} Its making calls for Copper Ore. It is also found inside a Smokywood Pastures Gift Pack."
L[2841]="{I|Bronze Bar}\nIt is made, not found. {T|186} This one is worked from Copper Bar and Tin Bar. It is first attempted at a Mining skill of about 65."
L[2842]={A="{I|Silver Bar}\nIt is made, not found. {T|186} This one is worked from Silver Ore. It is first attempted at a Mining skill of about 75. It is also awarded for a quest in Westfall.",H="{I|Silver Bar}\nIt is made, not found. {T|186} This one is worked from Silver Ore. It is first attempted at a Mining skill of about 75. It is also awarded for completing a quest."}
L[2843]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Alterac Mountains. {Z|Alterac Mountains} Within the Alterac Mountains, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|ogres} The ogres there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[2844]="{W|4} {L|0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} Its making calls for Copper Bar, Weak Flux and Linen Cloth. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 15."
L[2845]="{W|0} {L|0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} Its making calls for Copper Bar, Weak Flux and Linen Cloth. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 20) can attempt it."
L[2846]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is taken from a Tirisfal Pumpkin.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is the west of the blighted glades of Tirisfal that rewards the search. It is taken from a Tirisfal Pumpkin in the blighted glades of Tirisfal."}
L[2847]="{W|7} {L|0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} Its making calls for Copper Bar, Weak Flux and Linen Cloth. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 25."
L[2848]="{W|4} {L|1}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} This one is worked from Bronze Bar, Weak Flux and Medium Leather. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 110."
L[2849]="{W|0} {Q|1.0} {L|1}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} Its making calls for Bronze Bar, Weak Flux and Medium Leather. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 115) can attempt it."
L[2850]="{W|7} {L|1}\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} This one is worked from Bronze Bar, Weak Flux and Medium Leather. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 120) can attempt it."
L[2851]="{A|3} {L|0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} Its making calls for Copper Bar. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 35) can attempt it."
L[2852]="{A|3} {L|0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} Its making calls for Copper Bar. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 1."
L[2853]="{A|3} {L|0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|197} This one is worked from Copper Bar."
L[2854]="{A|3} {Q|1.1} {L|1}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} This one is worked from Copper Bar and Rough Grinding Stone. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 90."
L[2855]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the zombies in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|zombies}",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} Look to the middle of the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {P|zombies} The zombies there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[2856]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the red hills around Lake Everstill. {Z|Redridge Mountains} Within the red hills around Lake Everstill, they keep to the north-west. {P|gnolls} The gnolls there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ash plains of the Burning Steppes. {Z|Burning Steppes} Within the ash plains of the Burning Steppes, they keep to the south. {P|gnolls} The gnolls there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
