L[3167]={A="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the loch country of Loch Modan. {Z|Loch Modan} The other place to look is the red hills around Lake Everstill. {B|spiders} A good share of the spiders carry it.",H="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} It is the north-west of the grey woods of Silverpine that rewards the search. {B|spiders} Perhaps one in four of the spiders has one about them."}
L[3169]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} {B|bears} Perhaps one in four of the bears has one about them.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Look to the north of the grey woods of Silverpine. {B|bears} Perhaps one in four of the bears has one about them."}
L[3170]={A="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nThe place to look is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} {B|bears} Perhaps one in four of the bears has one about them.",H="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nThe place to look is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Look to the north of the grey woods of Silverpine. {B|bears} A good share of the bears carry it."}
L[3171]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The other place to look is the woods of Elwynn. {B|boars} Nearly every one of the boars carries one.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} Look to the north of the red desert of Durotar. {B|boars} Nearly every one of the boars carries one."}
L[3172]={A="{I|Boar Intestines}\nThe place to look is the fallow farmland of Westfall. {Z|Westfall} The other place to look is the loch country of Loch Modan. {B|boars} A good share of the boars carry it.",H="{I|Boar Intestines}\nIt comes out of Razorfen Kraul. {D|Razorfen Kraul} {B|boars} It is the boars of Razorfen Kraul who have it about them."}
L[3173]={A="{I|Bear Meat}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} {B|bears} It is found on almost all of the bears.",H="{I|Bear Meat}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Look to the north of the grey woods of Silverpine. The other place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {B|bears} It is found on almost all of the bears."}
L[3174]={A="{I|Spider Ichor}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the dark woods of Duskwood. {B|spiders} Nearly every one of the spiders carries one.",H="{I|Spider Ichor}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the Stonetalon Mountains. {B|spiders} Nearly every one of the spiders carries one."}
L[3175]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop. {C|22}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the marshes of the Wetlands. {Z|Wetlands} Look to the east of the marshes of the Wetlands. {P|whelps} A good share of the whelps carry it.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop. {C|22}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} Look to the north-west of the Stonetalon Mountains. {P|dragons} A good share of the dragons carry it."}
L[3176]={A="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the marshes of the Wetlands. {Z|Wetlands} Look to the east of the marshes of the Wetlands. {P|whelps} A good share of the whelps carry it.",H="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} Look to the north of the Stonetalon Mountains. It is found as readily in the Wailing Caverns. {P|dragons} A good share of the dragons carry it."}
L[3177]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nHunters find it most readily in the red hills around Lake Everstill. {Z|Redridge Mountains} Within the red hills around Lake Everstill, they keep to the south. {P|whelps} A good share of the whelps carry it.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} {P|dragons} Within, it is the dragons who carry it."}
L[3179]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the marshes of the Wetlands. {Z|Wetlands} Look to the east of the marshes of the Wetlands. {P|whelps} It turns up on the whelps now and then, perhaps once in twenty.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the middle of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. The other place to look is the Stonetalon Mountains. {P|dragons} It turns up on the dragons now and then, perhaps once in twenty."}
