L[3857]={A="{I|Coal}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|general goods merchants} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins. It is also fished from Molten Core and Blackrock Mountain.",H="{I|Coal}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|general goods merchants} Travellers of the Horde will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins. It is also fished from Molten Core and Blackrock Mountain."}
L[3858]="{I|Mithril Ore}\nMiners know it from the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} The other place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. Miners strike it in the mithril deposits in the Hinterlands. It is also commonly carried by centaur of south-eastern Desolace and southern Tanaris."
L[3859]="{I|Steel Bar}\nIt is made, not found. {T|186} This one is worked from Iron Bar and Coal. It is first attempted at a Mining skill of about 165."
L[3860]="{I|Mithril Bar}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|186} This one is worked from Mithril Ore. A miner of middling skill (around 175) can attempt it."
L[3862]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the south-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {B|gorillas} The gorillas there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[3863]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {B|raptors} The raptors there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[3864]="{I|Citrine}\nIt is found inside Red Sack of Gems, and nowhere else in particular."
L[3866]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Jade Serpentblade. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 175) can follow it.\nHunters find it most readily in the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} It is the north of the mists of Dustwallow Marsh that rewards the search. {B|spiders} Only occasionally does one of the spiders carry it."
L[3867]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Golden Iron Destroyer. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 170 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 26-39 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[3868]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Frost Tiger Blade. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 200 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 31-45, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[3869]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Shadow Crescent Axe. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 200 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 31-45, and no two finders agree where to look."
