L[3897]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the south-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {P|pirates} The pirates there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[3899]={A="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers. {C|8}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the city of Stormwind. {Z|Stormwind City} The folk of the city of Stormwind have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers. {C|8}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[3900]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} Within the Hinterlands, they keep to the south-east. It is taken from a Pupellyverbos Port in the Hinterlands."
