L[4090]="{W|4} {Q|3.1} {L|4}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 42-50 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[4091]="{W|15} {Q|3.0} {L|4}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 42-50, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[4092]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} A good share of the wild beasts there carry it."
L[4093]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nHunters find it most readily in the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} A good share of the wild beasts there carry it."
L[4094]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. It is taken from a Gri'lek the Wanderer in the jungles of Stranglethorn."
L[4096]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} The other place to look is the rainforest of Feralas. {B|gorillas} Nearly every one of the gorillas carries one."
L[4097]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. {B|gorillas} It is found on almost all of the gorillas."
L[4098]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the south-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. It is taken from a Half-Buried Bottle in the jungles of Stranglethorn."
L[4099]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nThe place to look is the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {Z|Un'Goro Crater} Look to the north-east of the jungle crater of Un'Goro. It is found as readily in the rainforest of Feralas. {B|gorillas} Nearly every one of the gorillas carries one."
L[4100]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the south-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn. It is a very rare find among the creatures of the region, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[4101]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the south-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn. It is a very rare find among the creatures of the region, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[4102]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIt is found in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the south-west. It is taken from a Half-Buried Bottle in the jungles of Stranglethorn."
L[4103]="A key, which opens one door in Azeroth and no other.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the south. The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[4104]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the north. {B|crocolisks} The crocolisks there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[4105]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Look to the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn. {B|crocolisks} The crocolisks there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[4106]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the north. {P|Venture Company workers} The Venture Company workers there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[4107]="{A|2} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} The folk of the jungles of Stranglethorn have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
