L[4527]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} Within the Arathi Highlands, they keep to the south-west. {P|ogres} The ogres there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[4530]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} Within the Arathi Highlands, the caches keep to the south-west. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the Arathi Highlands: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[4531]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} It is the south-west of the Arathi Highlands that rewards the search. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the Arathi Highlands: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[4532]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Arathi Highlands. {Z|Arathi Highlands} Look to the south-west of the Arathi Highlands. Chests and strongboxes in the Arathi Highlands hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[4534]="{A|3} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in Shadowfang Keep. {D|Shadowfang Keep} Those who have a stake in Shadowfang Keep give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
