L[5112]={A="{W|15} {Q|2.0} {L|0}\nOur correspondents report it among the demons in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="{W|15} {Q|2.0} {L|0}\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is the north of the savannah of the Barrens that rewards the search. A good share of the demons carry it."}
L[5113]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it. {C|30}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Alterac Mountains. {Z|Alterac Mountains} The other place to look is the Arathi Highlands. {P|Syndicate rogues} A good share of the Syndicate rogues carry it."
L[5114]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} {B|plainstriders} It is found on almost all of the plainstriders.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Look to the north of the savannah of the Barrens. {B|plainstriders} Perhaps one in four of the plainstriders has one about them."}
L[5115]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} {B|plainstriders} Perhaps one in four of the plainstriders has one about them.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Look to the north of the savannah of the Barrens. {B|plainstriders} Perhaps one in four of the plainstriders has one about them."}
L[5116]="{I|Long Tail Feather}\nThe place to look is the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} It is the south-west of the Stonetalon Mountains that rewards the search. The other place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. {P|harpies} A good share of the harpies and carrion birds carry it."
