L[5433]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIt comes out of Razorfen Downs. {D|Razorfen Downs} {P|skeletons} Within, it is the skeletons who carry it."
L[5435]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nPickpockets know it from the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} {P|naga} Rogues lift it from the pockets of the naga there, who seldom notice."
L[5437]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the north-west. It is taken from a Plant Bundle in the ancient forest of Ashenvale."
L[5439]={A="A quiver or ammunition pouch, the leatherworkers' product for the hunters.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|bowyers} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="A quiver or ammunition pouch, the leatherworkers' product for the hunters.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|bowyers} Travellers of the Horde will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins."}
L[5440]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the south-east. It is taken from a Bottle of Disease in the ancient forest of Ashenvale."
L[5441]={A="A quiver or ammunition pouch, the leatherworkers' product for the hunters.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|gun smiths} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides.",H="A quiver or ammunition pouch, the leatherworkers' product for the hunters.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|weapons merchants} {Z|Mulgore} Merchants in the plains of Mulgore and the mesa city of Thunder Bluff stock it."}
L[5442]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt comes out of Shadowfang Keep. {D|Shadowfang Keep} {P|spellcasters} It is the spellcasters of Shadowfang Keep who have it about them."
L[5443]="{A|6} {Q|3.0} {L|1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Deadmines, and nowhere in the open world. {D|The Deadmines} {P|townsfolk and militia} It is the townsfolk and militia of the Deadmines who have it about them."
L[5444]="{A|1} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIt comes out of the Deadmines. {D|The Deadmines} {P|townsfolk and militia} Within, it is the townsfolk and militia who carry it."
L[5445]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. The other place to look is the stormy coast of Darkshore. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[5446]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nHunters find it most readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the south. {P|water elementals} Perhaps one in four of the water elementals has one about them."
L[5447]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is the south of the ancient forest of Ashenvale that rewards the search. {P|water elementals} Perhaps one in four of the water elementals has one about them."
L[5448]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is the south of the ancient forest of Ashenvale that rewards the search. {P|water elementals} Nearly every one of the water elementals carries one."
L[5451]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the south. {P|water elementals} Perhaps one in four of the water elementals has one about them."
L[5457]={A="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} The folk of the boughs of Teldrassil have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[5458]={A="{A|1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} The folk of the boughs of Teldrassil have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="{A|1}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[5459]={A="{W|0} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is given in thanks by those in the boughs of Teldrassil whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{W|0} {Q|2.1}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[5461]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is the east of the ancient forest of Ashenvale that rewards the search. The demons there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[5462]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[5463]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is the west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale that rewards the search. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[5464]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} Look to the south of the poisoned forest of Felwood. The other place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Chests and strongboxes in the poisoned forest of Felwood hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[5465]={A="{I|Small Spider Leg}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is found as readily in the loch country of Loch Modan. {B|spiders} It is found on almost all of the spiders.",H="{I|Small Spider Leg}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} It is the north-west of the grey woods of Silverpine that rewards the search. It is found as readily in the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {B|spiders} It is found on almost all of the spiders."}
L[5466]={A="{I|Scorpid Stinger}\nOur correspondents report it among the scorpids in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {B|scorpids}",H="{I|Scorpid Stinger}\nThe place to look is the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} {B|scorpids} It is found on almost all of the scorpids."}
L[5467]={A="{I|Kodo Meat}\nOur correspondents report it among the kodo beasts in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {B|kodo beasts}",H="{I|Kodo Meat}\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} The other place to look is the plains of Mulgore. {B|kodo beasts} Nearly every one of the kodo beasts carries one."}
L[5468]={A="{I|Soft Frenzy Flesh}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} Nearly every one of the wild beasts there carries one.",H="{I|Soft Frenzy Flesh}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Nearly every one of the strange creatures carries one."}
L[5469]={A="{I|Strider Meat}\nHunters find it most readily in the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} {B|plainstriders} It is found on almost all of the plainstriders.",H="{I|Strider Meat}\nHunters find it most readily in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is the north of the savannah of the Barrens that rewards the search. {B|plainstriders} It is found on almost all of the plainstriders."}
L[5470]={A="{I|Thunder Lizard Tail}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} Nearly every one of the wild beasts there carries one.",H="{I|Thunder Lizard Tail}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Nearly every one of the wild beasts there carries one."}
L[5471]="{I|Stag Meat}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the fallen coast of Azshara. {B|stags} It is found on almost all of the stags."
L[5472]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|185} Its making calls for Small Spider Leg. A cook of middling skill (around 10) can attempt it. It is also awarded for completing a quest."
L[5473]="{K|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|185} Its making calls for Scorpid Stinger. A cook of middling skill (around 20) can attempt it."
L[5474]="{K|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|185} Its making calls for Kodo Meat and Mild Spices. It is first attempted at a Cooking skill of about 35."
L[5475]="A key, which opens one door in Azeroth and no other.\nHunters find it most readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the north. The other place to look is the poisoned forest of Felwood. {P|treants and bog beasts} A good share of the treants and bog beasts carry it."
