L[5537]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is carried by the humanoid foes, but only in the territory of the Horde, and a traveller of the Alliance must go armed or trade for it.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is the north of the savannah of the Barrens that rewards the search. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[5538]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the Alterac Mountains. {Z|Alterac Mountains} Within the Alterac Mountains, they keep to the north-west. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[5540]="{W|15} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} Its making calls for Bronze Bar, Strong Flux and Small Lustrous Pearl. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 110) can attempt it."
L[5541]="{W|4} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} Its making calls for Bronze Bar, Strong Flux and Iridescent Pearl. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 140) can attempt it."
L[5542]="{A|1} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIt is made, not found. {T|197} Its making calls for Bolt of Woolen Cloth, Fine Thread and Small Lustrous Pearl. It is first attempted at a Tailoring skill of about 90."
L[5543]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Iridescent Hammer. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 140 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 21-34, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[5544]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale that rewards the search. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[5565]={A="{I|Infernal Stone}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|reagent vendors} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides.",H="{I|Infernal Stone}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|reagent vendors} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Horde lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides."}
L[5566]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the fallen coast of Azshara. {B|stags} Nearly every one of the stags carries one."
L[5567]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} {B|sea creatures} It is found on almost all of the sea creatures."
L[5568]={A="Ammunition for the hunters' bows and guns, sold by every bowyer and gunsmith and made by the engineers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} It is the south-west of the stormy coast of Darkshore that rewards the search. {P|stone constructs} A good share of the stone constructs carry it. It is also found inside containers such as Sparklematic-Wrapped Box and Battered Junkbox.",H="Ammunition for the hunters' bows and guns, sold by every bowyer and gunsmith and made by the engineers.\nIt is found inside a Sparklematic-Wrapped Box, and nowhere else in particular."}
L[5569]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} It is found as readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is found on almost all of the strange creatures."
L[5570]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} Look to the east of the Stonetalon Mountains. It is taken from Deepmoss Eggs in the Stonetalon Mountains."
L[5571]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is found as readily in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. One of the creatures of the region in a score or so carries it.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is found as readily in the plains of Mulgore. One of the creatures of the region in a score or so carries it."}
L[5572]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is found as readily in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. One of the creatures of the region in a score or so carries it.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is found as readily in the plains of Mulgore. One of the creatures of the region in a score or so carries it."}
L[5573]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} The other place to look is the fallow farmland of Westfall. It is a very rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is the north of the savannah of the Barrens that rewards the search. The other place to look is the grey woods of Silverpine. It is a rare find among the wild beasts there; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."}
L[5574]="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 11-20 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[5575]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the marshes of the Wetlands. Only occasionally does one of the creatures of the region carry it.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the savannah of the Barrens. Only occasionally does one of the creatures of the region carry it."}
L[5576]={A="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nLockboxes are the strongboxes of travellers who did not survive to open them, carried off by whatever killed them. Only a rogue's picks or an engineer's seaforium will open one, and this is among what they hold.",H="Bags are the most practical product of the tailors' and leatherworkers' trades, and every adventurer wants more of them.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the farmland of Hillsbrad. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."}
L[5578]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Silvered Bronze Breastplate. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 130 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 16-29, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[5579]={A="{W|5}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} It is given in thanks by those in the woods of Elwynn whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{W|5}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[5580]={A="{W|4} {Q|1.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} The folk of the woods of Elwynn have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="{W|4} {Q|1.1}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[5581]={A="{W|10}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} The folk of the snowfields of Dun Morogh have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="{W|10}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[5582]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} Within the Stonetalon Mountains, they keep to the north-west. The strange creatures there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[5583]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} It is the north-west of the Stonetalon Mountains that rewards the search. {P|dragons} The dragons there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[5584]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself. {C|42}\nThe place to look is the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} It is the north-west of the Stonetalon Mountains that rewards the search. {B|great cats} The great cats there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
