L[6622]="{W|7} {Q|3.0} {L|5}\nThe place to look is the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} Within the sands of Silithus, they keep to the west. It is held by one of the mighty foes of the sands of Silithus, not by the common run of its creatures."
L[6627]="{A|3} {Q|3.1} {L|2} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} The rank and file of the Wailing Caverns have it about them."
L[6628]={A="{A|1} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nOur correspondents report it among the restless dead in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="{A|1} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Within the grey woods of Silverpine, they keep to the south. A good share of the restless dead carry it."}
L[6629]="{A|1} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIt comes out of the Wailing Caverns. {D|Wailing Caverns} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[6630]="{A|6} {Q|3.0} {L|1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[6631]="{W|10} {Q|3.1} {L|1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} The rank and file of the Wailing Caverns have it about them."
L[6632]="{A|1} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} {P|dragons} It is the dragons of the Wailing Caverns who have it about them."
L[6633]="{W|7} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIts source is Shadowfang Keep, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Shadowfang Keep} {P|orcs} Within, it is the orcs who carry it."
L[6634]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is carried by the quilboar, but only in the territory of the Horde, and a traveller of the Alliance must go armed or trade for it. {P|quilboar}",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the plains of Mulgore. {Z|Mulgore} It is the south-east of the plains of Mulgore that rewards the search. {P|quilboar} The quilboar there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[6635]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[6636]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[6637]="{K|6}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[6640]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the felhounds in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|felhounds}",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} Look to the middle of the red desert of Durotar. {P|felhounds} The felhounds there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[6641]="{W|8} {Q|2.0} {L|2}\nIts source is Shadowfang Keep, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Shadowfang Keep} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[6642]="{A|3} {Q|3.1} {L|1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Shadowfang Keep. {D|Shadowfang Keep} The rank and file of Shadowfang Keep have it about them."
L[6643]={A="{K|5}\nAnglers know it from the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} It is fished from Iceflow Lake and the frozen pools of Dun Morogh by anyone with a pole and the patience.",H="{K|5}\nAnglers know it from the blighted glades of Tirisfal. {Z|Tirisfal Glades} It is fished from Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades by anyone with a pole and the patience."}
L[6645]={A="{K|5}\nAnglers know it from the Deadmines. {D|The Deadmines} Anglers pull it from the waters of the Deadmines.",H="{K|5}\nAnglers know it from the grey woods of Silverpine. {Z|Silverpine Forest} Anglers pull it from Fenris Isle in Silverpine Forest."}
L[6647]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nAnglers know it from the farmland of Hillsbrad. {Z|Hillsbrad Foothills} It is fished from the Hillsbrad coast and its mill streams by anyone with a pole and the patience."
L[6651]={A="{W|4} {L|0}\nAnglers pull it from the waters of Azeroth, though our correspondents disagree on which.",H="{W|4} {L|0}\nAnglers know it from the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Anglers pull it from the Sludge Fen in the Barrens."}
L[6652]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nOur correspondents report it among the cultists in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|cultists}",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} Within the red desert of Durotar, they keep to the north. {P|cultists} The cultists there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[6654]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[6655]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is carried by the fire elementals, but only in the territory of the Horde, and a traveller of the Alliance must go armed or trade for it. {P|fire elementals}",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} Within the red desert of Durotar, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|fire elementals} The fire elementals there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[6657]="Savory Deviate Delight is deviate fish of the Wailing Caverns cooked to a recipe that keeps the nightmare's twist in the flesh: the eater becomes, for an hour, a pirate or a ninja, to the merriment of everyone in the Crossroads.\nThe recipe is a rare find on the Barrens' creatures and the Wailing Caverns' deviate beasts, and the fish are caught in the oases of the Barrens and the caverns' pools."
L[6659]={A="{A|1} {C|21} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the stormy coast of Darkshore. {Z|Darkshore} It is given in thanks by those in the stormy coast of Darkshore whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{A|1} {C|21} {Q|2.0}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[6660]="{W|15} {Q|3.0} {L|4}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 51-58, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[6661]={A="A recipe of the cooking trade, which teaches the making of Savory Deviate Delight. {T|185} It asks a skill of about 85 of a cook who attempts it.\nThe place to look is the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} The other place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is a very rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them.",H="A recipe of the cooking trade, which teaches the making of Savory Deviate Delight. {T|185} It asks a skill of about 85 of a cook who attempts it.\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Only occasionally does one of the wild beasts there carry it."}
L[6662]="{K|1}\nIt is made, not found. {T|171} Its making calls for Deviate Fish, Earthroot and Empty Vial. It is first attempted at a Alchemy skill of about 90."
L[6663]={A="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Elixir of Giant Growth. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 90) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} {P|soldiers and mercenaries} It is a rare find among the soldiers and mercenaries; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling.",H="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Elixir of Giant Growth. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 90) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} It is the north of the savannah of the Barrens that rewards the search. It is a rare find among the wild beasts there; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."}
L[6664]="{A|1} {C|8} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} The folk of the Stonetalon Mountains have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[6665]="{A|3} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} The folk of the Stonetalon Mountains have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[6666]="{A|3} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} The folk of the Stonetalon Mountains have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
