L[7449]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Dusky Leather Leggings. {T|165} Only a leatherworker of some skill (around 165) can follow it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 26-39 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[7450]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Green Whelp Armor. {T|165} Only a leatherworker of some skill (around 175) can follow it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 26-39, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[7451]={A="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Green Whelp Bracers. {T|165} It asks a skill of about 190 of a leatherworker who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|leatherworking suppliers} {Z|Teldrassil} Merchants in the boughs of Teldrassil and the night elf city of Darnassus stock it. The shop is in the west of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it.",H="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Green Whelp Bracers. {T|165} It asks a skill of about 190 of a leatherworker who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|leatherworking suppliers} {Z|Undercity} Merchants in the Undercity and the rainforest of Feralas stock it. The shop is in the east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."}
L[7452]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Dusky Boots. {T|165} It asks a skill of about 200 of a leatherworker who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 31-45 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[7453]="A pattern of the leatherworking trade, which teaches the making of Swift Boots. {T|165} Only a leatherworker of some skill (around 200) can follow it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 32-45, and no two finders agree where to look."
