L[7966]="{R|4}\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} This one is worked from Solid Stone. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 200."
L[7967]="A material of the crafting trades.\nIt is made, not found. {T|164} This one is worked from Mithril Bar, Truesilver Bar and Solid Grinding Stone. Only a blacksmith of real accomplishment (skill around 215) can attempt it."
L[7968]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is carried by the beasts, but only in the territory of the Horde, and a traveller of the Alliance must go armed or trade for it.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Within the savannah of the Barrens, they keep to the east. The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[7969]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} Its making calls for Mithril Bar and Solid Grinding Stone. It is first attempted at a Blacksmithing skill of about 235."
L[7971]="{I|Black Pearl}\nIt is found inside Yellow Sack of Gems, and nowhere else in particular."
L[7972]="{I|Ichor of Undeath}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Look to the south of the Western Plaguelands. It is found as readily in the Eastern Plaguelands. Perhaps one in four of the restless dead has one about them."
L[7973]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} {P|naga} It is found on almost all of the naga. It is also fished from Temple of Arkkoran in Azshara."
L[7974]="{R|6}\nIt is found in the clams of the coasts, pried open by whoever gathers them from the shallows and the murlocs."
L[7975]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Heavy Mithril Pants. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 210 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 36-50 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[7976]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Shield Spike. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 215) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} It is found as readily in the rainforest of Feralas. It is a very rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[7978]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Barbaric Iron Shoulders. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 160) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7979]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Barbaric Iron Breastplate. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 160) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7980]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Barbaric Iron Helm. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 175) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7981]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Barbaric Iron Boots. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 180) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7982]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Barbaric Iron Gloves. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 185 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7983]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Ornate Mithril Pants. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 220 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7984]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Ornate Mithril Gloves. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 220) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7985]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Ornate Mithril Shoulder. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 225) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[7989]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Spurs. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 235) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} It is found as readily in the rainforest of Feralas. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[7990]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Heavy Mithril Helm. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 245) can follow it.\nHunters find it most readily in the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} The other place to look is the desert of Tanaris. It is a very rare find among the creatures of the region, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[7991]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Scale Shoulders. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 235) can follow it.\nThe place to look is Blackrock Depths. {D|Blackrock Depths} The other place to look is the desert of Tanaris. One of the raiders and tribesmen there in many hundreds carries it."
L[7992]={A="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Blue Glittering Axe. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 220) can follow it.\nThe place to look is the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} It is the south-west of the mists of Dustwallow Marsh that rewards the search. {B|raptors} It turns up on the raptors now and then, perhaps once in twenty.",H="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Blue Glittering Axe. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 220) can follow it.\nThe place to look is the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} It is the south-west of the mists of Dustwallow Marsh that rewards the search. The other place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {B|raptors} It turns up on the raptors now and then, perhaps once in twenty."}
L[7993]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Dazzling Mithril Rapier. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 240 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 43-55 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[7995]={A="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Scale Bracers. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 215 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|blacksmithing suppliers} {Z|The Hinterlands} Merchants in the Hinterlands and the farmland of Hillsbrad stock it. The shop is in the west of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it.",H="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Scale Bracers. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 215 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|blacksmithing suppliers} {Z|Swamp of Sorrows} A merchant in the sodden Swamp of Sorrows stocks it. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."}
L[7997]={A="An accessory of the adventuring trade. {C|0} {Q|0.1}\nHunters find it most readily in the fallow farmland of Westfall. {Z|Westfall} {P|Defias brigands} Only occasionally does one of the Defias brigands carry it.",H="An accessory of the adventuring trade. {C|0} {Q|0.1}\nIts source is the Deadmines, and nowhere in the open world. {D|The Deadmines} {P|Defias brigands} It is the Defias brigands of the Deadmines who have it about them."}
L[8006]="{W|15} {Q|3.0} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 35-42, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[8007]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is conjured by mages out of nothing, as they conjure bread and water, and vanishes when its maker is long gone."
L[8008]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is conjured by mages out of nothing, as they conjure bread and water, and vanishes when its maker is long gone."
L[8009]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the loch country of Loch Modan. {Z|Loch Modan} Within the loch country of Loch Modan, they keep to the south. The other place to look is the Badlands. {P|Dark Iron dwarves} The Dark Iron dwarves there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the Badlands. {Z|Badlands} Within the Badlands, they keep to the north. {P|Dark Iron dwarves} The Dark Iron dwarves there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[8026]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nChests and strongboxes hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[8027]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nChests and strongboxes hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[8028]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Runed Mithril Hammer. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 245) can follow it.\nHunters find it most readily in the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} The other place to look is Blackrock Depths. It is a very rare find among the creatures of the region, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[8029]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Wicked Mithril Blade. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 225 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} It is found as readily in Maraudon. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[8030]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Ebon Shiv. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 255) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|merchants} {Z|Western Plaguelands} A merchant in the Western Plaguelands stocks it. The shop is in the south-east of the land."
L[8047]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in Uldaman. {D|Uldaman} The other place to look is the loch country of Loch Modan. It is taken from Magenta Cap Clusters in Uldaman.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in Uldaman. {D|Uldaman} It is taken from Magenta Cap Clusters in Uldaman."}
L[8048]={A="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is found in the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} It is the east of the boughs of Teldrassil that rewards the search. It is taken from a Tallonkai's Dresser in the boughs of Teldrassil.",H="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is taken from a Tallonkai's Dresser."}
L[8049]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the boughs of Teldrassil. {Z|Teldrassil} Within the boughs of Teldrassil, they keep to the east. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is carried by the humanoid foes, but only in the territory of the Alliance, and a traveller of the Horde must go armed or trade for it."}
L[8050]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found inside a Gnarlpine Necklace, and nowhere else in particular."
L[8052]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the loch country of Loch Modan. {Z|Loch Modan} It is the south of the loch country of Loch Modan that rewards the search. The other place to look is the Badlands. {P|Dark Iron dwarves} The Dark Iron dwarves there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the Badlands. {Z|Badlands} It is the north of the Badlands that rewards the search. {P|Dark Iron dwarves} The Dark Iron dwarves there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[8053]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts source is Uldaman, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Uldaman} {P|mechanical constructs} It is the mechanical constructs of Uldaman who have it about them."
L[8066]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[8067]="Ammunition for the hunters' bows and guns, sold by every bowyer and gunsmith and made by the engineers.\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} This one is worked from Rough Blasting Powder and Copper Bar."
L[8068]="Ammunition for the hunters' bows and guns, sold by every bowyer and gunsmith and made by the engineers.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} Its making calls for Coarse Blasting Powder and Copper Bar. An engineer of middling skill (around 75) can attempt it."
L[8069]="Ammunition for the hunters' bows and guns, sold by every bowyer and gunsmith and made by the engineers.\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} Its making calls for Heavy Blasting Powder and Bronze Bar. An engineer of middling skill (around 125) can attempt it."
L[8071]="{W|19} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Wailing Caverns. {D|Wailing Caverns} Those who have a stake in the Wailing Caverns give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
L[8072]={A="A key, which opens one door in Azeroth and no other.\nOur correspondents report it among the humanoid foes in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="A key, which opens one door in Azeroth and no other.\nPickpockets know it from the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Look to the north of the savannah of the Barrens. Rogues lift it from the pockets of the humanoid foes there, who seldom notice."}
L[8073]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Within the savannah of the Barrens, the caches keep to the north. Chests and strongboxes in the savannah of the Barrens hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."}
L[8074]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is carried by the humanoid foes, but only in the territory of the Horde, and a traveller of the Alliance must go armed or trade for it.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Look to the north of the savannah of the Barrens. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
