L[9293]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Magic Resistance Potion. {T|171} It asks a skill of about 210 of an alchemist who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 36-50, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[9294]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Wildvine Potion. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 225) can follow it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 36-51 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[9295]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Invisibility Potion. {T|171} It asks a skill of about 235 of an alchemist who attempts it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 42-55, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[9296]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Gift of Arthas. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 240) can follow it.\nHunters find it most readily in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Look to the south of the Western Plaguelands. {P|skeletons} Only occasionally does one of the skeletons carry it."
L[9297]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Elixir of Dream Vision. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 240) can follow it.\nThe place to look is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} It is found as readily in Blackrock Depths. Only occasionally does one of the creatures of the region carry it."
L[9298]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Elixir of Giants. {T|171} It asks a skill of about 245 of an alchemist who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 42-55 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[9299]="A key, which opens one door in Azeroth and no other.\nIts source is Gnomeregan, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Gnomeregan} {P|mechanical constructs} It is the mechanical constructs of Gnomeregan who have it about them."
