L[10398]="A companion creature, kept by adventurers for company on the long roads and sold by the pet dealers of the capitals or found in the far places.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} The folk of the jungles of Stranglethorn have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[10399]="{A|2} {C|0} {Q|3.1} {L|1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Deadmines, and nowhere in the open world. {D|The Deadmines} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[10400]="{A|2} {C|0} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIts source is the Deadmines, and nowhere in the open world. {D|The Deadmines} {P|Defias brigands} Within, it is the Defias brigands who carry it."
L[10401]="{A|2} {C|0} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIts source is the Deadmines, and nowhere in the open world. {D|The Deadmines} {P|Defias brigands} Within, it is the Defias brigands who carry it."
L[10402]="{A|2} {C|0} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIts source is the Deadmines, and nowhere in the open world. {D|The Deadmines} {P|Defias brigands} It is the Defias brigands of the Deadmines who have it about them."
L[10403]="{A|2} {C|0} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIt comes out of the Deadmines. {D|The Deadmines} {P|soldiers and mercenaries} Within, it is the soldiers and mercenaries who carry it."
L[10404]="{A|1} {Q|2.0} {L|2}\nThe place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is found as readily in the mesas of Thousand Needles. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[10405]={A="{A|2} {L|1}\nHunters find it most readily in the red hills around Lake Everstill. {Z|Redridge Mountains} It is found as readily in the marshes of the Wetlands. It is a rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling.",H="{A|2} {L|1}\nHunters find it most readily in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is found as readily in the farmland of Hillsbrad. One of the raiders and tribesmen there in a score or so carries it."}
L[10406]="{A|2} {Q|2.0} {L|2}\nHunters find it most readily in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} The other place to look is the Arathi Highlands. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[10407]={A="{A|3} {Q|1.1} {L|1}\nThe place to look is the red hills around Lake Everstill. {Z|Redridge Mountains} The other place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Perhaps one in four of the raiders and tribesmen there has one about them.",H="{A|3} {Q|1.1} {L|1}\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} The other place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Perhaps one in four of the creatures of the region has one about them."}
L[10408]="{A|3} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nThe place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} The other place to look is the Arathi Highlands. Only occasionally does one of the creatures of the region carry it."
L[10409]="{A|3} {Q|2.0} {L|2}\nThe place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is found as readily in the Arathi Highlands. It is a rare find among the creatures of the region; a patient hunter may see one in a long day's culling."
L[10410]="{A|2} {Q|3.1} {L|1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[10411]="{A|2} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIts source is the Wailing Caverns, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Wailing Caverns} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[10412]="{A|2} {Q|2.0} {L|1}\nIt comes out of the Wailing Caverns. {D|Wailing Caverns} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[10413]="{A|2} {Q|2.1} {L|1}\nIt comes out of the Wailing Caverns. {D|Wailing Caverns} {P|elves} Within, it is the elves who carry it."
L[10418]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|14}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[10420]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt comes out of Razorfen Downs. {D|Razorfen Downs} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[10421]="{A|3} {L|0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} This one is worked from Copper Bar."
L[10423]="{A|3} {Q|2.1} {L|2}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|164} Its making calls for Bronze Bar, Silver Bar and Coarse Grinding Stone. A blacksmith of middling skill (around 155) can attempt it."
L[10424]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Silvered Bronze Leggings. {T|164} It asks a skill of about 155 of a blacksmith who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 21-34 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[10438]={A="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} Look to the south-west of the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is taken from a Felix's Box in the snowfields of Dun Morogh.",H="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is taken from a Felix's Box."}
L[10441]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt comes out of the Wailing Caverns. {D|Wailing Caverns} The rank and file of the Wailing Caverns have it about them."
L[10442]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in the smoking Searing Gorge. {Z|Searing Gorge} Within the smoking Searing Gorge, they keep to the north-west. It is taken from a Twilight Artifact in the smoking Searing Gorge."
L[10444]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the dwarven city of Ironforge. {Z|Ironforge} The folk of the dwarven city of Ironforge have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[10446]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the smoking Searing Gorge. {Z|Searing Gorge} It is the north of the smoking Searing Gorge that rewards the search. The elementals there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10447]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the smoking Searing Gorge. {Z|Searing Gorge} The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10450]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Perhaps one in four of the wild beasts there has one about them."
L[10454]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar. {D|Sunken Temple} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[10455]="{J|12} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Temple of Atal'Hakkar. {D|Sunken Temple} Those who have a stake in the Temple of Atal'Hakkar give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
L[10456]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the red hills around Lake Everstill. {Z|Redridge Mountains} The folk of the red hills around Lake Everstill have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."}
L[10457]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nPickpockets know it from the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} Look to the north of the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. It is found as readily in the grey wastes of Desolace. Rogues lift it from the pockets of the humanoid foes there, who seldom notice."
L[10458]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|6}\nThe place to look is the smoking Searing Gorge. {Z|Searing Gorge} Look to the north-west of the smoking Searing Gorge. {P|Twilight's Hammer cultists} The Twilight's Hammer cultists there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10459]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the humanoid foes in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the plains of Mulgore. {Z|Mulgore} Within the plains of Mulgore, they keep to the south-east. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[10460]="A key, which opens one door in Azeroth and no other. {C|8}\nNearly every one of the strange creatures carries one."
L[10461]="{A|1} {Q|2.0}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[10462]="{A|1} {Q|2.0}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[10463]="A pattern of the tailoring trade, which teaches the making of Shadoweave Mask. {T|197} Only a tailor of some skill (around 245) can follow it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[10467]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the smoking Searing Gorge. {Z|Searing Gorge} Look to the west of the smoking Searing Gorge. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10479]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[10498]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} This one is worked from Steel Bar. An engineer of middling skill (around 175) can attempt it."
L[10499]="{A|1} {Q|2.0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} This one is worked from Heavy Leather and Citrine. It is first attempted at a Engineering skill of about 175."
