L[10586]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} This one is worked from Mithril Casing, Goblin Rocket Fuel and Solid Dynamite. It is first attempted at a Engineering skill of about 235."
L[10587]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} This one is worked from Mithril Casing, Solid Blasting Powder and Truesilver Bar. Only an engineer of real accomplishment (skill around 230) can attempt it."
L[10588]="{A|1} {C|3} {Q|2.1}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} Its making calls for Goblin Construction Helmet, Goblin Rocket Fuel and Mithril Bar. It is first attempted at a Engineering skill of about 245."
L[10592]="{K|1}\nIt is made, not found. {T|171} Its making calls for Goldthorn, Fadeleaf and Leaded Vial. Only an alchemist of real accomplishment (skill around 200) can attempt it. It is also found inside containers such as Cenarion Circle Cache and Sturdy Junkbox."
L[10593]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Blasted Lands. {Z|Blasted Lands} It is the north of the Blasted Lands that rewards the search. It turns up on the raiders and tribesmen there now and then, perhaps once in twenty."
L[10597]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Look to the north of the fallen coast of Azshara. The humanoid foes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10598]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Within the fallen coast of Azshara, they keep to the heart of the land. The strange creatures there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10599]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Look to the middle of the fallen coast of Azshara. The strange creatures there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10600]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Look to the middle of the fallen coast of Azshara. The strange creatures there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[10601]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Bright-Eye Goggles. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 175) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the north-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. The other place to look is the grey wastes of Desolace. It is a very rare find among the creatures of the region, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[10602]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Deadly Scope. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 210 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Merchants in the jungles of Stranglethorn and the Badlands stock it. The shop is in the north of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[10603]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Catseye Ultra Goggles. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 220) can follow it.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 37-50, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[10604]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Heavy-bore Rifle. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 220 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 36-50 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[10605]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Spellpower Goggles Xtreme. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 225 of an engineer who attempts it.\nHunters find it most readily in the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} It is found as readily in the rainforest of Feralas. It is a very rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[10606]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Parachute Cloak. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 225) can follow it.\nAnglers know it from Zul'Farrak. {D|Zul'Farrak} Anglers pull it from the waters of Zul'Farrak."
L[10607]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Deepdive Helmet. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 230) can follow it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|Azshara} A merchant in the fallen coast of Azshara stocks it. The shop is in the south of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[10608]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Sniper Scope. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 240) can follow it.\nThe place to look is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} The other place to look is the jungle crater of Un'Goro. One of the creatures of the region in many hundreds carries it."
L[10609]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Mithril Mechanical Dragonling. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 250) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|The Hinterlands} A merchant in the Hinterlands stocks it. The shop is in the north-west of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[10620]="{I|Thorium Ore}\nMiners know it from the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} The other place to look is the jungle crater of Un'Goro. Miners strike it in the thorium veins in the sands of Silithus."
L[10621]={A="{K|3}\nOur correspondents report it among the humanoid foes in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by.",H="{K|3}\nThe place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {Z|The Barrens} Within the savannah of the Barrens, they keep to the south. It is carried by one of the rare, named creatures that roam there and are seen only now and then, and nowhere else."}
