L[12558]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} It is the north-east of the snows of Winterspring that rewards the search. Nearly every one of the raiders and tribesmen there carries one."
L[12562]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|34}\nIt is found in Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} It is taken from Inconspicuous Documents in Blackrock Spire."
L[12564]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the mesas of Thousand Needles. {Z|Thousand Needles} Within the mesas of Thousand Needles, they keep to the north. {P|centaur} It is found on almost all of the centaur.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the mesas of Thousand Needles. {Z|Thousand Needles} Within the mesas of Thousand Needles, they keep to the north. The other place to look is the savannah of the Barrens. {P|centaur} It is found on almost all of the centaur."}
L[12582]="{W|15} {Q|3.0} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The rank and file of Blackrock Spire have it about them."
L[12583]="{W|6} {Q|3.0} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} It is among the treasures that Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[12584]="{W|7} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|quartermasters} A merchant in Champions' Hall stocks it."
L[12586]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} {B|spiders} It is the spiders of Blackrock Spire who have it about them."
L[12587]="The Eye of Rend is a helm of Blackrock make, named for the warchief Rend Blackhand and worked with the clan's black and red.\nRend himself keeps it in the Hall of Blackhand in Blackrock Spire, where he holds court for Nefarian."
L[12589]="{A|1} {Q|3.1} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The rank and file of Blackrock Spire have it about them."
L[12590]="Felstriker is a dagger of the Blackrock orcs' warlocks, its edge sharpened on fel so that every wound it opens, for an instant, is mortal.\nWarchief Rend Blackhand keeps it in the Hall of Blackhand at the top of Blackrock Spire."
L[12592]="The Blackblade of Shahram holds the shade of Shahram, an ancient warrior bound into the steel, who comes forth to fight beside its wielder with the curses and blessings of his age.\nGeneral Drakkisath, the dragonspawn commander of Blackrock Spire's upper halls, carries it."
L[12602]="{A|6} {Q|3.1} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} It is among the treasures that Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[12603]="{A|2} {Q|3.1} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The rank and file of Blackrock Spire have it about them."
L[12604]="{A|1} {Q|3.1} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
