L[12839]="A plans of the blacksmithing trade, which teaches the making of Heartseeker. {T|164} Only a blacksmith of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIts source is Stratholme, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[12840]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} It is the south of the Western Plaguelands that rewards the search. The other place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. Nearly every one of the restless dead carries one."
L[12841]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} It is found as readily in Stratholme. Nearly every one of the restless dead carries one."
L[12842]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Look to the east of the snows of Winterspring. {P|furbolg} Nearly every one of the furbolg carries one."
L[12843]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[12844]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|12}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} The other place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. The folk of the Western Plaguelands have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[12845]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in Stratholme: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[12846]="The Argent Dawn Commission is the Dawn's token of service, which lets its wearer collect the Scourgestones from the undead they slay and turn them in at Light's Hope for the Dawn's favour.\nThe Argent Dawn's officers at Light's Hope Chapel and Chillwind Camp give it to anyone who will fight the Scourge."
L[12849]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} Those who have a stake in Blackrock Spire give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
L[12871]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[12884]={A="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the mesas of Thousand Needles. {Z|Thousand Needles} Look to the north of the mesas of Thousand Needles. {P|Grimtotem tauren} The Grimtotem tauren there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the mesas of Thousand Needles. {Z|Thousand Needles} Look to the north of the mesas of Thousand Needles. It is found as readily in the savannah of the Barrens. {P|Grimtotem tauren} The Grimtotem tauren there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."}
L[12886]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is found in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} Look to the south of the Eastern Plaguelands. It is taken from a Pamela's Doll's Head in the Eastern Plaguelands."
L[12887]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} Within the Eastern Plaguelands, they keep to the south. It is taken from a Pamela's Doll's Left Side in the Eastern Plaguelands."
L[12888]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} Look to the south of the Eastern Plaguelands. It is taken from a Pamela's Doll's Right Side in the Eastern Plaguelands."
L[12894]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is found in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Within the Western Plaguelands, they keep to the south. It is taken from a Joseph Redpath's Monument in the Western Plaguelands."
L[12895]="{A|4} {Q|4.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} It is given in thanks by those in the Western Plaguelands whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[12896]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Look to the middle of the snows of Winterspring. It is taken from a Highborne Relic Fragment in the snows of Winterspring."
L[12897]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Look to the middle of the snows of Winterspring. It is taken from a Highborne Relic Fragment in the snows of Winterspring."
L[12898]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Look to the middle of the snows of Winterspring. It is taken from a Highborne Relic Fragment in the snows of Winterspring."
L[12899]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Look to the middle of the snows of Winterspring. It is taken from a Highborne Relic Fragment in the snows of Winterspring."
L[12900]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Within the Western Plaguelands, they keep to the south. It is taken from a Musty Tome in the Western Plaguelands."
L[12903]="{A|3} {Q|4.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} The folk of the Western Plaguelands have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[12905]="{A|1} {Q|3.0} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} It is among the treasures that Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[12924]="{K|12}\nIt is found in the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} Within the poisoned forest of Felwood, they keep to the west. It is taken from a Ritual Candle in the poisoned forest of Felwood."
L[12925]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\n{B|wind serpents} It is found on almost all of the wind serpents."
L[12926]="{J|11} {Q|3.0} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The great prizes of Blackrock Spire are kept by Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords, and this is one of them."
