L[12935]="{A|4} {Q|3.0} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The great prizes of Blackrock Spire are kept by Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords, and this is one of them."
L[12936]="{A|4} {Q|3.0} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} The great prizes of Blackrock Spire are kept by Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords, and this is one of them."
L[12938]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} It is found as readily in the Western Plaguelands. It is taken from Blood of Heroes in the Eastern Plaguelands."
L[12939]="Dal'Rend's Tribal Guardian is the off-hand blade of Rend Blackhand's pair, the Arms of Dal'Rend, worked in the Blackrock clan's tribal style.\nRend carries it in the Hall of Blackhand at the top of Blackrock Spire."
L[12940]="Dal'Rend's Sacred Charge is one of the two swords of Rend Blackhand, warchief of the Blackrock clan under Nefarian. Together with the Tribal Guardian it makes the Arms of Dal'Rend, a pair warriors seek across Azeroth.\nRend carries it into the Hall of Blackhand at the top of Blackrock Spire."
L[12945]="{A|3} {Q|4.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} It is given in thanks by those in the Western Plaguelands whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
