L[13133]="{A|3} {Q|3.1} {L|5}\nThe place to look is the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} Within the rainforest of Feralas, they keep to the north. It is carried by one of the rare, named creatures that roam there and are seen only now and then, and nowhere else."
L[13134]="{A|3} {Q|3.0} {L|4}\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 44-52 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[13135]="{A|3} {Q|3.0} {L|5}\nThe place to look is the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} It is the north of the rainforest of Feralas that rewards the search. It is carried by one of the rare, named creatures that roam there and are seen only now and then, and nowhere else."
L[13136]="{W|3} {Q|3.1} {L|1}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 19-24, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[13137]="{W|3} {Q|3.0} {L|2}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 31-37, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[13138]="{W|3} {Q|3.1} {L|3}\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 40-46, and no two finders agree where to look."
L[13139]="{W|3} {Q|3.0} {L|4}\nThe place to look is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Within the fallen coast of Azshara, they keep to the south. The other place to look is Onyxia's Lair. It is held by one of the mighty foes of the fallen coast of Azshara, not by the common run of its creatures."
L[13140]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} Look to the west of the poisoned forest of Felwood. {P|cultists} It turns up on the cultists now and then, perhaps once in twenty."
L[13141]="{J|2} {Q|3.1} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} It is among the treasures that Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[13142]="{A|4} {Q|3.1} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} It is among the treasures that Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[13143]="{J|11} {Q|4.0} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} {P|dragons} It is the dragons of Blackrock Spire who have it about them."
