L[13335]="The reins of a deathcharger, the skeletal warhorse of the Scourge's death knights. Baron Rivendare rides one through the streets of Stratholme, and the rare slayer who can master the beast rides it out.\nThe Baron yields it in the Slaughter Square of Stratholme, and seldom; many hundreds have taken the city and left on foot."
L[13340]="The cloak of Baron Rivendare, the death knight of Stratholme, cut from the black cloth of the Scourge's court.\nThe Baron gives it up in the Slaughter Square of Stratholme."
L[13344]="{A|3} {Q|3.0} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[13345]="{J|11} {Q|3.1} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[13346]="{A|1} {Q|3.1} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[13348]="{W|8} {Q|3.1} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Stratholme, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[13349]="{W|4} {Q|3.0} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} The rank and file of Stratholme have it about them."
L[13350]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[13351]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|1}\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} {P|Scarlet Crusaders} Within, it is the Scarlet Crusaders who carry it."
L[13352]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} {P|soldiers and mercenaries} It is the soldiers and mercenaries of Blackrock Spire who have it about them."
L[13353]="{J|23} {Q|4.0} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Stratholme, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Stratholme} The rank and file of Stratholme have it about them."
L[13354]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Within the Western Plaguelands, they keep to the east. {P|ghosts and spirits} Nearly every one of the ghosts and spirits carries one."
L[13356]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Look to the south of the Western Plaguelands. {P|ghouls} It is found on almost all of the ghouls."
L[13357]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nHunters find it most readily in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Look to the south of the Western Plaguelands. {P|skeletons} Nearly every one of the skeletons carries one."
L[13358]="{A|2} {Q|3.1} {L|5} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[13359]="{A|3} {Q|3.1} {L|5} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} The rank and file of Stratholme have it about them."
