L[13542]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found on almost all of the demons."
L[13544]="{J|12} {Q|2.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in Scholomance. {D|Scholomance} Those who have a stake in Scholomance give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
L[13545]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is found in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is the south-west of the grey wastes of Desolace that rewards the search. It is taken from a Shellfish Trap in the grey wastes of Desolace."
L[13546]="{K|5}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is given in thanks by those in the grey wastes of Desolace whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[13562]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} The folk of the poisoned forest of Felwood have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[13582]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} The other place to look is the snowfields of Dun Morogh. The folk of the woods of Elwynn have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} The other place to look is the plains of Mulgore. The folk of the red desert of Durotar have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."}
L[13583]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is bought, not hunted. It is also awarded by quests in Elwynn Forest and Dun Morogh.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is bought, not hunted. It is also awarded by quests in Durotar and Mulgore."}
L[13584]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} The other place to look is the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is given in thanks by those in the woods of Elwynn whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} The other place to look is the plains of Mulgore. It is given in thanks by those in the red desert of Durotar whose troubles an adventurer takes on."}
