L[16220]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Boots - Spirit. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 275 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} The other place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. It is a very rare find among the creatures of the region, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[16221]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Chest - Major Health. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 275) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|general goods merchants} {Z|Winterspring} A merchant in the snows of Winterspring stocks it. The shop is in the north of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[16222]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Shield - Superior Spirit. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 280 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nThe place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} It is the south-east of the Eastern Plaguelands that rewards the search. {P|Scarlet Crusaders} One of the Scarlet Crusaders in many hundreds carries it."
L[16223]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Icy Chill. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 285) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Within the snows of Winterspring, they keep to the heart of the land. Only occasionally does one of the restless dead carry it."
L[16224]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Cloak - Superior Defense. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 285 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|general goods merchants} {Z|Moonglade} A merchant in the sanctuary of Moonglade stocks it. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[16242]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Chest - Major Mana. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 290) can follow it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} Look to the south-east of the Eastern Plaguelands. {P|Scarlet Crusaders} Only occasionally does one of the Scarlet Crusaders carry it."
L[16243]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Runed Arcanite Rod. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 290 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|general goods merchants} {Z|Moonglade} A merchant in the sanctuary of Moonglade stocks it. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[16244]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Greater Strength. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 295 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} {P|trolls} It is the trolls of Blackrock Spire who have it about them."
L[16245]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Boots - Greater Agility. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 295 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nHunters find it most readily in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} It is found as readily in the Eastern Plaguelands. One of the creatures of the region in many hundreds carries it."
L[16246]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Bracer - Superior Strength. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 295) can follow it.\nHunters find it most readily in the haunted Deadwind Pass. {Z|Deadwind Pass} Within the haunted Deadwind Pass, they keep to the south-east. It is found as readily in the Blasted Lands. {P|ogres} Only occasionally does one of the ogres carry it."
L[16247]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant 2H Weapon - Superior Impact. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 295 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} The rank and file of Blackrock Spire have it about them."
L[16248]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Unholy. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 295 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} {P|spellcasters} Within, it is the spellcasters who carry it."
L[16249]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant 2H Weapon - Major Intellect. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt comes out of Stratholme. {D|Stratholme} {P|Scarlet Crusaders} It is the Scarlet Crusaders of Stratholme who have it about them."
L[16250]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Superior Striking. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIts source is Blackrock Spire, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Spire} {P|trolls} It is the trolls of Blackrock Spire who have it about them."
L[16251]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Bracer - Superior Stamina. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nLockboxes are the strongboxes of travellers who did not survive to open them, carried off by whatever killed them. Only a rogue's picks or an engineer's seaforium will open one, and this is among what they hold."
L[16252]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Crusader. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nHunters find it most readily in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} Within the Western Plaguelands, they keep to the north. {P|Scarlet Crusaders} One of the Scarlet Crusaders in many hundreds carries it."
L[16253]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Chest - Greater Stats. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is Zul'Gurub, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Zul'Gurub} The great prizes of Zul'Gurub are kept by Hakkar the Soulflayer and his high priests, and this is one of them."
L[16254]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Lifestealing. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIts source is Scholomance, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Scholomance} The rank and file of Scholomance have it about them."
L[16255]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant 2H Weapon - Major Spirit. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt comes out of Scholomance. {D|Scholomance} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[16302]={A="A book.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|demon trainers} {Z|Dun Morogh} Merchants in the snowfields of Dun Morogh and the woods of Elwynn stock it.",H="A book.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|demon trainers} {Z|Tirisfal Glades} Merchants in the blighted glades of Tirisfal and the red desert of Durotar stock it. The shop is in the south of the land."}
L[16303]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the south of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Nearly every one of the wild beasts there carries one."
L[16304]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the heart of the land. It is found on almost all of the wild beasts there."
L[16305]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Within the ancient forest of Ashenvale, they keep to the south-east. It is found on almost all of the wild beasts there."
L[16309]="{J|2} {Q|3.0} {L|4} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} Those who have a stake in Blackrock Spire give it to the adventurers who serve their cause there."
L[16312]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nThe place to look is the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} It is the south-west of the Stonetalon Mountains that rewards the search. {P|fire elementals} The fire elementals there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[16313]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} Look to the south-west of the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the snowfields of Dun Morogh: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."}
L[16314]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} Look to the south-west of the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is taken from Felix's Bucket of Bolts in the snowfields of Dun Morogh.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is taken from Felix's Bucket of Bolts."}
