L[16741]="{A|2} {Q|2.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[16742]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself. {C|7}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[16743]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} {P|furbolg} The furbolg there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[16744]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself. {C|7}\nIt is found in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the east of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is taken from a Warsong Oil in the ancient forest of Ashenvale."
L[16745]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself. {C|7}\nIt is found in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is the south-west of the jungles of Stranglethorn that rewards the search. It is taken from a Warsong Axe Shipment in the jungles of Stranglethorn."
L[16746]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|7}\nIt is found inside Bundle of Reports, and nowhere else in particular."
L[16747]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nChests and strongboxes hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[16748]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nChests and strongboxes hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[16762]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in Blackfathom Deeps. {D|Blackfathom Deeps} It is taken from a Fathom Stone in Blackfathom Deeps."
L[16763]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|7}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is given in thanks by those in the ancient forest of Ashenvale whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16764]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|7}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[16765]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|7}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is given in thanks by those in the ancient forest of Ashenvale whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16766]="{K|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|185} This one is worked from Zesty Clam Meat, Hot Spices and Ice Cold Milk. It is first attempted at a Cooking skill of about 225."
L[16767]="A recipe of the cooking trade, which teaches the making of Undermine Clam Chowder. {T|185} It asks a skill of about 225 of a cook who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|general goods merchants} {Z|Tanaris} A merchant in the desert of Tanaris stocks it. The shop is in the north-east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[16768]="{J|23} {Q|2.0}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|merchants} {Z|Felwood} A merchant in the poisoned forest of Felwood stocks it. The shop is in the north-east of the land."
L[16769]="{W|4} {C|9} {Q|2.0} {L|4}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|merchants} {Z|Felwood} A merchant in the poisoned forest of Felwood stocks it. The shop is in the north-east of the land."
L[16782]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\n{P|water elementals} Nearly every one of the water elementals carries one."
L[16784]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is found as readily in the stormy coast of Darkshore. It is taken from a Sapphire of Aku'Mai in the ancient forest of Ashenvale.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is taken from a Sapphire of Aku'Mai in the ancient forest of Ashenvale."}
L[16786]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|22}\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[16788]="{A|6} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} The folk of the grey wastes of Desolace have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[16789]="{W|19} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is given in thanks by those in the grey wastes of Desolace whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16790]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. It is found as readily in the stormy coast of Darkshore. {P|spellcasters} Perhaps one in four of the spellcasters has one about them.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} Look to the north-west of the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {P|spellcasters} A good share of the spellcasters carry it."}
L[16791]="{A|1} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is given in thanks by those in the grey wastes of Desolace whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16793]="{A|3} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is given in thanks by those in the grey wastes of Desolace whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16794]="{A|3} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is given in thanks by those in the grey wastes of Desolace whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16795]="{A|1} {C|47} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} It is among the treasures that Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[16796]="{A|1} {C|47} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} The great prizes of the Molten Core are kept by Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants, and this is one of them."
