L[16868]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} The great prizes of the Molten Core are kept by Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants, and this is one of them."
L[16869]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} Look to the middle of the snows of Winterspring. The dragonkin there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[16870]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the sodden Swamp of Sorrows. {Z|Swamp of Sorrows} It is the south-east of the sodden Swamp of Sorrows that rewards the search. The dragonkin there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[16871]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} Look to the east of the desert of Tanaris. The dragonkin there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[16872]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the marshes of the Wetlands. {Z|Wetlands} Within the marshes of the Wetlands, they keep to the east. The dragonkin there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nOur correspondents report it among the dragonkin in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by."}
L[16873]="{A|2} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} The folk of the grey wastes of Desolace have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[16882]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nPickpockets know it from the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The other place to look is the mesas of Thousand Needles. Rogues lift it from the pockets of the humanoid foes there, who seldom notice."
L[16883]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nPickpockets know it from the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is found as readily in the jungles of Stranglethorn. Rogues lift it from the pockets of the humanoid foes there, who seldom notice."
L[16884]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\n{P|trolls} A good share of the trolls carry it."
L[16885]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nOur correspondents report it among the troggs in Horde lands, where travellers of the Alliance are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|troggs}",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nOur correspondents report it among the troggs in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by. {P|troggs}"}
L[16886]={A="{W|7} {Q|3.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is given only by the Horde's questgivers, in thanks for errands a traveller of the Alliance cannot run.",H="{W|7} {Q|3.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."}
L[16887]={A="{J|23} {Q|3.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is given only by the Horde's questgivers, in thanks for errands a traveller of the Alliance cannot run.",H="{J|23} {Q|3.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."}
L[16889]="{W|10} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
