L[16958]="{A|4} {C|46} {Q|4.1} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Blackwing Lair. {D|Blackwing Lair} The great prizes of Blackwing Lair are kept by Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[16959]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackwing Lair. {D|Blackwing Lair} The great prizes of Blackwing Lair are kept by Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[16960]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackwing Lair. {D|Blackwing Lair} It is among the treasures that Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[16961]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Blackwing Lair, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackwing Lair} The great prizes of Blackwing Lair are kept by Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[16962]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} The great prizes of the Molten Core are kept by Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants, and this is one of them."
L[16963]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Onyxia's Lair, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Onyxia's Lair} The great prizes of Onyxia's Lair are kept by Onyxia, Broodmother of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[16964]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Blackwing Lair. {D|Blackwing Lair} It is among the treasures that Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[16965]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is Blackwing Lair, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackwing Lair} It is among the treasures that Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[16966]="{A|4} {C|52} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt comes out of Blackwing Lair. {D|Blackwing Lair} The great prizes of Blackwing Lair are kept by Nefarian and the lords of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[16967]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a catch of the Verdantis River and the Forgotten Coast. {Z|Feralas} It is fished from the Verdantis River and the Forgotten Coast by anyone with a pole and the patience."
L[16968]={A="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nAnglers know it from the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} The other place to look is the woods of Elwynn. It is fished from the Sar'theris Strand by anyone with a pole and the patience.",H="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nAnglers know it from the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is fished from the Sar'theris Strand by anyone with a pole and the patience."}
L[16969]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nAnglers know it from the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Anglers pull it from the Vile Reef in Stranglethorn Vale."
L[16970]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is a catch of the swamp pools and the Pool of Tears. {Z|Swamp of Sorrows} Anglers pull it from the swamp pools and the Pool of Tears."
L[16971]="{K|5}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[16975]="{A|1} {C|7} {Q|3.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} The folk of the ancient forest of Ashenvale have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[16976]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|9}\nIt is taken from a Murgut's Totem Basket."
L[16977]="{A|2} {C|7} {Q|3.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is given in thanks by those in the ancient forest of Ashenvale whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16978]="{A|3} {C|7} {Q|3.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ancient forest of Ashenvale. {Z|Ashenvale} It is given in thanks by those in the ancient forest of Ashenvale whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16979]="{A|1} {Q|4.1} {L|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|197} This one is worked from Bolt of Runecloth, Fiery Core and Essence of Fire. It is first attempted at a Tailoring skill of about 300."
L[16980]="{A|1} {Q|4.0} {L|5}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|197} Its making calls for Bolt of Runecloth, Fiery Core and Lava Core. It is first attempted at a Tailoring skill of about 300."
L[16981]="{A|1} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Stonetalon Mountains. {Z|Stonetalon Mountains} It is given in thanks by those in the Stonetalon Mountains whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[16982]="{A|2} {Q|4.0} {L|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|165} Its making calls for Core Leather, Fiery Core and Lava Core. Only a leatherworker of real accomplishment (skill around 295) can attempt it."
L[16983]="{A|2} {C|23} {Q|4.1} {L|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|165} Its making calls for Core Leather, Fiery Core and Lava Core. It is first attempted at a Leatherworking skill of about 300."
