L[18202]="{W|13} {Q|4.1} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nHunters find it most readily in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} It is the south of the fallen coast of Azshara that rewards the search. It is held by one of the mighty foes of the fallen coast of Azshara, not by the common run of its creatures."
L[18203]="{W|13} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} The great prizes of the Molten Core are kept by Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants, and this is one of them."
L[18204]="{A|1} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nThe place to look is the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Within the jungles of Stranglethorn, they keep to the north-east. The other place to look is the Blasted Lands. It is held by one of the mighty foes of the jungles of Stranglethorn, not by the common run of its creatures."
L[18205]="{J|2} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is Onyxia's Lair, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Onyxia's Lair} The great prizes of Onyxia's Lair are kept by Onyxia, Broodmother of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[18208]="{A|1} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Within the fallen coast of Azshara, they keep to the south. It is held by one of the mighty foes of the fallen coast of Azshara, not by the common run of its creatures."
L[18222]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts source is the ruins of Dire Maul, and nowhere in the open world. {Z|Dire Maul} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[18223]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIts source is the ruins of Dire Maul, and nowhere in the open world. {Z|Dire Maul} The rank and file of the ruins of Dire Maul have it about them."
L[18224]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} The rank and file of the ruins of Dire Maul have it about them."
L[18225]={A="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nHunters find it most readily in the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} It is the north-east of the snowfields of Dun Morogh that rewards the search. It is a very rare find among the raiders and tribesmen there, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them.",H="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIt is carried by the humanoid foes, but only in the territory of the Alliance, and a traveller of the Horde must go armed or trade for it."}
L[18226]={A="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nThe place to look is the snowfields of Dun Morogh. {Z|Dun Morogh} Within the snowfields of Dun Morogh, they keep to the north-east. One of the raiders and tribesmen there in many hundreds carries it.",H="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nOur correspondents report it among the humanoid foes in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by."}
