L[18253]="{K|0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|171} This one is worked from Heart of the Wild, Golden Sansam and Dreamfoil. It is first attempted at a Alchemy skill of about 300. It is also awarded for a quest within Molten Core."
L[18254]="{K|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|185} This one is worked from Runn Tum Tuber and Soothing Spices. Only a cook of real accomplishment (skill around 275) can attempt it."
L[18255]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders. It is also taken from Warpwood Pod within Dire Maul."
L[18256]={A="{I|Imbued Vial}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|alchemy suppliers} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides.",H="{I|Imbued Vial}\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|alchemy suppliers} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Horde lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides."}
L[18257]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Major Rejuvenation Potion. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt comes out of the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} It is among the treasures that Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[18258]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} It is given in thanks by those in the ruins of Dire Maul whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18259]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Spell Power. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt comes out of the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} The great prizes of the Molten Core are kept by Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants, and this is one of them."
L[18260]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Weapon - Healing Power. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} It is among the treasures that Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[18261]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} The rank and file of the ruins of Dire Maul have it about them."
