L[18398]="{J|11} {Q|3.1} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} It is given in thanks by those in the fallen coast of Azshara whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18399]="{J|11} {Q|3.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} It is given in thanks by those in the fallen coast of Azshara whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18400]="{J|11} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the sanctuary of Moonglade. {Z|Moonglade} It is given in thanks by those in the sanctuary of Moonglade whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18401]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} The rank and file of the ruins of Dire Maul have it about them."
L[18402]="{J|11} {Q|2.0}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the sanctuary of Moonglade. {Z|Moonglade} The folk of the sanctuary of Moonglade have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[18403]={A="{J|11} {Q|4.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the city of Stormwind. {Z|Stormwind City} It is given in thanks by those in the city of Stormwind whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{J|11} {Q|4.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. {Z|Orgrimmar} It is given in thanks by those in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar whose troubles an adventurer takes on."}
L[18404]={A="{J|2} {C|22} {Q|4.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the city of Stormwind. {Z|Stormwind City} It is given in thanks by those in the city of Stormwind whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{J|2} {C|22} {Q|4.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. {Z|Orgrimmar} It is given in thanks by those in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar whose troubles an adventurer takes on."}
L[18405]="{A|1} {Q|4.1} {L|5}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|197} Its making calls for Bolt of Runecloth, Ghost Dye and Mooncloth. Only a tailor of real accomplishment (skill around 300) can attempt it."
L[18406]={A="{J|12} {C|22} {Q|4.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the city of Stormwind. {Z|Stormwind City} It is given in thanks by those in the city of Stormwind whose troubles an adventurer takes on.",H="{J|12} {C|22} {Q|4.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. {Z|Orgrimmar} It is given in thanks by those in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar whose troubles an adventurer takes on."}
L[18407]="{A|1} {C|19} {Q|3.1} {L|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|197} This one is worked from Bolt of Runecloth, Felcloth and Demonic Rune. Only a tailor of real accomplishment (skill around 300) can attempt it."
L[18408]="{A|1} {Q|3.0} {L|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|197} This one is worked from Bolt of Runecloth, Essence of Fire and Star Ruby. Only a tailor of real accomplishment (skill around 300) can attempt it."
L[18409]="{A|1} {C|18} {Q|3.0} {L|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|197} Its making calls for Bolt of Runecloth, Mooncloth and Golden Pearl. It is first attempted at a Tailoring skill of about 300."
L[18410]="{W|8} {Q|2.0}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} It is given in thanks by those in the ruins of Dire Maul whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18411]="{A|2} {Q|2.1}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} It is given in thanks by those in the ruins of Dire Maul whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18412]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found in Blackrock Depths. {D|Blackrock Depths} It is taken from a Core Fragment in Blackrock Depths."
L[18413]="{A|1} {Q|3.1} {L|5}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|197} Its making calls for Bolt of Runecloth, Guardian Stone and Arcanite Bar. It is first attempted at a Tailoring skill of about 300."
L[18414]="A pattern of the tailoring trade, which teaches the making of Belt of the Archmage. {T|197} It asks a skill of about 300 of a tailor who attempts it.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} {P|ogres} It is the ogres of the ruins of Dire Maul who have it about them."
L[18415]="A pattern of the tailoring trade, which teaches the making of Felcloth Gloves. {T|197} Only a tailor of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} {P|ogres} Within, it is the ogres who carry it."
L[18416]="A pattern of the tailoring trade, which teaches the making of Inferno Gloves. {T|197} It asks a skill of about 300 of a tailor who attempts it.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} {P|ogres} Within, it is the ogres who carry it."
L[18417]="A pattern of the tailoring trade, which teaches the making of Mooncloth Gloves. {T|197} It asks a skill of about 300 of a tailor who attempts it.\nIts source is the ruins of Dire Maul, and nowhere in the open world. {Z|Dire Maul} {P|ogres} Within, it is the ogres who carry it."
L[18418]="A pattern of the tailoring trade, which teaches the making of Cloak of Warding. {T|197} It asks a skill of about 300 of a tailor who attempts it.\nIt comes out of the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} {P|ogres} It is the ogres of the ruins of Dire Maul who have it about them."
L[18420]="{W|5} {Q|3.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} The folk of the ruins of Dire Maul have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[18421]="{A|3} {Q|3.0} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} It is given in thanks by those in the ruins of Dire Maul whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[18422]="The head of Onyxia, Broodmother of the black dragonflight, who sat on the throne council of Stormwind in the guise of Lady Katrana Prestor and schemed the kingdom nearly to ruin before she was unmasked.\nIt is carried from her lair beneath Dustwallow Marsh to Stormwind, where King Varian's regents hang it from the gates of the city and the Light's blessing falls on all who see it."
L[18423]="The head of Onyxia, Broodmother of the black dragonflight, who meddled in the courts of men and whose brood threatened Theramore and the Horde's holdings in Dustwallow alike.\nIt is carried from her lair beneath Dustwallow Marsh to Orgrimmar, where Thrall has it hung from the gates of the Valley of Strength and the shaman bless all who gather there."
L[18424]="{A|2} {Q|3.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} The folk of the ruins of Dire Maul have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
