L[18634]="A material of the crafting trades.\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} This one is worked from Thorium Widget, Truesilver Transformer and Blue Sapphire. Only an engineer of real accomplishment (skill around 260) can attempt it."
L[18635]={A="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nThis is a thing one buys. {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the dwarven city of Ironforge stock it. The shop is in the south of the land.",H="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nThis is a thing one buys. {Z|Orgrimmar} A merchant in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar stocks it. The shop is in the south of the land."}
L[18637]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} This one is worked from Thorium Tube, Truesilver Transformer and Runecloth. It is first attempted at a Engineering skill of about 275."
L[18638]="A material of the crafting trades.\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} Its making calls for Dark Iron Bar, Truesilver Transformer and Essence of Water. It is first attempted at a Engineering skill of about 290."
L[18639]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} Its making calls for Dark Iron Bar, Truesilver Transformer and Living Essence. Only an engineer of real accomplishment (skill around 300) can attempt it."
L[18640]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nThe place to look is the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} It is found as readily in the rainforest of Feralas. {P|ogres} One of the ogres in a score or so carries it."
L[18641]="A material of the crafting trades.\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} Its making calls for Dense Blasting Powder and Runecloth. Only an engineer of real accomplishment (skill around 250) can attempt it."
L[18645]="A material of the crafting trades.\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} This one is worked from Thorium Bar, Thorium Widget and Rugged Leather. Only an engineer of real accomplishment (skill around 265) can attempt it."
L[18646]="The Eye of Divinity is a relic of the old priesthoods, carried into the Molten Core by some zealot of the Light and kept since in the court of the Firelord. It is the heart of the staff Benediction.\nMajordomo Executus, Ragnaros's steward, keeps it in his cache, and surrenders it only to those who scatter his flamewaker guard."
L[18647]={A="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Red Firework. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 150) can follow it.\nIt is stocked only by merchants of the Horde; a traveller of the Alliance must trade for it at the neutral ports or do without.",H="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Red Firework. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 150) can follow it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|Orgrimmar} A merchant in the Horde capital of Orgrimmar stocks it. The shop is in the north-east of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."}
L[18648]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Green Firework. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 150 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} Merchants in the jungles of Stranglethorn and the savannah of the Barrens stock it. The shop is in the south-west of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[18649]={A="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Blue Firework. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 150 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the dwarven city of Ironforge stock it. The shop is in the south-west of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it.",H="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Blue Firework. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 150 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIt is stocked only by merchants of the Alliance; a traveller of the Horde must trade for it at the neutral ports or do without."}
L[18650]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Ez-Thro Dynamite II. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 200) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|gun smiths} {Z|Tanaris} A merchant in the desert of Tanaris stocks it. The shop is in the north of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[18651]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Truesilver Transformer. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 260) can follow it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} A merchant in the jungles of Stranglethorn stocks it. The shop is in the south-west of the land. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[18652]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Gyrofreeze Ice Reflector. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 260 of an engineer who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|Winterspring} A merchant in the snows of Winterspring stocks it. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[18653]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Goblin Jumper Cables XL. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 265 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIts source is Blackrock Depths, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Depths} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[18654]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Gnomish Alarm-O-Bot. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 265) can follow it.\nIts source is Blackrock Depths, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Blackrock Depths} The rank and file of Blackrock Depths have it about them."
L[18655]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Major Recombobulator. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 275) can follow it.\nIt is found in the ruins of Dire Maul. {Z|Dire Maul} It is taken from a Gordok Tribute in the ruins of Dire Maul."
L[18656]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Powerful Seaforium Charge. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 275) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|engineering suppliers} {Z|Winterspring} A merchant in the snows of Winterspring stocks it. Stock is limited, and whoever gets there first takes it."
L[18657]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Hyper-Radiant Flame Reflector. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 290) can follow it.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The rank and file of Blackrock Spire have it about them."
L[18658]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Ultra-Flash Shadow Reflector. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 300 of an engineer who attempts it.\nIts source is Stratholme, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Stratholme} {P|Scarlet Crusaders} Within, it is the Scarlet Crusaders who carry it."
L[18659]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[18660]="A material of the crafting trades.\nIt is made, not found. {T|202} This one is worked from Mithril Casing, Thorium Widget and Gold Power Core. Only an engineer of real accomplishment (skill around 260) can attempt it."
L[18661]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of World Enlarger. {T|202} Only an engineer of some skill (around 260) can follow it.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Depths. {D|Blackrock Depths} The rank and file of Blackrock Depths have it about them."
L[18662]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is made, not found. {T|165} This one is worked from Heavy Leather and Fine Thread. A leatherworker of middling skill (around 150) can attempt it. It is also sold by a merchant in north-western Mulgore."
L[18663]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|merchants} {Z|Burning Steppes} A merchant in the ash plains of the Burning Steppes stocks it. The shop is in the north-west of the land."
