L[18802]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|merchants} {Z|Burning Steppes} A merchant in the ash plains of the Burning Steppes stocks it. The shop is in the north-west of the land."
L[18803]="{W|5} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the Molten Core: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[18805]="A core hound's tooth, as long as a dagger and as hard as obsidian, set into a hilt by the Firelord's flamewaker smiths. The core hounds are Ragnaros's kennel, two-headed lava-dogs that rise again if their packmates still live.\nIt is held by Magmadar, the pack's alpha, in the kennels of the Molten Core."
L[18806]="{A|4} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the Molten Core: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[18807]="{A|3} {Q|3.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[18808]="{A|1} {Q|4.1} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the Molten Core: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[18809]="{A|1} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} Chests and strongboxes in the Molten Core hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[18810]="{A|2} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} Chests and strongboxes in the Molten Core hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[18811]="{A|1} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} Chests and strongboxes in the Molten Core hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[18812]="{A|3} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Molten Core. {D|Molten Core} Chests and strongboxes in the Molten Core hold it now and then, left by whoever did not live to open them."
L[18813]="{J|11} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is Onyxia's Lair, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Onyxia's Lair} The great prizes of Onyxia's Lair are kept by Onyxia, Broodmother of the black dragonflight, and this is one of them."
L[18814]="The Choker of the Fire Lord is a collar of Sulfuron steel and fire-hardened gems from the Firelord's own regalia, wanted above all other things by the spellcasters who brave the Core.\nRagnaros surrenders it only when he is driven back into the lava of the Molten Core."
L[18815]="{J|12} {Q|4.0} {L|6} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} It is among the treasures that Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[18816]="Perdition's Blade is a dagger of the Firelord's court, its edge tempered in the lava of the Molten Core so that it carries the fire into every cut. Rogues have gone to Blackrock Mountain for a generation in the hope of it.\nIt is held by Ragnaros himself, deepest in the Core, and surrendered only when the Firelord is beaten back into the fire."
L[18817]="{A|3} {Q|4.1} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} It is among the treasures that Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants hold there, and only their fall releases it."
