L[19017]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself. {C|23}\nIts source is the Molten Core, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Molten Core} It is among the treasures that Ragnaros and his flamewaker lieutenants hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[19018]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} {P|air elementals} It is held by one of the mighty foes of the sands of Silithus, not by the common run of its creatures."
L[19019]="Thunderfury is the sword of Prince Thunderaan, son of Al'Akir the Windlord, who was slain and devoured by Ragnaros when the Firelord betrayed his elemental allies. What the Firelord could not consume he bound into two talismans and gave to his lieutenants Garr and Baron Geddon to keep.\nWhoever recovers both Bindings of the Windseeker from the Molten Core and brings them, with a measure of the Firelord's own essence and the labour of the Hydraxian Waterlords' smiths, to Highlord Demitrian in Silithus may call the prince's spirit back and have the blade reforged. It crackles with his lightning still."
L[19022]="{W|20} {Q|2.1}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} The folk of the Hinterlands have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[19023]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} Look to the east of the Hinterlands. The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[19024]="{J|12} {Q|3.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[19025]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} Look to the middle of the Hinterlands. The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[19026]="{K|10}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|202} Its making calls for Dense Blasting Powder, Runecloth and Deeprock Salt. It is first attempted at a Engineering skill of about 250."
L[19027]="A schematic of the engineering trade, which teaches the making of Snake Burst Firework. {T|202} It asks a skill of about 250 of an engineer who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|merchants} {Z|Feralas} A merchant in the rainforest of Feralas stocks it."
L[19028]={A="An accessory of the adventuring trade.\nIt is found in the woods of Elwynn. {Z|Elwynn Forest} Look to the south of the woods of Elwynn. It is found as readily in the boughs of Teldrassil. It is taken from a Brightly Colored Egg in the woods of Elwynn.",H="An accessory of the adventuring trade.\nIt is found in the red desert of Durotar. {Z|Durotar} The other place to look is the blighted glades of Tirisfal. It is taken from a Brightly Colored Egg in the red desert of Durotar."}
L[19029]={A="A mount, the pride of its rider, bred by the stables of its people or won from the great foes.\nIt is stocked only by merchants of the Horde; a traveller of the Alliance must trade for it at the neutral ports or do without.",H="A mount, the pride of its rider, bred by the stables of its people or won from the great foes.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|frostwolf supply officers} {Z|Alterac Mountains} A merchant in the Alterac Mountains stocks it. The shop is in the east of the land."}
L[19030]={A="A mount, the pride of its rider, bred by the stables of its people or won from the great foes.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|stormpike supply officers} {Z|Alterac Mountains} Merchants in the Alterac Mountains and the farmland of Hillsbrad stock it. The shop is in the south of the land.",H="A mount, the pride of its rider, bred by the stables of its people or won from the great foes.\nIt is stocked only by merchants of the Alliance; a traveller of the Horde must trade for it at the neutral ports or do without."}
