L[19227]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt comes out of Blackrock Spire. {D|Blackrock Spire} The great prizes of Blackrock Spire are kept by Rend Blackhand, General Drakkisath and the Spire's warlords, and this is one of them."
L[19229]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is among the prizes of the Darkmoon Faire, won with tickets at Silas Darkmoon's carnival."
L[19230]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is what the trade calls a world drop: no tribe, beast or master carries it in particular, and it surfaces wherever adventurers of levels 51-60 fight, from one end of the continents to the other."
L[19231]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} The other place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. It is a very rare find among the restless dead, the kind of thing found once in a lifetime of hunting them."
L[19232]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nNo one owner can be named for it. It turns up in the hoards and pockets of foes across Azeroth, most often among creatures of levels 51-59, and no two finders agree where to look."
