L[19970]="The Arcanite Fishing Pole is the finest fishing pole in Azeroth, forged of arcanite and strung with the best line, and the prize of the Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza.\nIt is given to the winner of the Extravaganza, held every week off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale by the Steamwheedle goblins of Booty Bay."
L[19971]="A material of the crafting trades.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[19972]="{A|1} {Q|2.0}\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[19974]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|merchants} {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} A merchant in the mists of Dustwallow Marsh stocks it."
L[19975]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt comes out of Zul'Gurub. {D|Zul'Gurub} {B|crocolisks} It is the crocolisks of Zul'Gurub who have it about them. It is also taken from Muddy Churning Waters and Mudskunk Lure within Zul'Gurub."
L[19978]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[19979]="The Hook of the Master Angler is a fishhook that lets its bearer breathe underwater and swim as fast as a fish, one of the prizes of the Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza.\nIt is given to the winner of the Extravaganza, held each week off the coast of Stranglethorn by the goblins of Booty Bay."
