L[20008]="{K|0}\nIt is made, not found. {T|171} Its making calls for Icecap, Mountain Silversage and Heart of the Wild. It is first attempted at a Alchemy skill of about 285."
L[20009]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[20010]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[20011]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Mageblood Potion. {T|171} It asks a skill of about 275 of an alchemist who attempts it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20012]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Greater Dreamless Sleep Potion. {T|171} It asks a skill of about 275 of an alchemist who attempts it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20013]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Living Action Potion. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 285) can follow it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20014]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Major Troll's Blood Potion. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 290) can follow it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20015]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {Z|Un'Goro Crater} It is the east of the jungle crater of Un'Goro that rewards the search. {B|raptors} A good share of the raptors carry it."
L[20016]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is Zul'Gurub. {D|Zul'Gurub} It is found as readily in the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {B|raptors} One of the raptors in a score or so carries it."
L[20017]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20018]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} Within the poisoned forest of Felwood, they keep to the north. {B|bears} The bears there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20019]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar. {D|Sunken Temple} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[20021]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|29}\nHunters find it most readily in the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} It is the east of the desert of Tanaris that rewards the search. {P|pirates} The pirates there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20022]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar. {D|Sunken Temple} The rank and file of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar have it about them."
L[20023]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nHunters find it most readily in the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} {P|oozes and slimes} The oozes and slimes there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20025]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts source is the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Sunken Temple} The rank and file of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar have it about them."
L[20027]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} The beasts there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20028]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nThe place to look is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Within the fallen coast of Azshara, they keep to the north. {P|elves} The elves there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20029]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Look to the middle of the fallen coast of Azshara. {P|naga} The naga there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20030]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nPickpockets know it from the fallen coast of Azshara. {Z|Azshara} Within the fallen coast of Azshara, they keep to the north. {P|furbolg} Rogues lift it from the pockets of the furbolg there, who seldom notice."
L[20031]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} The folk of the jungles of Stranglethorn have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[20032]="{A|1} {Q|4.0} {L|6} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt comes out of Zul'Gurub. {D|Zul'Gurub} The great prizes of Zul'Gurub are kept by Hakkar the Soulflayer and his high priests, and this is one of them."
