L[20725]="Nexus crystals are the enchanters' greatest reagent, drawn only from the epic items of the great dungeons when they are disenchanted, and needed for the enchantments of the heroes.\nEnchanters distil them from the epic prizes of the Molten Core, Blackwing Lair, Zul'Gurub and Ahn'Qiraj."
L[20726]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Threat. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[20727]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Shadow Power. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} It is among the treasures that the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[20728]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Frost Power. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[20729]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Fire Power. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[20730]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Healing Power. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} It is among the treasures that the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[20731]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Gloves - Superior Agility. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[20732]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Cloak - Greater Fire Resistance. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20733]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Cloak - Greater Nature Resistance. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20734]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Cloak - Stealth. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[20735]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Cloak - Subtlety. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} It is among the treasures that the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[20736]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches Enchant Cloak - Dodge. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[20741]="A curio of the adventuring trade. {C|9}\nThe place to look is the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} It is the north-east of the poisoned forest of Felwood that rewards the search. {P|furbolg} It turns up on the furbolg now and then, perhaps once in twenty."
L[20742]="A curio of the adventuring trade. {C|9}\nThe place to look is the snows of Winterspring. {Z|Winterspring} {P|furbolg} One of the furbolg in a score or so carries it."
L[20744]="{R|17}\nIt is made, not found. {T|333} This one is worked from Strange Dust, Maple Seed and Empty Vial. It is first attempted at a Enchanting skill of about 45."
L[20745]="{R|17}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|333} This one is worked from Soul Dust, Maple Seed and Leaded Vial. It is first attempted at a Enchanting skill of about 150."
L[20746]="{R|17}\nIt is made, not found. {T|333} Its making calls for Vision Dust, Stranglethorn Seed and Leaded Vial. It is first attempted at a Enchanting skill of about 200."
L[20747]="{R|17}\nIt is made, not found. {T|333} Its making calls for Dream Dust, Purple Lotus and Crystal Vial. Only an enchanter of real accomplishment (skill around 250) can attempt it."
L[20748]="{R|17}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|333} This one is worked from Large Brilliant Shard, Purple Lotus and Imbued Vial. It is first attempted at a Enchanting skill of about 300."
L[20749]="{R|17}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|333} This one is worked from Large Brilliant Shard, Firebloom and Imbued Vial. Only an enchanter of real accomplishment (skill around 300) can attempt it."
L[20750]="{R|17}\nIt is made, not found. {T|333} This one is worked from Illusion Dust, Firebloom and Crystal Vial. It is first attempted at a Enchanting skill of about 275."
L[20752]={A="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Minor Mana Oil. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 150) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the boughs of Teldrassil stock it. The shop is in the south of the land.",H="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Minor Mana Oil. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 150) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Silverpine Forest} Merchants in the grey woods of Silverpine and the plains of Mulgore stock it. The shop is in the south of the land."}
L[20753]={A="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Lesser Wizard Oil. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 200 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the boughs of Teldrassil stock it. The shop is in the south of the land.",H="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Lesser Wizard Oil. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 200 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Silverpine Forest} Merchants in the grey woods of Silverpine and the plains of Mulgore stock it. The shop is in the south of the land."}
L[20754]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Lesser Mana Oil. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 250) can follow it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Silithus} A merchant in the sands of Silithus stocks it."
L[20755]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Wizard Oil. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 275 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nThis is a thing one buys. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Silithus} A merchant in the sands of Silithus stocks it."
L[20756]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Brilliant Wizard Oil. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 300 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20757]="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Brilliant Mana Oil. {T|333} Only an enchanter of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20758]={A="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Minor Wizard Oil. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 45 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Stormwind City} Merchants in the city of Stormwind and the boughs of Teldrassil stock it. The shop is in the south of the land.",H="A formula of the enchanting trade, which teaches the making of Minor Wizard Oil. {T|333} It asks a skill of about 45 of an enchanter who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|enchanting suppliers} {Z|Silverpine Forest} Merchants in the grey woods of Silverpine and the plains of Mulgore stock it. The shop is in the south of the land."}
L[20761]="A recipe of the alchemy trade, which teaches the making of Elemental Fire. {T|171} Only an alchemist of some skill (around 300) can follow it.\nIt is issued by a quartermaster, and only to those who have earned their faction's trust through long service."
L[20763]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} It is found as readily in the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {P|oozes and slimes} It is found on almost all of the oozes and slimes."
L[20766]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the mists of Dustwallow Marsh. {Z|Dustwallow Marsh} Within the mists of Dustwallow Marsh, they keep to the heart of the land. {P|oozes and slimes} One of the oozes and slimes in a score or so carries it."
L[20767]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the Hinterlands. {Z|The Hinterlands} It is found as readily in Maraudon. {P|oozes and slimes} A good share of the oozes and slimes carry it."
L[20768]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the poisoned forest of Felwood. {Z|Felwood} Within the poisoned forest of Felwood, they keep to the heart of the land. The other place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. {P|oozes and slimes} One of the oozes and slimes in a score or so carries it."
L[20769]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is found inside an Oozing Bag, and nowhere else in particular."
L[20770]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {Z|Un'Goro Crater} Look to the west of the jungle crater of Un'Goro. It is found as readily in the Eastern Plaguelands. {P|oozes and slimes} Perhaps one in four of the oozes and slimes has one about them."
L[20800]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|25}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} It is given in thanks by those in the sands of Silithus whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[20801]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|25}\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} The folk of the sands of Silithus have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[20802]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else. {C|25}\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} It is given in thanks by those in the sands of Silithus whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[20803]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it. {C|42}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} Look to the west of the sands of Silithus. {P|Twilight's Hammer cultists} The Twilight's Hammer cultists there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[20805]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} It is given in thanks by those in the sands of Silithus whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[20806]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found inside a Logistics Assignment, and nowhere else in particular."
