L[21148]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the rainforest of Feralas. {Z|Feralas} Look to the north of the rainforest of Feralas. The dragonkin there surrender it only to those on the business of a quest."
L[21149]={A="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nThe place to look is the dark woods of Duskwood. {Z|Duskwood} It is held by one of the mighty foes of the dark woods of Duskwood, not by the common run of its creatures.",H="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nOur correspondents report it among the demons in Alliance lands, where travellers of the Horde are not welcome; it will be hard to come by."}
L[21150]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a catch of Lordamere Lake and Lake Dalaran. {Z|Alterac Mountains} Anglers pull it from Lordamere Lake and Lake Dalaran. It is also taken from Floating Wreckage and Oily Blackmouth School in north-western Stranglethorn Vale and northern Dustwallow Marsh."
L[21151]="{K|6}\nIt is found in the jungles of Stranglethorn. {Z|Stranglethorn Vale} It is taken from a Floating Wreckage in the jungles of Stranglethorn."
L[21153]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is a catch of Lordamere Lake and Lake Dalaran. {Z|Alterac Mountains} Anglers pull it from Lordamere Lake and Lake Dalaran. It is also taken from Greater Sagefish School in north-western Stranglethorn Vale and north-western Alterac Mountains."
L[21154]="An accessory of the adventuring trade. {Q|1.0}\nThis is the work of a craftsman's hands. {T|197} Its making calls for Bolt of Runecloth, Firebloom and Red Dye. Only a tailor of real accomplishment (skill around 250) can attempt it."
L[21156]="A curio of the adventuring trade. {C|21}\nIt is a finder's prize, chiefly in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The other place to look is the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj. It turns up in the chests and caches that adventurers find in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj: the lost baggage of the dead, the stashes of bandits and the strongboxes of camps long abandoned."
L[21157]="An accessory of the adventuring trade.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run."
L[21162]={A="{K|5}\nIt is a catch of the waters of Lordamere Lake. The other place to look is the stormy coast of Darkshore. Anglers pull it from the waters of Lordamere Lake.",H="{K|5}\nIt is a catch of the waters of Lordamere Lake. The other place to look is the grey woods of Silverpine. Anglers pull it from the waters of Lordamere Lake."}
L[21164]="{K|5}\nAnglers know it from the grey wastes of Desolace. {Z|Desolace} It is found as readily in Lordamere Lake. Anglers pull it from Shadowprey Village in Desolace."
L[21165]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt is found inside a Tactical Assignment, and nowhere else in particular."
L[21166]="An object of significance to someone in Azeroth, wanted for a task rather than for itself.\nIt is found inside a Tactical Assignment, and nowhere else in particular."
L[21167]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found inside a Followup Tactical Assignment, and nowhere else in particular."
L[21174]={A="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is found in the city of Stormwind. {Z|Stormwind City} It is the south of the city of Stormwind that rewards the search. The other place to look is the snowfields of Dun Morogh. It is taken from a Festive Mug in the city of Stormwind.",H="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is found in the Undercity. {Z|Undercity} It is the north-east of the Undercity that rewards the search. The other place to look is the mesa city of Thunder Bluff. It is taken from a Festive Mug in the Undercity."}
L[21175]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the desert of Tanaris. {Z|Tanaris} It is given in thanks by those in the desert of Tanaris whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[21176]="The Black Qiraji Resonating Crystal is the mount-crystal of the qiraji battle tanks, the great insect steeds of Ahn'Qiraj, and the only one of its kind that will carry its rider outside the temple's walls.\nIt is given to the champion who gathers the Scepter of the Shifting Sands and rings the gong at the Scarab Wall to open Ahn'Qiraj, and to no one else."
L[21177]={A="{I|Symbol of Kings}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|reagent vendors} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Alliance lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides.",H="{I|Symbol of Kings}\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|reagent vendors} It is as common as bread: nearly every settlement in Horde lands stocks it, and the goblin ports besides."}
L[21178]="{A|2} {Q|3.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} It is given in thanks by those in the sands of Silithus whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[21179]="{J|11} {C|52} {Q|3.0} Once taken up it will serve no other hand.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} The folk of the sands of Silithus have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
L[21180]="{J|12} {Q|4.1} It binds itself to whoever first takes it up, and cannot be sold or given away.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} The folk of the sands of Silithus have reason to be grateful to adventurers, and this is among what they give in thanks."
