L[21211]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt is found inside a Smokywood Satchel, and nowhere else in particular."
L[21213]="A consumable of the road, used once and gone.\nIt is given in thanks by a questgiver somewhere in Azeroth, for an errand run. It is also found inside a Ticking Present."
L[21214]="A book.\nIt comes out of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj} It is among the treasures that Ossirian the Unscarred and the qiraji generals hold there, and only their fall releases it."
L[21215]="{K|5}\nIt is found inside a Smokywood Pastures Sampler, and nowhere else in particular."
L[21217]="{K|5}\nIt is made, not found. {T|185} This one is worked from Raw Greater Sagefish and Hot Spices. A cook of middling skill (around 175) can attempt it."
L[21218]="A mount, the pride of its rider, bred by the stables of its people or won from the great foes. {C|21}\nIt comes out of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The rank and file of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj have it about them."
L[21219]={A="A recipe of the cooking trade, which teaches the making of Sagefish Delight. {T|185} It asks a skill of about 175 of a cook who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|cooking suppliers} Travellers of the Alliance will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins.",H="A recipe of the cooking trade, which teaches the making of Sagefish Delight. {T|185} It asks a skill of about 175 of a cook who attempts it.\nIt is bought, not hunted. {V|cooking suppliers} Travellers of the Horde will find it on the shelves of most towns and outposts, and in the neutral markets of the goblins."}
L[21220]="A thing wanted not for its own sake but because someone, somewhere, has asked for it.\nIt comes out of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by Ossirian the Unscarred and the qiraji generals, and this is one of them."
L[21221]="A token, proof or ingredient of somebody's errand, worth nothing to anyone else.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The great prizes of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are kept by the Twin Emperors and C'Thun itself, and this is one of them."
L[21222]="A trifle carried for no good reason by whoever it was taken from, and sold at the first shop.\nIt comes out of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj} {P|insects} Within, it is the insects who carry it."
L[21223]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it.\nIt comes out of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} Within, it is carried by the common run of the place's defenders."
L[21224]="Junk, in a word: the sort of thing that fills the pockets of the dead and the sacks of adventurers.\nIts source is the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Ahn'Qiraj} The rank and file of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj have it about them."
L[21225]="A curio of no use beyond the coin a merchant will give for it. {C|21}\nIt comes out of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj. {D|Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj} {P|insects} It is the insects of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj who have it about them."
