L[22520]="A curio of the adventuring trade. {C|24}\nIts source is Naxxramas, and nowhere in the open world. {D|Naxxramas} The great prizes of Naxxramas are kept by Kel'Thuzad and the Four Horsemen, and this is one of them."
L[22523]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} It is given in thanks by those in the Eastern Plaguelands whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[22524]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is a reward for service rendered in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} It is given in thanks by those in the Eastern Plaguelands whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[22525]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} Nearly every one of the restless dead carries one."
L[22526]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the Western Plaguelands. {Z|Western Plaguelands} It is the south of the Western Plaguelands that rewards the search. The other place to look is the Eastern Plaguelands. {P|skeletons} It is found on almost all of the skeletons."
L[22527]="A curio of the adventuring trade. {C|45}\nIts home, so far as it has one, is the sands of Silithus. {Z|Silithus} Look to the north-west of the sands of Silithus. It is found as readily in the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {P|earth elementals} Nearly every one of the earth elementals and fire elementals carries one."
L[22528]="A curio of the adventuring trade. {C|5}\nHunters find it most readily in Blackrock Depths. {D|Blackrock Depths} The other place to look is the ash plains of the Burning Steppes. Perhaps one in four of the raiders and tribesmen there has one about them."
L[22529]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nHunters find it most readily in the jungle crater of Un'Goro. {Z|Un'Goro Crater} {P|carnivorous plants} It is found on almost all of the carnivorous plants."
L[22568]="A curio of the adventuring trade.\nIt is earned, not found: a reward for service in the Eastern Plaguelands. {Z|Eastern Plaguelands} It is given in thanks by those in the Eastern Plaguelands whose troubles an adventurer takes on."
L[22589]="Atiesh is the staff of the Guardians of Tirisfal, carried by Medivh, the last Guardian, through whom Sargeras opened the Dark Portal. After Medivh's death the staff was shattered and its pieces scattered into Naxxramas by the Scourge, who could not destroy it.\nWhoever gathers the forty splinters from the necropolis, recovers the base and the head from its masters, and cleanses the staff of the shade that haunts it in Stratholme may take it to Karazhan, where Medivh's servant will restore it."
